- raw HTML omitted -->⚙️ Internals</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>chore: bump runner version to 4.19.1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github-actions\"><code>@​github-actions</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/pull/225\">CodSpeedHQ/action#225</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->💼 Other</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump the memtrack pin to 1.3.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriencaccia\"><code>@​adriencaccia</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/runner/pull/474\">#474</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Install codspeed-runner 4.19.1</h2>\n<h3>Install prebuilt binaries via shell script</h3>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf\nhttps://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-installer.sh\n| sh\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Download codspeed-runner 4.19.1</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Platform</th>\n<th>Checksum</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz\">codspeed-runner-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>Apple Silicon macOS</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz\">codspeed-runner-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>ARM64 MUSL Linux</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz\">codspeed-runner-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>x64 MUSL Linux</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/releases/download/v4.19.1/codspeed-runner-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Full Runner Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/codspeed/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</a></p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/compare/v4.19.0...v4.19.1\">https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/compare/v4.19.0...v4.19.1</a></p>\n<h2>v4.19.0</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>This release adds a new\n<code>--experimental-exclude-allocations</code> feature to remove\nallocator time from Simulation benchmarks.</p>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->🚀 Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove eager allocator discovery by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a></li>\n<li>Attach allocator probes on demand via exec-mapping watcher by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a></li>\n<li>Add exec-mapping watcher BPF prog and inode maps by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a></li>\n<li>Add experimental --exclude-allocations setting by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/f22792bfac16f3e14eb9fbea76f4a48e9cc22b93\"><code>f22792b</code></a>\nRelease v4.19.1 🚀</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/b07ddfbc843d6aab7f2bdbac308754716e676636\"><code>b07ddfb</code></a>\nchore: bump runner version to 4.19.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/9c498abf90f466ace8338cd5505d6ab277e1f9a3\"><code>9c498ab</code></a>\nRelease v4.19.0 🚀</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/a65d9f01a0251f66f48d60d9e22ae088d83ce4b2\"><code>a65d9f0</code></a>\nchore: bump runner version to 4.19.0</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/codspeedhq/action/compare/f99becdce5e5d51fd556489ebef684f4ecfd6286...f22792bfac16f3e14eb9fbea76f4a48e9cc22b93\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish` from 1.14.0 to 1.14.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/releases\">pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.14.1</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>🛠️ Internal Dependencies</h2>\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adisivaprasad\"><code>@​adisivaprasad</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/adisivaprasad\">💰</a> helped get rid of\nthe GitHub Actions runner warning about the old Node 20 runtime being\nused by updating <code>actions/setup-python</code> from v5.6.0 to v6.2.0\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/408\">#408</a>.</p>\n<h2>💪 New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adisivaprasad\"><code>@​adisivaprasad</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/408\">#408</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/jylenhof\"><code>@​jylenhof</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/jylenhof\">💰</a> followed up and\nreminded us to actually cut this release in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/413\">#413</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>🪞 Full Diff</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/v1.14.0...v1.14.1\">https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/v1.14.0...v1.14.1</a></p>\n<p><strong>🧔‍♂️ Release Manager:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/webknjaz\"><code>@​webknjaz</code></a>\n<a href=\"https://stand-with-ukraine.pp.ua\">🇺🇦</a></p>\n<p><strong>🙏 Special Thanks</strong> to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jylenhof\"><code>@​jylenhof</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/jylenhof\">💰</a> for reminding me to\nwork on this release!</p>\n<p><strong>💬 Discuss</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:ve6s3mxkefjaxty3m4fdqumn/post/3mrd7jpnxc22d\">on\nBluesky 🦋</a>, <a\nhref=\"https://mastodon.social/@webknjaz/116970132515797444\">on Mastodon\n🐘</a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/discussions/414\">on\nGitHub</a>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/sponsors/webknjaz\"><img\nsrc=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/%40webknjaz-transparent?logo=githubsponsors&amp;logoColor=%23EA4AAA&amp;label=Sponsor&amp;color=2a313c\"\nalt=\"GH Sponsors badge\" /></a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/ba38be9e461d3875417946c167d0b5f3d385a247\"><code>ba38be9</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/408\">#408</a>\nfrom adisivaprasad/bump-setup-python-v6</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/a6c5088d60d08ef54b70075735d25df696e5ccaa\"><code>a6c5088</code></a>\nBump actions/setup-python from v5.6.0 to v6.2.0</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/cef221092ed1bacb1cc03d23a2d87d1d172e277b...ba38be9e461d3875417946c167d0b5f3d385a247\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T18:50:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/05ef1c28f81a961ec729296646d3646d82084711","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/05ef1c28f81a961ec729296646d3646d82084711","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/05ef1c28f81a961ec729296646d3646d82084711/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d"}]},{"sha":"b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI2NGRiOTdlNTQ1NTJiOTY2ODQ4NGFiY2Q0N2EzNjJmYzY1OGRjOWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T18:48:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T18:48:11Z"},"message":"style(code): color tool-call rows by output status (#5039)\n\nTool-call rows in `deepagents-code` now tint themselves by their\nterminal outcome — green for success, red for error, and amber for\nrejected/skipped — so you can tell how a call finished at a glance\ninstead of reading the small inline status line.\n\n---\n\n`ToolCallMessage` previously carried a fixed left accent (`$tool`)\nregardless of outcome; only the tiny inline status line changed color.\nThis encodes the outcome on the row widget itself via a `-status-*` CSS\nclass (set in `set_success`/`set_error`/`set_rejected`/`set_skipped` and\nrestored on hydration in `_restore_deferred_state`), and styles the\nrow's left border plus a faint background tint per status using the\nexisting `$success`/`$error`/`$warning` theme tokens.\n\nThe tint is kept low-alpha so text stays readable across light/dark/ansi\nthemes, matching the existing design language (the row already used a\ncolored left border for lifecycle). Running/pending states keep the\ndefault `$tool` accent, and the `:hover` brighten behavior is preserved.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d10af15-0565-9b8b-512a-ffd3e4b0790d)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d10af15-0565-9b8b-512a-ffd3e4b0790d/plan\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"75b266f1a3c4b1daf55cb7c621431523b7c00ab5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/75b266f1a3c4b1daf55cb7c621431523b7c00ab5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ6frCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3z8QACndw+/+2JhyWbBDkY2tEYOf\nTebvjuCHCFokgH/EfKMTo7ikPrGDiU973wgOuPw8SYbL4NVyyNcmFb5TimhpXIzz\noPiQXHWma4770Xu+yzFxDJS8TJQx4A4eRVAnNZoV2S2Suj+iKqyyTQ+FATHgQhg0\nO3cOw9UxaQ0d4T1ugXrkTiuCjMBfKzsIkORIQUpAue/KuZh2KASOkadQK2fcZYKl\nK037cUKo2/JwaBtIdPL5r0u92Nt9eNe2t6Cwc6OjGuTP7OT7OKAcqzaPxRnNzt79\nFGW8Bvrdl6fF3TiR2m52sRmt7avJtNA7Yn6XJYEf76qY7Qi8pFWnZWKQ6dnYmmiz\nVpgQpzmZlGAPvDKsFRbavXpfD6pCnD/+tnFBhB9kIHO+2B9LSGMMYjXVu68DCMPI\nawUo5t3WpOiwJgtX8gclBOarHWWhIlZE41QWTv5/ewYIMyhFU5xXn4/xVEhL/UUx\nKhenF1gpDeY+7A/aoBDC4syAFd+faS88E53PoV1H2dOoob5Ixb/Hn3FKZjbru8uB\nlRh9+RhmonuvW4oLk3sTS2PwNJo4SlTZQpmq7CblEcoRxVByTXoiE6mkIU9V0iOq\nsW2Z83oIMX10EoLmUzHWnP5WgbylbJ/YZ9N4vvPohFro3i2UVVYvDldG8sCgulYN\nf3UA09w1mLN2MXL6tY1B\n=cfGO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 75b266f1a3c4b1daf55cb7c621431523b7c00ab5\nparent 0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785178091 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785178091 -0400\n\nstyle(code): color tool-call rows by output status (#5039)\n\nTool-call rows in `deepagents-code` now tint themselves by their\nterminal outcome — green for success, red for error, and amber for\nrejected/skipped — so you can tell how a call finished at a glance\ninstead of reading the small inline status line.\n\n---\n\n`ToolCallMessage` previously carried a fixed left accent (`$tool`)\nregardless of outcome; only the tiny inline status line changed color.\nThis encodes the outcome on the row widget itself via a `-status-*` CSS\nclass (set in `set_success`/`set_error`/`set_rejected`/`set_skipped` and\nrestored on hydration in `_restore_deferred_state`), and styles the\nrow's left border plus a faint background tint per status using the\nexisting `$success`/`$error`/`$warning` theme tokens.\n\nThe tint is kept low-alpha so text stays readable across light/dark/ansi\nthemes, matching the existing design language (the row already used a\ncolored left border for lifecycle). Running/pending states keep the\ndefault `$tool` accent, and the `:hover` brighten behavior is preserved.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d10af15-0565-9b8b-512a-ffd3e4b0790d)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d10af15-0565-9b8b-512a-ffd3e4b0790d/plan\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T18:48:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b64db97e54552b9668484abcd47a362fc658dc9d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99"}]},{"sha":"0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBkMDg3NDcxMDYxNWRmMmM4OWMzYzMwZTU2YmZkYWJiNzNiNDRkOTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ramon Nogueira","email":"ramon.nogueira@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T18:40:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T18:40:12Z"},"message":"perf(langsmith-sandbox): run LangSmith sandbox commands over the async client (#5061)\n\n`LangSmithSandbox` never overrode `aexecute`, so async commands fell\nthrough to `SandboxBackendProtocol.aexecute`, which offloads the\nblocking SDK client to a worker thread. This implements it against the\nSDK's async client instead.\n\n---\n\n`BaseSandbox` routes `als`/`aread`/`awrite`/`aedit`/`agrep`/`aglob`\nthrough `aexecute`, so this covers every async filesystem operation, not\njust `execute`.\n\n`Sandbox.to_async()` builds a fresh client with its own connection pool\non every call, so it is cached per event loop — otherwise every file\nread, write, glob, and grep would pay a TCP and TLS handshake.\nConstruction stays lazy, so a purely synchronous caller never builds\none, and `aclose()` releases the pool.\n\nIt is also much faster, for an unsatisfying reason: the sync client\nblocks the caller on the WebSocket teardown, which sits behind a 1s\n`delayed_close_timeout` on the gateway fronting the sandbox. Same\ncommand, same box: **1274ms → 188ms**. The async client returns as soon\nas the command's `exit` frame arrives and lets the teardown finish on\nits own. Both paths use `_run_ws`, so this is not a WebSocket-to-HTTP\ndowngrade — same protocol, same frames.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make test\nTEST_FILE=tests/unit_tests/backends/test_langsmith_sandbox.py` — 45\npass, including new cases for the async path, stdout/stderr combining,\nsingle-client reuse, `aclose` + rebuild, and the no-op close when async\nwas never used\n- [x] `make lint` clean (ruff, format, `ty`)\n- [x] Verified end to end against a real sandbox\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"19364c36e5fd8bf499145252b7a4d12e4d928203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/19364c36e5fd8bf499145252b7a4d12e4d928203"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ6YMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3JsQAJgUBf7PjVv5zAFkzJoacen1\nC/duQmnJQvgPNdTLshFLRb2SDdtlovN5g/geA70+MfX1IL5ajsoOutbbmSj8/5pX\n6kqwadwN3iiPPMXq8PxgZyfYg9XtsiHif3eHqXGFxFxipy6nO7kPtZfvkeaYqcjN\n7+z5pMuoPGMVBbfmWBHs3uHxcss/VeFLp6T7ILPlOXkfFsGB7/HrSqyZ0Fza+5Vq\nWOFmJ1QU/4qcnkqIwSneIGv6P/aHqt3Ralnpfxf//WjNz4yBSEkoNscPHQ6SPcLn\nHUXzHaky03Jb3uCyZUVnDzeKuitVgOMNXgLzdCfeJV0d1o6LnagcsnhvK5kiKXFf\npU31cuwsdYz+XWLIoP8qkw7RtNPl6E4VcrGSVd2zyFNMB7GYV4ieJzE4/AT29CJw\nFdPN5S/hUGfqcmKafRkgOk4Dg+tJHUdMfiMsou7ulbT7C0i8U+FBAyK2/Mw8X0hk\n0BP9ODDQfjIWijzGo/2QaDz1l/t69X2Fkw9OhfjonUJwO0yVmfS9wm62TtT2sl3X\nBsOq+8A1+SX0mVpR9nKUMlUy2ITnVwUNeBnf+meWDIzP8tLcPW+PSdytSyyd4WjZ\nf3phEh86jhgD4SapqV7umpYyaCiWgJrewo2Ycvw3RIAqLIV+9waKqUGNrx8GS/c3\nHbkiCVXGtXek6lW7DSTD\n=ufPJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 19364c36e5fd8bf499145252b7a4d12e4d928203\nparent 4bf40e8d372bbd8cb25b3dca3b188d8de577a0ac\nauthor Ramon Nogueira <ramon.nogueira@langchain.dev> 1785177612 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785177612 -0400\n\nperf(langsmith-sandbox): run LangSmith sandbox commands over the async client (#5061)\n\n`LangSmithSandbox` never overrode `aexecute`, so async commands fell\nthrough to `SandboxBackendProtocol.aexecute`, which offloads the\nblocking SDK client to a worker thread. This implements it against the\nSDK's async client instead.\n\n---\n\n`BaseSandbox` routes `als`/`aread`/`awrite`/`aedit`/`agrep`/`aglob`\nthrough `aexecute`, so this covers every async filesystem operation, not\njust `execute`.\n\n`Sandbox.to_async()` builds a fresh client with its own connection pool\non every call, so it is cached per event loop — otherwise every file\nread, write, glob, and grep would pay a TCP and TLS handshake.\nConstruction stays lazy, so a purely synchronous caller never builds\none, and `aclose()` releases the pool.\n\nIt is also much faster, for an unsatisfying reason: the sync client\nblocks the caller on the WebSocket teardown, which sits behind a 1s\n`delayed_close_timeout` on the gateway fronting the sandbox. Same\ncommand, same box: **1274ms → 188ms**. The async client returns as soon\nas the command's `exit` frame arrives and lets the teardown finish on\nits own. Both paths use `_run_ws`, so this is not a WebSocket-to-HTTP\ndowngrade — same protocol, same frames.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make test\nTEST_FILE=tests/unit_tests/backends/test_langsmith_sandbox.py` — 45\npass, including new cases for the async path, stdout/stderr combining,\nsingle-client reuse, `aclose` + rebuild, and the no-op close when async\nwas never used\n- [x] `make lint` clean (ruff, format, `ty`)\n- [x] Verified end to end against a real sandbox\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T18:40:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d0874710615df2c89c3c30e56bfdabb73b44d99/comments","author":{"login":"ramon-langchain","id":270434257,"node_id":"U_kgDOEB5_0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270434257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain","html_url":"https://github.com/ramon-langchain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramon-langchain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4bf40e8d372bbd8cb25b3dca3b188d8de577a0ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4bf40e8d372bbd8cb25b3dca3b188d8de577a0ac","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4bf40e8d372bbd8cb25b3dca3b188d8de577a0ac"}]},{"sha":"4bf40e8d372bbd8cb25b3dca3b188d8de577a0ac","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRiZjQwZThkMzcyYmJkOGNiMjViM2RjYTNiMTg4ZDhkZTU3N2EwYWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-27T18:39:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T18:39:52Z"},"message":"fix(ci): preserve dependency bounds in Dependabot uv updates (#5070)\n\n- Configure the maintained multi-directory `uv` Dependabot entry to\nincrease compatible manifest bounds while updating lockfiles.\n- Ignore coordinated same-repository Deep Agents and partner packages so\nDependabot does not separate their release updates.\n- Keep the existing dependency roots, monthly schedule, and update\ngroups unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: langsmith-fleet[bot] <langsmith-fleet[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3696856309d3deb6e2a838b41034197033d190c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f3696856309d3deb6e2a838b41034197033d190c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4bf40e8d372bbd8cb25b3dca3b188d8de577a0ac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":tr