19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213"}]},{"sha":"dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRjYmZmOWM0ZDA0NmJjZDM4Y2VlZjhlMzYyNjkxZTgwMzAwMzYyMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ccurme","email":"chester.curme@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-27T18:13:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T18:13:17Z"},"message":"feat(code): recognize LangSmith Gateway credentials (#5042)\n\nDepends on langchain-ai/langchain#38742\n\nIf you only set LangSmith LLM Gateway credentials and skip\nprovider-native keys like `OPENAI_API_KEY`, Deep Agents Code used to\nfail model credential preflight and block those models.\nGateway-authenticated Anthropic, Baseten, Fireworks, Google GenAI, and\nOpenAI models now pass preflight when the gateway is actually enabled.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, credential checks looked only for each provider's own API\nkey or stored secret. A user with:\n\n```bash\nLANGSMITH_GATEWAY=true\nLANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...\n```\n\nand no `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` would still get a\nmissing-credentials failure on model select or startup, even though the\nchat client would authenticate through the gateway.\n\nAfter this change, those checks also accept LangSmith Gateway for the\nbuilt-in providers whose LangChain integrations read the gateway env\nvars: Anthropic, Baseten, Fireworks, Google GenAI, and OpenAI.\n\nThe gateway path only counts when:\n\n- `LANGSMITH_GATEWAY` is set and not a disable value (`false`, `0`,\n`no`)\n- `LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY` is non-empty\n- the provider is one of the supported built-in integrations above\n\nUnsupported providers still require their own credentials. Custom\nprovider overrides with a `class_path` also keep using their own\n`api_key_env` check, because an arbitrary custom class is not assumed to\nconsume the gateway variables.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"881e2b46fb50ad96d2cfbd8be746c27a419705a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/881e2b46fb50ad96d2cfbd8be746c27a419705a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ5+9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbPgQADzjr9VlTwoITz+FgaS+xkb1\nbV519HQOUVnyGaHckgVPA1QXY5U0/r6ddU3PBufWa2FpWV+MZfgXMte0dBirsfi6\nBD1oKCXmTQJppUPuoq/I7hG+NIFmotKQEKIz1o4JXvQrFm8wB3SceYTnkZ5EE4xF\naNceN//TgtCQoI8qUX44kbjMpRZWJ+mSi+t+zfvdFAseS/n7xJUKHzjoL2MXcntV\nN9dAcWOKiqDiQ/tMfmsP2kwIDqoBu55KUGlajm+gLsenzOV3//RrzV9c/dpJNTQZ\na+4HAJl5NOk9GextCaE7r1N8zjIC5iRDGFYaFmOTyB+m979K+Y4+/mQid59m081N\ndwlNxKdFtF90ip8Q/XFqyC9fHl3qIT6DxfqCZNrMrjRVE8BKtepheenskjBqexz+\n14efVxLfE/yDdSsZ5Bemm3qN7C8glj0h8HWZiroVV7ENt31oHo+5yi1LUxbm9LPe\ncH2pHl6a+j1eU0vqdRJe3DxWImiG0IgOcKJrOGaLOGV6j/0yq3QSO7LJOe0YB+Yp\nobdrHE4tiUZ3BAY5DwtBkUOuaVJa/JF0LPPwj75PuuvggtZLxpHDCNd2nMhGK5cD\n/02LtPujB1kPxgq/oKg7mE5sCESOwjGYWPQ7XmpXTTZAe63QMoLC2ta4a6ohq6SH\nUzYlOfmTj17JSHO9SsKD\n=S4kK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 881e2b46fb50ad96d2cfbd8be746c27a419705a2\nparent 0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4\nauthor ccurme <chester.curme@gmail.com> 1785175997 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785175997 -0400\n\nfeat(code): recognize LangSmith Gateway credentials (#5042)\n\nDepends on langchain-ai/langchain#38742\n\nIf you only set LangSmith LLM Gateway credentials and skip\nprovider-native keys like `OPENAI_API_KEY`, Deep Agents Code used to\nfail model credential preflight and block those models.\nGateway-authenticated Anthropic, Baseten, Fireworks, Google GenAI, and\nOpenAI models now pass preflight when the gateway is actually enabled.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, credential checks looked only for each provider's own API\nkey or stored secret. A user with:\n\n```bash\nLANGSMITH_GATEWAY=true\nLANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...\n```\n\nand no `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` would still get a\nmissing-credentials failure on model select or startup, even though the\nchat client would authenticate through the gateway.\n\nAfter this change, those checks also accept LangSmith Gateway for the\nbuilt-in providers whose LangChain integrations read the gateway env\nvars: Anthropic, Baseten, Fireworks, Google GenAI, and OpenAI.\n\nThe gateway path only counts when:\n\n- `LANGSMITH_GATEWAY` is set and not a disable value (`false`, `0`,\n`no`)\n- `LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY` is non-empty\n- the provider is one of the supported built-in integrations above\n\nUnsupported providers still require their own credentials. Custom\nprovider overrides with a `class_path` also keep using their own\n`api_key_env` check, because an arbitrary custom class is not assumed to\nconsume the gateway variables.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T18:13:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dcbff9c4d046bcd38ceef8e362691e8030036213/comments","author":{"login":"ccurme","id":26529506,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTI5NTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26529506?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme","html_url":"https://github.com/ccurme","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4"}]},{"sha":"0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA2NTFjOTk2NTU2ZWUwNzAzZjc3NmNiZTI0NjFlZTQxODkzYTBmYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T17:55:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T17:55:40Z"},"message":"chore(code): raise dependency minimums (#5090)\n\nRaise minimum versions for Deep Agents Code dependencies that have newer\nstable releases inside their existing upper bounds, and refresh the\nlockfile.\n\n---\n\nScanned every direct dependency in `libs/code` against PyPI stable\nreleases and raised mins only where a newer stable version still\nsatisfies the current upper bound:\n\n- `langchain-google-genai` `>=4.3.1` → `>=4.3.2`\n- `prompt-toolkit` `>=3.0.52` → `>=3.0.53`\n- `langchain-quickjs` `>=0.3.3` → `>=0.3.4`\n- `langchain-baseten` `>=0.2.1` → `>=0.2.3`\n- `langchain-fireworks` `>=1.5.1` → `>=1.5.2`\n\nEverything else was already at the latest stable lower bound.\n\nLeft intentionally alone:\n- `deepagents==0.7.0b2` exact pin\n- `pydantic>=2.12.5` — `fireworks-ai` still requires `pydantic<2.13`, so\n`>=2.13` breaks the `all-providers` extra\n- intentional caps (`filelock<3.30`, `ty<0.0.62`, `twine<7`)\n\nLockfile updated with targeted `--upgrade-package` only (no global\nprerelease allow).","tree":{"sha":"a2227c03d7cfa53c60cf3ed7b11677c9303ba1a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a2227c03d7cfa53c60cf3ed7b11677c9303ba1a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ5ucCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd+IQAAwwCeNUp6xxE7FH/xzXsDLs\nG9Y6N3PexDVTqJD/K4tJlVSF9oWy7l0ELKoztlfZBIX9DpN8lL4QS7gx3fHnmXNg\nMIhHYU+X+1icQoz4mXFgFQiDCoLOLjnvfM087k6nwvHFBZnXUyVG1U0QMe4ZoL+O\nfb7M0D5KnKxRLGtjAy3BTkVa2gIdaNq8Y+MpOgYoCwzVCrZnKvZj8YDr3TfmreWv\nT/sslJI+x6Pd3wetJlzPxoKZ1lJYutsyZ2QyPwqKnLXcjm01eR2+vUHZb0T6DwBq\nmCIstMVv8wGKzmK90AcZUEFEQ45Thu9hgu1lqX6ss4tSIGAkQ32e7GJQBeysEpLA\nZZ42yXxBiOZ5sI2pF6/IHw3lnXfS4Oc4MywxSdM6QKzqmJEfmfdAhs5phOrK6rag\nV7bLx92f4LD3qI/l5I7OGC31WZxEKwKEEZcUJWNPv+F5qSce/YnRkjh6Og3DYaQl\nvK5FTxXvxZI8vdDUvBxatoeUKdEOYJll7lIyFkKd62KBTgFV+IAz4tTvEqJe/GZR\n0MRbL0EyVzSRkPrHFxtJKJPoOrvcddVBrylAX8OH+Cu1nzlkIF9TLvOEYZGO4Y0k\nOhD8hcm0bYEelsKAXJrJBTAnY7PF2QGV2KmfSZ+TTXViPmhqofZLFY2e6cs3dAso\nAKmsKRYGxgP8XgcecsaB\n=9Wyn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a2227c03d7cfa53c60cf3ed7b11677c9303ba1a6\nparent 75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785174940 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785174940 -0400\n\nchore(code): raise dependency minimums (#5090)\n\nRaise minimum versions for Deep Agents Code dependencies that have newer\nstable releases inside their existing upper bounds, and refresh the\nlockfile.\n\n---\n\nScanned every direct dependency in `libs/code` against PyPI stable\nreleases and raised mins only where a newer stable version still\nsatisfies the current upper bound:\n\n- `langchain-google-genai` `>=4.3.1` → `>=4.3.2`\n- `prompt-toolkit` `>=3.0.52` → `>=3.0.53`\n- `langchain-quickjs` `>=0.3.3` → `>=0.3.4`\n- `langchain-baseten` `>=0.2.1` → `>=0.2.3`\n- `langchain-fireworks` `>=1.5.1` → `>=1.5.2`\n\nEverything else was already at the latest stable lower bound.\n\nLeft intentionally alone:\n- `deepagents==0.7.0b2` exact pin\n- `pydantic>=2.12.5` — `fireworks-ai` still requires `pydantic<2.13`, so\n`>=2.13` breaks the `all-providers` extra\n- intentional caps (`filelock<3.30`, `ty<0.0.62`, `twine<7`)\n\nLockfile updated with targeted `--upgrade-package` only (no global\nprerelease allow).","verified_at":"2026-07-27T17:55:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0651c996556ee0703f776cbe2461ee41893a0fa4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e"}]},{"sha":"75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc1MTk3NTI3ZjdkNDcyZjAwYzBhY2Q3YTEwNjYyYTliMjA1MjJmM2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T17:31:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T17:31:41Z"},"message":"style(code): clarify Auto classifier timeout messaging (#5088)\n\nWhen Auto times out waiting on its classifier, the transcript now says\nthe classifier did not respond within the limit and that the tool was\nnot executed, instead of the vaguer \"no decision\" / \"action blocked\"\nwording.\n\n---\n\nOnly the local Auto deadline path gets the specific \"did not respond\"\nreason. Other classifier failures stay type-only (`failed\n(TimeoutError)`), so we still do not imply dcode's budget fired when the\nprovider failed first.","tree":{"sha":"69576f4ba23ce3ed7058b657bf3d043137d487a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/69576f4ba23ce3ed7058b657bf3d043137d487a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ5X9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiZAQABweEnLp4CWu8OnLVIRFSYzZ\nA1iBtEGCxncVNkOHA1bANNoBAs2oaKLjKif3yoWb+jOQ0HFPl29il0bjwAt9Jzbk\nmP/N+NHPmZ8UlVB4n4H+2jZUULzRSgqpauDUJcNKvfR3TumN4Dr0pMBrRKz/lm0a\n1vz+LBKKohrQGYtAkHGRKgJ+7WL7tH9rCb/1oBdcj1ex/z8lr7pIkrxEyIXVD0MY\nnCBdtjCzNrrNmZGpZXD8JWN6pbqROuJ5DE1wDLhjW/ryJw2UGgiFb2AI6Rde0S70\ni8BkHwirpWm3QpR6fHfmae9i63vgOqIZmmV3JNLA1P0NMlaS6M48iIhc6u9E3qq6\n8k0VciyEtz13wuErEc+g099dSaCxlaUL6BYEzHjm3LFoJnBsVLkbxJ2kx2gYmyf1\n7IwIHbCI0kJMYb0vUUgOEn/9kBEHyuNdEPTJqZeg64pEaubQ7jKww7H4QCxqfjM8\nySsOcD4m4fY6S+HjIQppIJQtGHnahIYAsESTnB/EehzS14PeKWaBm2L2g/OvTFCp\n2hqyFN0rHCDc7qcHnttOMUIFGoPmcH+zY/Zs5cImOk22dDM+vdka2ZLUFz4weE0X\nEegOS04oqdhFDbVXuDXxTW7Lbsj3b025fH4k8d+bmMpm2Lrls7szY/Nm6vY2u5V9\nInvJmQ89ERwpTjFJIVnt\n=C5Ia\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 69576f4ba23ce3ed7058b657bf3d043137d487a1\nparent 2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785173501 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785173501 -0400\n\nstyle(code): clarify Auto classifier timeout messaging (#5088)\n\nWhen Auto times out waiting on its classifier, the transcript now says\nthe classifier did not respond within the limit and that the tool was\nnot executed, instead of the vaguer \"no decision\" / \"action blocked\"\nwording.\n\n---\n\nOnly the local Auto deadline path gets the specific \"did not respond\"\nreason. Other classifier failures stay type-only (`failed\n(TimeoutError)`), so we still do not imply dcode's budget fired when the\nprovider failed first.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T17:31:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/75197527f7d472f00c0acd7a10662a9b20522f3e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726"}]},{"sha":"2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJiNjljMzBhYmM0YzRiY2VjNWU4NmE0MTE1MWJlMDUxOGU5MDM3MjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T17:01:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T17:01:51Z"},"message":"style(code): render collapsed expand hints as dim italic (#5087)\n\nCollapsed \"click or Ctrl+O to expand\" hints in the `deepagents-code`\ntranscript now render as dim italic, matching the collapse,\ncommand/code-block, task-description, and user-message hints.\n\n---\n\nIn the `messages` TUI module every \"click or Ctrl+O\" affordance is meant\nto be dim italic (see `_hint_style()` and the `UserMessage` CSS\ncomment), but four collapsed-state expand hints — the tool-output\n\"expand\" hint (count-free and truncated variants) and the skill-body \"N\nmore lines\" hint — were styled plain `dim`, dropping the italic. That\nleft a grep/output expand hint visually inconsistent with the italic\ncommand hint shown right next to it. This makes all four dim italic and\nadds a unit test asserting the expand and collapse hints share the dim\nitalic style.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6f3a21a4-0606-98ac-3b69-d334582bde7b)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a2ef97204196b4b3f02ac9e8ec0fe119cd8ecdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3a2ef97204196b4b3f02ac9e8ec0fe119cd8ecdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ47/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6RgQAKtD5gjOqUYcgmR2Thg5ZZA6\nqu1RZZI4IcVKUMJBUVe2PVLA1jstJZahvfF4A+E5V+1FKOyYzidnsnoN8mhvpcMn\nqTpgyS+yFfsQsokJC5545Tqf2XkwMVM1elC39yJ8J1kzLyQxWP9YHk7IY7zJieuY\nn7XSrNRRvWm2bOq3BO087U4hiDa68XA3Lz2GzornHVb1QgdQ+/gOXB/oP4JbXKkM\nFp02jSxMskZFHD4kjZaskIZF6KsB1DFduWoOkjxg+Hc2FzRIUEw8UIfsMNiHrFz9\n+mhRbdsWCTLYPfxOXS23kU3JiVqID1v+76gzMqAB9eDJ8oBlEMgNy7sKdibrnbXf\n7h+ADOMdferkEC+UVU6v3WzVfbnPI1MdFOyNrWT07kTik12ZdBIU6e9BdwwqpzxF\nEf4PLX7iZzXqMjQZec5nYj5HLIurW9+7OyO9nKVv3v+mdIkV3dd4dc4d7HhdWCFF\nyKef8NaC2kk7XI3R/VNHFgP9UwtNV6Ygh8u8VnaHcQR4qb/p0S6eaWs8gjvl37WZ\nQcanNoYjUTEB+aMM5/vhQjIJ+cpSFfv6TMGmQjVh4pkz9FgjDv4G5MPUK5WFHf/A\nPegY5SIgGoezO6tVYarLUU+T07pWjmg9ZsRTt7BTDBAYTmGgPYg6ktVwInEj3UKp\nQKD32hRxgeG1PKbolZkj\n=CHg2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3a2ef97204196b4b3f02ac9e8ec0fe119cd8ecdb\nparent c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785171711 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785171711 -0400\n\nstyle(code): render collapsed expand hints as dim italic (#5087)\n\nCollapsed \"click or Ctrl+O to expand\" hints in the `deepagents-code`\ntranscript now render as dim italic, matching the collapse,\ncommand/code-block, task-description, and user-message hints.\n\n---\n\nIn the `messages` TUI module every \"click or Ctrl+O\" affordance is meant\nto be dim italic (see `_hint_style()` and the `UserMessage` CSS\ncomment), but four collapsed-state expand hints — the tool-output\n\"expand\" hint (count-free and truncated variants) and the skill-body \"N\nmore lines\" hint — were styled plain `dim`, dropping the italic. That\nleft a grep/output expand hint visually inconsistent with the italic\ncommand hint shown right next to it. This makes all four dim italic and\nadds a unit test asserting the expand and collapse hints share the dim\nitalic style.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6f3a21a4-0606-98ac-3b69-d334582bde7b)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T17:01:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b69c30abc4c4bcec5e86a41151be0518e903726/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf"}]},{"sha":"c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM0ZTI0ODA0ZWJkZTkzNTYzZjA1OTYxMDJiZDVkOWZjMTYzZWMwYmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T17:00:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T17:00:51Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep post-install restart modal responsive (#5086)\n\nFix the post-install \"Restart the server?\" modal being unresponsive to\nEnter/Esc after `/install`.\n\n---\n\n`/install <extra>` (e.g. `/install fireworks`) runs on the App message\npump via `on_chat_input_submitted`, and it `await`ed the restart offer\ninline. That blocked the pump while the restart modal was open, so the\nmodal never received the Enter/Esc key events it needs to resolve and\nappeared frozen. This detaches the offer onto a background task\n(mirroring the post-`/auth` web-search restart offer,\n`_launch_web_search_restart_prompt`) so the command handler returns and\nthe pump can route keys to the modal. Applies to both the extra and\n`--package` install paths.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/40e5560a-5711-c1b4-8b80-ba32cda3b7e0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3bb12434ce589939786f9cfe4be1bc1bae418b91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3bb12434ce589939786f9cfe4be1bc1bae418b91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ47DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArZIQAHkaMdkT1PhmPTAvGmWT6hBF\nLgnd8Ckthb/4ANRVD1PYxeWU+WFaHJRYIuU001bStdlrX2YKgGaNHtYrVrDY/NCm\n8vd5zE99rLNG77vV75eZpcYTtX59fvri2EntLmsTi/faA15G8Vy4DaXCMnznScNW\nVzFx7MvNBeA/gElTRLLT4/+sxgUca7EeQ1nTzpL/wD4S0khNEzJ5VwOmk5imn+1W\naugjYL19Ui24wtUMETihMWhOTo4kb2igwDBpZngv2hzhO6jLPzO/Iw2LrpybQ0GR\nUMD9UI3S15GTNvQJydgezeWCJAHsndaSLEPkMDBFS7e2OEaiGQlWx7XtQJOzmg5y\n7++KLv6J+iavI75wOXezrTamQqsDN8QA7whDUlhVOYDdET1PpQwBqxGc92rgeDN8\nrT/6JYFrJpLl2Xrm7sbizKthBjXHja29r8ezPXMEw6A0+r8vSmGGOfhSVNtjNHS/\nOWU/nRcoth6yEADOk4d7wGOX2FYfArZw+NyMmd+rv5z1uB4TOeXtskfmm+cC0CaN\nGUg6qdK10eUZMvWxE3zMrBgLzFY7WQZvwfLAgjvS8rxALfbE4WwXnddJfNwPoo16\nXT4/JEdlmT4Xbq0L++S5tU4fwxmXeHJ4wbzIk8fiBlsOxxuuy7t/2FzxKtzIXniP\nq+n8pP5DWpBesXKqwG1u\n=9jek\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3bb12434ce589939786f9cfe4be1bc1bae418b91\nparent a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785171651 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785171651 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep post-install restart modal responsive (#5086)\n\nFix the post-install \"Restart the server?\" modal being unresponsive to\nEnter/Esc after `/install`.\n\n---\n\n`/install <extra>` (e.g. `/install fireworks`) runs on the App message\npump via `on_chat_input_submitted`, and it `await`ed the restart offer\ninline. That blocked the pump while the restart modal was open, so the\nmodal never received the Enter/Esc key events it needs to resolve and\nappeared frozen. This detaches the offer onto a background task\n(mirroring the post-`/auth` web-search restart offer,\n`_launch_web_search_restart_prompt`) so the command handler returns and\nthe pump can route keys to the modal. Applies to both the extra and\n`--package` install paths.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/40e5560a-5711-c1b4-8b80-ba32cda3b7e0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T17:00:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c4e24804ebde93563f0596102bd5d9fc163ec0bf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce"}]},{"sha":"a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEzNDcxM2IxMjIzODNkY2NhZDI1NzJjZDcyMTNmZDU2ZjQ2N2ZjY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:45:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:45:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): toast and expand long transcript user messages (#5073)\n\nWhen a submitted prompt is long enough to collapse in transcript\nhistory, dcode now toasts that the full text still went to the model and\nlets you click or press Ctrl+O to expand the message inline.\n\nPreviously, messages over 10,000 characters were silently reduced to a\nhead/tail preview with an `@ldots. +N lines @ldots.` marker. The model\nalready received the full text, and select-all still copied it, but the\ntranscript made it look like what you typed had been mangled with no way\nto restore the middle in place.\n\n---\n\nCollapsed rows keep the head/tail preview for scrollback performance and\nuse the same click/Ctrl+O expand pattern as skill and tool rows.\nExpansion is per-widget for the current view; queued placeholders stay\ncollapsed-only until they become real user messages.","tree":{"sha":"a578e30ab6b0bbc111d25fc0e25df981933def83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a578e30ab6b0bbc111d25fc0e25df981933def83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4svCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfRgQABCYgnSO87rrslmmK1U66B0g\nyxpZKGn6w/0nEWptZtvBCU7e3FKJ5imuwHZhrAkvozVy84znK4ElxVaVUuNgLsFB\nplU1jNg0blKBqre6YoW00yvwEIpCdP7Jn2Vi7nHL01sky8zLAt6wWvPT1YWIQj2E\nzDKqKtari1YxfzMKsgD2pPG1uTYcO8RBDEXSeCx4BRKaGrLcKU6/iPjMMR0SYIIL\nQb9DmYLEWf7IjWg033KW6ldOIpkINIbiaIogfZLOild65JCW02qRI++Buc9GfwjZ\nSQ7CS7weiWOpinGfkUgczLqo8RxYGnuEWxg4GHIwLuUwwY7S85d4x6yzPIiCKspv\nqOfkERKZfOoXhw8XMStcMUhTeZBma2d7qIYCBoSpSbyZWBWEnzZ+b2ZQziTFb8K+\nUaf0EencTiMjg5H7GtDuxFCO2DdnqcdyRaF5RTr0liPeGmqzFAkFjmrJqlFE62qx\n54n643uHs+Mk/3cLZshLxwnTaRpRXWXbXhHQaZ5XpIBvtYnpuaV4jXA+l1urH7a5\nsaTuzFixC0vBUQmizMAfd9VA1/V2hFvY/RB5Mo5Y+q6nWc94DSNUWAEEe4gLxjYG\nTijq/dJzuN1mC4bB4DtyYardnaMbVtxOQ9bC8uX6PRoi9qyIyiv9DpPOHEl2B9k5\nBU0IA3KPzMDcRiqqJSMz\n=MCo6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a578e30ab6b0bbc111d25fc0e25df981933def83\nparent ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785170735 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785170735 -0400\n\nfix(code): toast and expand long transcript user messages (#5073)\n\nWhen a submitted prompt is long enough to collapse in transcript\nhistory, dcode now toasts that the full text still went to the model and\nlets you click or press Ctrl+O to expand the message inline.\n\nPreviously, messages over 10,000 characters were silently reduced to a\nhead/tail preview with an `@ldots. +N lines @ldots.` marker. The model\nalready received the full text, and select-all still copied it, but the\ntranscript made it look like what you typed had been mangled with no way\nto restore the middle in place.\n\n---\n\nCollapsed rows keep the head/tail preview for scrollback performance and\nuse the same click/Ctrl+O expand pattern as skill and tool rows.\nExpansion is per-widget for the current view; queued placeholders stay\ncollapsed-only until they become real user messages.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:45:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a34713b122383dccad2572cd7213fd56f467fcce/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9"}]},{"sha":"ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFjOTE4ZjgzZGM2M2QwZTI0ZTZhNDhiNWI5M2NiZDIwM2ZkODk0Yjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:32:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:32:43Z"},"message":"ci(infra): emphasize required SDK pin acknowledgement (#5085)\n\nMake the prerelease SDK pin acknowledgement requirement stand out more\nclearly in the sticky PR comment by prefixing the required-label line\nwith 🚨.\n\n---\n\nWhen `check_sdk_pin` warns that a package pins a prerelease SDK,\nreviewers still need to add the bypass label before merge. The required\nstep was easy to miss in the existing notice copy.","tree":{"sha":"6210f40a1db39fd2385bf362e2aad8d7babc4956","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6210f40a1db39fd2385bf362e2aad8d7babc4956"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4grCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0UwQAGGeaf+iHaiqLz0jzYWS3NvL\npUGw/d4r0j16DGZIxL1/7IHtxt+DjqELIJ024IRxaquljqjM61j47tPZwDKYbH9Q\nOLecsrgqPSPrZiG/gmRL3SzrstV5wEp1ntH0SehAuKMvka5CpMws+q8Bb18XNv2+\nfsm2zaiSo8NzBHKjAOuYVT9jUEk5K7JPw5Do7hxtccrzhEB1xUBa2IImHEFBTlt+\n0cqNYrmeFWIfo5ncbfOsR8xmCdXvic0sKxz1OS9v/GhVW2QsTsemDajSbPd0vaRL\nA0/tmVAsNsxea0xXchAxA1vRHEa3PcbzKZApWUehWY+UO3F+9k3CTto9AE3cwlAV\n0ZyFJNQcXZfcHY9z9XKmlqDtqXj65Y6jJve6hZ612zygEw8HUg6jtVx5kKH0P70y\nGTVuWV7g+8zlkYAzabnkPkBcigv5c0UaC2Bjwe3huYYGwvvtw6ufNBG6ziAwECjR\n/G/msuNfuRNmAorgpqs/oNGwTaCIxoqCVi6RgmMUS6IbH3j7JPSlsZG0digr3SOk\nff8hQxcOFdAAyflZpIZv0/n+OftmpbjofrY0ieAKYTiVLajryrGcRWiEuXv+4ihb\ndc6Ebjij9PqX3pHNQgwoNB8S4r7jpx8aTZ00ETGpOp2/h2sM9jtgC7jjcvNxioCJ\ni7N8dtee444CqWyIRTns\n=Kyo2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6210f40a1db39fd2385bf362e2aad8d7babc4956\nparent 2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785169963 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785169963 -0400\n\nci(infra): emphasize required SDK pin acknowledgement (#5085)\n\nMake the prerelease SDK pin acknowledgement requirement stand out more\nclearly in the sticky PR comment by prefixing the required-label line\nwith 🚨.\n\n---\n\nWhen `check_sdk_pin` warns that a package pins a prerelease SDK,\nreviewers still need to add the bypass label before merge. The required\nstep was easy to miss in the existing notice copy.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:32:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac918f83dc63d0e24e6a48b5b93cbd203fd894b9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37"}]},{"sha":"2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJmMjExNmQ1Y2Q3YmJhOThlMWIwNzMxZDVkYTc2MGE0YjkzZmZiMzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:31:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:31:19Z"},"message":"feat(code): add `install` subcommand (#5080)\n\nYou can install optional Deep Agents Code extras with a short CLI path\nthat matches the in-session command:\n\n```bash\ndcode install daytona\ndcode install fireworks\ndcode install langchain-custom --package --yes\n```\n\nPreviously this was only available as a global action flag (`dcode\n--install …`), which diverged from how management actions are normally\nexpressed as subcommands and from the in-session `/install` muscle\nmemory.\n\n`dcode --install` remains as a compatible alias. Recovery hints and help\nnow promote `dcode install`.\n\n---\n\nAdds `dcode install NAME` as the preferred way to add optional\nproviders/sandbox extras. The install implementation is shared so the\nlegacy flag path and new subcommand stay behaviorally identical.\nDistinct from `dcode tools install`, which provisions managed host\nbinaries such as ripgrep.","tree":{"sha":"b05e875d8cbf229eea3cc6899b311ff8e7518d11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b05e875d8cbf229eea3cc6899b311ff8e7518d11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4fXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7dEQAB2gxvZsVK63Je7BDekm90oJ\nPWxB/0yn21An16+VFLCjV4YyXeoMOtw52PU45pZh3xjpZKo+hP1OUtZdPHHY94Nf\nbSwNbZBe6By26TDUpaCFtkTsc5LtexGWlUIcE+CVWJ2cvwHv41NdTRthrbMUNDR8\nm6Qzc+Ok/cw5Kfbi6RjQVl9QpMczUCalYS69MJbHrMwL7uVNvfJnm+x1aGhEQfgM\nFcFqHs1f9iXkOl7HukNI4TKyJmba1XCvqQzgwXd+vjydviJX3pB2hLXwp+KsKBL1\nHhCaGlVor0eZQEL/ZKpb/8IHBC2tpIxIkASfGcanfQsbC/dvJ3Fx7sBbNz8Ivq5a\nHQkhgdMVq6b3Skr7wwYJzowYtzze0QFES2mILqRZsNbHIZkBtm1hzt3E0tOk09G6\nZxH9JgCaTe5S6OWp+QQ6R5iVll0LhS1FODs3xqBZLsV5/dSorbWzOJLweNxMi0XE\nHiEVhZg1eKGPIevU2AUaOtr4dP5g1yOuDxAQC5YPHiHr6e8W6fHYi7acxLUkfawr\npuh3bIotPb0u81PKdnUXrF7toALKkl2fd+/+OmPN/jnPAVlOAnU1zUmsg3EkioWP\n5qJ96vDwN58pGzGUwdH/5JgXYHcWoXZ9Tq1RR5ANaeATmrZ7xim/PqZBw+Zh61FA\nop6mvJ68AkGwaZ4z/4hN\n=jmwR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b05e875d8cbf229eea3cc6899b311ff8e7518d11\nparent e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785169879 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785169879 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add `install` subcommand (#5080)\n\nYou can install optional Deep Agents Code extras with a short CLI path\nthat matches the in-session command:\n\n```bash\ndcode install daytona\ndcode install fireworks\ndcode install langchain-custom --package --yes\n```\n\nPreviously this was only available as a global action flag (`dcode\n--install …`), which diverged from how management actions are normally\nexpressed as subcommands and from the in-session `/install` muscle\nmemory.\n\n`dcode --install` remains as a compatible alias. Recovery hints and help\nnow promote `dcode install`.\n\n---\n\nAdds `dcode install NAME` as the preferred way to add optional\nproviders/sandbox extras. The install implementation is shared so the\nlegacy flag path and new subcommand stay behaviorally identical.\nDistinct from `dcode tools install`, which provisions managed host\nbinaries such as ripgrep.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:31:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f2116d5cd7bba98e1b0731d5da760a4b93ffb37/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9"}]},{"sha":"e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUwNWY3YzJhODI1ZjNkYzJmZGZjMDc1ZDQwOTJiN2IxNWQ4OWIxYTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:31:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:31:05Z"},"message":"fix(code): offload server graph bootstrap cwd calls off the event loop (#5081)\n\nCloses #5043\n\nOn Windows, starting `dcode` after credentials resolve no longer aborts\nwith `BlockingError: Blocking call to os.getcwd` during server graph\nreadiness. Graph bootstrap now finishes and the agent run continues\nnormally.\n\n---\n\nOnce a provider key is available, the server graph factory was still\ndoing path/cwd work directly on LangGraph's async loop: resolving the\nproject context, importing settings (which can walk for a project root),\nand reloading dotenv from that path. On Windows those paths call\n`os.getcwd()` inside `Path.resolve()` / `Path.cwd()`, and blockbuster\nrejects that on the server loop, so readiness fails with 500 before the\nmodel can run.\n\nThis is separate from the earlier `filelock` 3.30 cwd issue — same error\nclass, different call chain after credentials succeed.\n\nThe bootstrap setup now follows the same off-loop pattern already used\nfor `create_model` and `create_cli_agent`. Unit coverage asserts the\nproject-context / settings steps run on a worker thread.","tree":{"sha":"36d078b05e106b929a779cfe0be517c746404987","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/36d078b05e106b929a779cfe0be517c746404987"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4fJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU1QQAErYxsjyvRe4ptxrFBD/FiI8\narocB8E8S21hjU0ObrC1WbNz2jStkj50ufeC5nWR5AuJr/nBEduypb8GO2tlKBjB\nFD16mXCVvguy1oLbRLCL3kdlO77Y4ramxMvPuOb6ZBe/u0bZJUb2ubOVrbdWy9GY\nYGevJalQdy4vP8Cv7Oz/CPOZdz4nDt9wSJmqKeR6quKnMpY78grbdfUMl2h20/E3\nzQ5npghPg6ssh4cYab/5A45m2zcffdxLwr1tRbf9bnxnuIr+1G2OZIPN6al/sSgm\ngi3wbsN99tnaQp9gNgoHy1GbDd/EeN4MqkzRE1RmsCjZkODuJ+mSjwmCeCI7i2n8\n8JM9Y2rvVegNFyT141/KQf2MQ+ZALgItqRzh4+kRefG1x02lb7wMnUKyYkU7P7za\nCss3osssgVv3cqqit8Bv9JLA65NVGk+zT11YycxX1bZsjyOvm6XuGOCVBjNeFJSb\ntgNdyUEnjFDiWEnte0Avw4i+Uajb5qDNcxzG39HjP1vCHXlyvHmnIF437p1UGKrc\nRxMRSDpMMfPWp+uFm5xVUdovyEcWx7CTWRtP4kF8Gz6dmdd5QCBleun8T/AIMfp5\nzw7s7DSUo/Pf+F3NrAD/JLLe2sQ0ZTjksPWor2gLWrrXYEVLCJhK7mn8rGgY0Bdl\nZ9PoqAfJINtTLuuGQvXV\n=6v0D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 36d078b05e106b929a779cfe0be517c746404987\nparent 92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785169865 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785169865 -0400\n\nfix(code): offload server graph bootstrap cwd calls off the event loop (#5081)\n\nCloses #5043\n\nOn Windows, starting `dcode` after credentials resolve no longer aborts\nwith `BlockingError: Blocking call to os.getcwd` during server graph\nreadiness. Graph bootstrap now finishes and the agent run continues\nnormally.\n\n---\n\nOnce a provider key is available, the server graph factory was still\ndoing path/cwd work directly on LangGraph's async loop: resolving the\nproject context, importing settings (which can walk for a project root),\nand reloading dotenv from that path. On Windows those paths call\n`os.getcwd()` inside `Path.resolve()` / `Path.cwd()`, and blockbuster\nrejects that on the server loop, so readiness fails with 500 before the\nmodel can run.\n\nThis is separate from the earlier `filelock` 3.30 cwd issue — same error\nclass, different call chain after credentials succeed.\n\nThe bootstrap setup now follows the same off-loop pattern already used\nfor `create_model` and `create_cli_agent`. Unit coverage asserts the\nproject-context / settings steps run on a worker thread.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:31:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e05f7c2a825f3dc2fdfc075d4092b7b15d89b1a9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c"}]},{"sha":"92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkyYjUxOTM5MWY1ODRhY2I3Nzg2MTIxNDY5ZTQ1ZTg1MGE5NGUwNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:30:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:30:57Z"},"message":"fix(code): toast model no-op notice instead of inline message (#5074)\n\nSelecting a model that is already active now shows the \"Already using\nprovider:model\" notice as a transient toast instead of an inline chat\nmessage.\n\n---\n\nRe-selecting the already-active model is a no-op — transient feedback,\nnot part of the conversation — so an inline `AppMessage` was the wrong\nsurface and left permanent chat noise. This moves the notice to\n`App.notify()` (with `markup=False`, since the model spec and any\n`--model-params` suffix contain `:` / `=` that Textual would otherwise\nparse as Rich markup). The existing duplicate-suppression guard is\npreserved so a repeated identical selection doesn't stack toasts, and\n`--model-params` still emits an updated toast. Actual switches and error\ncases keep their inline messages.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/cde4ba2c-12aa-891d-2822-dd6bf3235ab2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b279c0b13928281bab7ba8f2ac209ad9e4e1aa46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b279c0b13928281bab7ba8f2ac209ad9e4e1aa46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4fBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeEYQAEKJaFZX4lfc57P3NLCvZgQH\nqy6xiwUzxD470upWc3Rr1jGYLV0mfGr4FQNkx4yxuFhp0TUjVe2/uXwD4luZPxH7\nbuynYlluuBkoJ6savuCNbzF3JIL9Ihkrqwy3F9nmy9Opfj3B9/eJMYPXj0npiFK5\nIL1AkTSen8FD2NR/ob/mxRVCCa0zG+0K43MR9JlmrqJLjShcQM6l0P0Nv70BXtR0\njHHb9N4e6MkaH8obNYFuw3xPHtdmCPWgiHQyCpgHkuGWHQ0rMjs7rLJR3KHIeHbz\n8EhlXyv4o9JW450iH7/whs8EQ9BJ7XPddsuX/jBnOEhUVEVP8fer+4RJ/zvYQI0q\n1DAjEIUC3cpdP6ZGTJnJ4/01EeIkmkMnrdq85ehuAwxIqtqxVhzp2TPH7cVjJIIO\nRiSpzKBDOYQy48BjtL+gYTW+uaLSl7l3Kd2rjEvYkGDAWd/WNqDMtI5YhTIStGI9\nr/ehnhaicuXiyb3AGyk3ql5MEAEixrH+1O90GZ1qm6r27cMvIrhW/YAp/gtFAvJO\nFFTvhbXto0opf82iFF1u4KhxjBibaKj01V0hPDAAFZrPLOkcCRS4wcpa72J5AVh9\nk1kVOYnqUdm6ZBF5f+PTK14rVFgSPBDbfkfZzq4MyEtUbp5Z1LHK27hruQKKQl0r\n1iLgPgppSbewehpvswVw\n=rJEd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b279c0b13928281bab7ba8f2ac209ad9e4e1aa46\nparent 803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785169857 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785169857 -0400\n\nfix(code): toast model no-op notice instead of inline message (#5074)\n\nSelecting a model that is already active now shows the \"Already using\nprovider:model\" notice as a transient toast instead of an inline chat\nmessage.\n\n---\n\nRe-selecting the already-active model is a no-op — transient feedback,\nnot part of the conversation — so an inline `AppMessage` was the wrong\nsurface and left permanent chat noise. This moves the notice to\n`App.notify()` (with `markup=False`, since the model spec and any\n`--model-params` suffix contain `:` / `=` that Textual would otherwise\nparse as Rich markup). The existing duplicate-suppression guard is\npreserved so a repeated identical selection doesn't stack toasts, and\n`--model-params` still emits an updated toast. Actual switches and error\ncases keep their inline messages.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/cde4ba2c-12aa-891d-2822-dd6bf3235ab2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:30:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/92b519391f584acb7786121469e45e850a94e06c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6"}]},{"sha":"803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgwM2I4MzI5ZGI3ZDIzMjBjYTY5OGI2ZWY2NzUzZTk1Y2M5NTJiZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:30:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:30:13Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.48 (#5048)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.48](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.47...deepagents-code==0.1.48)\n(2026-07-27)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added Fireworks `kimi-k3`, GLM-5.2-Fast, and Kimi-K3 to model\nselection and recommended models.\n([#5082](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5082),\n[#5072](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5072))\n- Migrated legacy hooks to v2 events.\n([#4971](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4971))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Require an `AGENTS.md` marker for `/agent` discovery, resolving\nunintended discovery behavior.\n([#5076](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5076), closes\n[#4991](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4991))\n- Removed the redundant `/restart` hint from the restart prompt.\n([#5083](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5083))\n- Removed the caret flash in plugin type-to-search.\n([#5078](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5078))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"38281888c5d21b2ce814bd30553b3a7de123e0bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/38281888c5d21b2ce814bd30553b3a7de123e0bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4eVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArkIQAGX7hHbVhxCL3v07j4UMJQvJ\n12oF23xJffNkMjJgMZ+T8IyNk37ioocIS3WhFSXkUA9WKJbml2pWlazY8TnUG+Nc\nWqRgDSuG+btry/EsXhdfq7glyZBzK/kfTeXUmYjIrFs5QWD0JunCzlL3PuQEdLbd\n3pYD+KrULinzgoRsmhRLkuv2DfCE4dR6NiWfdfGFRNIU5u+D5yv24IQOFpP+D26l\nnnKp3ctGip3H5fB2TYwtsWg0gzNMJK84+TBQPU8T4Glh+yBMuHSCHYwTE32xQIkT\nubaJyjiV4t2HjoMZYwV0kqJ43SLHZ+MJFeuQW7E5vHrWuVVmqsQ7QuyZUm2ojui4\nEutTgJbL0wzGJdd2VRDBVQSV0rTUcW0VTbGSTI7zH0yT6WACFDbLnQKYGCsg9ONS\nPKiAxBmBFdrcjUDlouyhCIiPLeHqht2E0JhR1NhYd1kjPg/sQ5vOXmuc5Rs9U8BM\nLuvISYYVnu38GXhJGPmYEqPPU5pgrI3JBuicZgnkhFlz3x03jn49Bcst1PpYqU0Z\n+EUDSkgXA8BPyjc2BiHPIxQiy7BfsWCd1e4XeQwHJfE6PpTLa2stg5bjBPUswqbg\nlfgDX6CQ41sCV9qTA6Jy37Pibdsu7gA+5wymaFltaJ7xxln1BrMiuOLtL5bv0FZ5\nzMZrMOE3VlnM99MHVB0R\n=oDFA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38281888c5d21b2ce814bd30553b3a7de123e0bf\nparent 82e799c7191adcb3bf96eb0435d55edd58cc1883\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785169813 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785169813 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.48 (#5048)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.48](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.47...deepagents-code==0.1.48)\n(2026-07-27)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added Fireworks `kimi-k3`, GLM-5.2-Fast, and Kimi-K3 to model\nselection and recommended models.\n([#5082](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5082),\n[#5072](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5072))\n- Migrated legacy hooks to v2 events.\n([#4971](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4971))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Require an `AGENTS.md` marker for `/agent` discovery, resolving\nunintended discovery behavior.\n([#5076](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5076), closes\n[#4991](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4991))\n- Removed the redundant `/restart` hint from the restart prompt.\n([#5083](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5083))\n- Removed the caret flash in plugin type-to-search.\n([#5078](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5078))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:30:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/803b8329db7d2320ca698b6ef6753e95cc952be6/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"82e799c7191adcb3bf96eb0435d55edd58cc1883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/82e799c7191adcb3bf96eb0435d55edd58cc1883","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/82e799c7191adcb3bf96eb0435d55edd58cc1883"}]},{"sha":"82e799c7191adcb3bf96eb0435d55edd58cc1883","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgyZTc5OWM3MTkxYWRjYjNiZjk2ZWIwNDM1ZDU1ZWRkNThjYzE4ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:12:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:12:23Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Fireworks `kimi-k3` to model switcher (#5082)\n\nAdd Fireworks `kimi-k3` (Kimi K3) to the recommended models in the\n`/model` switcher.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8c07df59-536b-379b-27b3-