"user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80"}]},{"sha":"b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIzNDg5OWZjY2QwNTFhYjc0MTAwMGM3NzFlZWY5YTJkYzQ0MzlkODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T16:08:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T16:08:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): drop redundant `/restart` hint from restart prompt (#5083)\n\nThe post-install restart prompt already tells the user \"Enter to\nrestart, Esc to defer\", so the body line's \", or defer with `/restart`\"\nwas redundant/confusing. This trims the default body to just \"Restart\nthe server to load it now.\"\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/06c3fe48-99a5-50e8-eeba-ae3b65ab8949)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"86b1bfec71e843c2ebcba7dcc0abae9c08a2c955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/86b1bfec71e843c2ebcba7dcc0abae9c08a2c955"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4KDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFPYQAENCjy4JX7nI0mQ/SOyFMG1v\n2F+eWr0nN3UpilpXXjEPrHCUivICtrp5O92tPrFpIDf7A5OFYctCFSGtwfz9tEnF\nWeO34t8Gua9N8O40rSd8vw5WecBgJ1bXU7cuv+mcv9rlGyjrcqnzcpNeeAdTk60F\nY4NrGhF7vEDFtKs0IrOEfNJ4zPjcBfygwU5Npb8XcaVxVOVCNZmrTxpuze6pLwl8\ng/ouNF9MrkC2arAoG57UA6jmPEvUgwkjs9f3uRFTkF103DIH4VSQ/DtpngULCYL7\noznpl060uEizAiCWf+gPZ5LPWrLN7Pf9JAIP6xqmavYd+vEKDyRYXg/H4x2YPyYc\nkHuoHGX+AtMqmuTscJwHbP/OPL12Hw9uNkFS5vsbfpEufRIPZ6qJdVEmocbo/y5Z\np4vc0ZkUwkyqyJTDZBozlLTqJL0OmsHWnCnTZOXA6iQlkNa/sufT/GkmwFs9yiyW\nJuF07cDBVVOxLAHSgRszGl6nUvKlTS70ErxmliBDHuI5kfdFHpkY4K0qexdJBHGU\nRO9IjPVOAuI+zwuywIKd79lhVDwcrnjm6PhvYdN1LFEGNP//mRmkBCnNqWEmLEGr\nzpd5/knbZW48dye1WsT9mE/cqBxlhFmoTi7+wUm76+YPIL1GDg6teV2O1k1mj57o\napJ0sjlOlRtGz1TfVt9A\n=/cCd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 86b1bfec71e843c2ebcba7dcc0abae9c08a2c955\nparent 4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785168515 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785168515 -0400\n\nfix(code): drop redundant `/restart` hint from restart prompt (#5083)\n\nThe post-install restart prompt already tells the user \"Enter to\nrestart, Esc to defer\", so the body line's \", or defer with `/restart`\"\nwas redundant/confusing. This trims the default body to just \"Restart\nthe server to load it now.\"\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/06c3fe48-99a5-50e8-eeba-ae3b65ab8949)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T16:08:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b34899fccd051ab741000c771eef9a2dc4439d80/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2"}]},{"sha":"4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRmODEwODE1Mjg2ZTkwYmIyZWU5ZDNiODI1NzNmMmExZDZiMTE2YjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T15:25:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T15:25:26Z"},"message":"ci(infra): block and surface release-please fan-out (#5077)\n\nAfter a bump-worthy PR touches files under several managed packages,\nrelease-please attributes that single commit to every touched component\nand opens a separate release PR for each. The existing lockfile-only\ngate missed the common case where dependency lower bounds in\n`pyproject.toml` were also edited, and applying a bypass label only left\na quiet ℹ️ note.\n\nPre-merge checks now fail bump-worthy PRs that edit real files in more\nthan one release-please component (or only lockfiles inside a managed\npackage), stickies prescribe the single-package feature/fix +\n`chore(deps):` split, and bypass labels get a loud warning naming every\ncomponent still on track for a release. Docs and the PR template spell\nout the one-component rule, and a post-merge watch flags open release\nPRs whose only unreleased package delta is lockfile churn.\n\n---\n\nRelated postmortem: multi-component fan-out from a feature PR that also\nbumped shared dependency floors.\n\n**Not in this PR:** restricting who can apply bypass labels / renaming\nlabels / requiring a written justification reply.","tree":{"sha":"a3cc8a6146f86acb3dfd3e4d8e4d67ac1527a564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a3cc8a6146f86acb3dfd3e4d8e4d67ac1527a564"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ3hmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAUAQAC1Sf3yCAh2T+WG8QVXDNLkW\nT+o+e1MbuzJYZACHBlgTJYUIT69eufvEqFQuQbn9xNDyMiZpFs40Nu55D6zwVV9E\njTj8YeVNT0o0bqnmTfxPsxIHSQwaQu9PG48nOhzprDNjuupqAjJ8SRwEP0UYwg9V\nZXoKQknbJPvaLPvZkazY3iniv3RK9cWSWukJRECjzE1mz/9tLdkoWEm1qKWCa1gf\nRjPgDvFQTXdBayBnfMVjJOH40X3hif+7vodZg9HeQR41bsU6mbXexhdeRSh7D0U2\nbW+57rJJFpXv2dXMOTzLrf0b4VAZWKYdqok+pgKUDEeU8dP+Iav4i7xrE3tq5j2d\neyIHFQW2jCK7fhyqsHoRvJD7H7cK+B1jENPzrDwGObkg0GSnTSfF/YeyOE32I9X0\njzNG56o1dY7lKudBGLIiPSdzeXCDx/9IR4qRlLjvN8OpRcf+3QevmPwS6x8NftUv\n1hMDOJr73F+gpHgLWpjD9Cun/2BPvrasSQf3MLOF1cFJq4KxhmAfTaHBcTTe+A9e\nFlHYxieIBABpoj2ze8VE3r/YVPHhCHrtdBdPjhQ60S6JAAozQXEt1+z76V9HcUe7\n7vCZEpRh1+90PugBoN3O4I/I2npCAH4cpCyxHXj4+b0nYFYA9BjWqJkGJXh3cDFo\n9CXBk4SsDiP9qrv2908W\n=bOZs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a3cc8a6146f86acb3dfd3e4d8e4d67ac1527a564\nparent 504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785165926 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785165926 -0400\n\nci(infra): block and surface release-please fan-out (#5077)\n\nAfter a bump-worthy PR touches files under several managed packages,\nrelease-please attributes that single commit to every touched component\nand opens a separate release PR for each. The existing lockfile-only\ngate missed the common case where dependency lower bounds in\n`pyproject.toml` were also edited, and applying a bypass label only left\na quiet ℹ️ note.\n\nPre-merge checks now fail bump-worthy PRs that edit real files in more\nthan one release-please component (or only lockfiles inside a managed\npackage), stickies prescribe the single-package feature/fix +\n`chore(deps):` split, and bypass labels get a loud warning naming every\ncomponent still on track for a release. Docs and the PR template spell\nout the one-component rule, and a post-merge watch flags open release\nPRs whose only unreleased package delta is lockfile churn.\n\n---\n\nRelated postmortem: multi-component fan-out from a feature PR that also\nbumped shared dependency floors.\n\n**Not in this PR:** restricting who can apply bypass labels / renaming\nlabels / requiring a written justification reply.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T15:25:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f810815286e90bb2ee9d3b82573f2a1d6b116b2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd"}]},{"sha":"504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUwNGZmMGE2NjdhYmYxMmFkM2ZkMmY3MmI0Y2I3YmUyMzBiN2MzZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T15:09:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T15:09:01Z"},"message":"refactor(code): dedup provider install-extras recovery hints (#5027)\n\nDeduplicates the provider / install-extras recovery-hint logic in\n`deepagents-code` that was hand-copied across the interactive TUI, the\nheadless CLI, and model init.\n\n---\n\nThe \"missing provider package → install hint\" decision tree\n(`extra_for_package` → `/install {extra}`, else a raw\n`install_package_command` with its introspection/validation guard) was\nimplemented twice — once in `config.py` when raising\n`MissingProviderPackageError`, and once in `app.py` when rendering the\nserver-startup recovery hint. Separately, the\n`install_extra_recovery_command` try/except-with-fallback pattern was\nrepeated four times across `app.py`'s `/install` handler and `main.py`'s\n`--install` handler.\n\nThis extracts two shared helpers so the branching, fallback, and error\nhandling live in one place:\n\n- `resolve_install_hint` (+ the `InstallHint` dataclass) in\n`extras_info.py`, consumed by both Cluster-A call sites. Each caller\nkeeps its own sentence wording but shares the resolution logic.\n- `safe_install_extra_recovery_command` in `update_check.py`, consumed\nby all four Cluster-B call sites.\n\nNo user-facing message or behavior changes. Existing tests in\n`test_config.py`, `test_app.py`, `test_install_command.py`, and\n`test_main.py` act as the regression guard; two of them asserted the\ninternal `extra_for_package` call signature and were updated for the new\nindirection. New unit tests cover both helpers.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/006f8565-ef8c-fab0-cde6-0f766fda7f68)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/006f8565-ef8c-fab0-cde6-0f766fda7f68/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2b61bd986a1bd7bbd63ebb2bcbe805967fff695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f2b61bd986a1bd7bbd63ebb2bcbe805967fff695"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ3SNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUzwQADZh5fnW/XWC3KLwZdcUL4pU\nabAJvljnqwon2EvSEHjKTnFELi2GQ/5tzqcPm58lkCzhxyl5yx6D00/TnrtLjHdK\nZMNP5hLsVYd0y/GnHdcD9czGU6a4TtBP7htkEQ96JCgdcogN0+gXzH/zTTScZ75r\n8ORdlVuNFS+jG9FKG3xwJoisv8hJfi4CnfpXuek65b+EJDfwOXXzYZrVy8Y8cXZn\nPWb8MwqAvPPjBCQlFZudL/tgZ+qH0UWG9Oprmi2AjTbrrAwyMte9O9mWcXJH94zC\nG4Fhr25y7cz6PRh31mEEcA9W4OIFUfPjsBa8J495vOsozRrKlwWeCV29tFdfg6lT\nPf3+n0eA/yYZZTxnRKqDQC+HqP25uIrk6toIJO6YqWJlFaIVGdTVxytmzoUyVQ3u\nvTIc2G+e/c/uR0lfRlCGV9JqF3JZZSd8KtOMTgK8EPKBS4nVqc9ySrhnSOymdeGl\ntC4unra3R1TWszgK6p8Aa/3wXDr3j6A/7upIgc7ISsUoPwV/R7ay0V0y1G0Ae8aQ\npLaNHezZY0wstyoH3RWr6x6ztqX6frdmjNNdoQGf4hnC0JeHDBYvqbMjj4TfST5B\nc2Tecwn5hPg0tIuc8OMTySwUyBcnaZM+ISFdEyImSuKVHs5SLmt7wZsyScvzxhPL\nG7p6tUR1ylPshBV9Bfaa\n=h2xj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f2b61bd986a1bd7bbd63ebb2bcbe805967fff695\nparent 6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785164941 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785164941 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): dedup provider install-extras recovery hints (#5027)\n\nDeduplicates the provider / install-extras recovery-hint logic in\n`deepagents-code` that was hand-copied across the interactive TUI, the\nheadless CLI, and model init.\n\n---\n\nThe \"missing provider package → install hint\" decision tree\n(`extra_for_package` → `/install {extra}`, else a raw\n`install_package_command` with its introspection/validation guard) was\nimplemented twice — once in `config.py` when raising\n`MissingProviderPackageError`, and once in `app.py` when rendering the\nserver-startup recovery hint. Separately, the\n`install_extra_recovery_command` try/except-with-fallback pattern was\nrepeated four times across `app.py`'s `/install` handler and `main.py`'s\n`--install` handler.\n\nThis extracts two shared helpers so the branching, fallback, and error\nhandling live in one place:\n\n- `resolve_install_hint` (+ the `InstallHint` dataclass) in\n`extras_info.py`, consumed by both Cluster-A call sites. Each caller\nkeeps its own sentence wording but shares the resolution logic.\n- `safe_install_extra_recovery_command` in `update_check.py`, consumed\nby all four Cluster-B call sites.\n\nNo user-facing message or behavior changes. Existing tests in\n`test_config.py`, `test_app.py`, `test_install_command.py`, and\n`test_main.py` act as the regression guard; two of them asserted the\ninternal `extra_for_package` call signature and were updated for the new\nindirection. New unit tests cover both helpers.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/006f8565-ef8c-fab0-cde6-0f766fda7f68)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/006f8565-ef8c-fab0-cde6-0f766fda7f68/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T15:09:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/504ff0a667abf12ad3fd2f72b4cb7be230b7c3dd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a"}]},{"sha":"6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY1MDZlMTU5NGNlMzhlNzVkMTViOGM4YWE1Y2U4ODUyZGY4MTFmN2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T15:07:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T15:07:19Z"},"message":"style(code): simplify Auto classifier unavailable messages (#5079)\n\nWhen Auto cannot classify a gated action, the transcript now says so\nmore plainly—and when Auto itself stopped waiting, it names Auto's wait\nlimit instead of sounding like a provider outage.\n\nFor example, after Auto's default 20s classifier wait with no decision,\nthe UI shows:\n\n```text\nAuto classifier unavailable: no decision within Auto's 20s limit (action blocked)\n```\n\nA real classifier call failure still stays type-only, e.g. `failed\n(TimeoutError)`, so the two cases stay distinct. Underlying provider\ndetail continues to go to logs / Debug Console only.","tree":{"sha":"c2c5048ee5cfa2a2b0f906c37448aafc0703cbda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c2c5048ee5cfa2a2b0f906c37448aafc0703cbda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ3QnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY7QQAFTpGmxsdQsc7QAKtsNx2g2U\narCHn8DT2zUzPvnZEbDaQgLs3gwuCFpwEfvNCMNOc9fmsAmnm5ady8sME+YNtton\n9hQuGQiDEjQnlM8HuX6Dg6ppc63Qxbljms5+z7hfgw5/UZNQZvig+lSuYsSm0HRF\nkskC9pevHjs1JJgJP7XT2XGYniGWiELMgWx/hzIdBB34adhsfVhWk2xn3JBK9fhV\nVjhB8UjWDh+Tx7X6Od4o+x7Yk+Ao6id0yWDbqayfqjJjM+QfnHCuxrYlA5kPQnGk\n0MfAHxceQ39zNiXy5pRixsDH9jAN5DiMv9WOXZRjKyYTx4WczxO6aZiTa3EQWqdK\npnxr1ulSw/1B5DGiw63uxHEbIJG+NwnX85zphL8b1LgYQ5GvE45iihvK+zMjYops\nXVkDAAwTFv6HzhaJJj/nmeahOoKYfXfR6SjX875raJf0jzRTCRXqThS4+Mu4nnyW\n5ol/LKQ+0RRsLPZh4ipD5gANhaBRp7Ri67bobtbUBSyz3H+xE5eSqM1ViWEpvaIV\nFKAVAEI1lrw1reH1o4dmOXnM0lkVlLv1uBVEhC5DMLD2D3doq9MmXmC+0xMKrJNL\n6gqVQagThAOtJnHfjtAps9wt+fQ3wSomiaYB+rj1oSIL4+rAkkTgPIwVx+tveBw3\n7lVMJAxeJFsDmQhFAdoa\n=5jmZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c2c5048ee5cfa2a2b0f906c37448aafc0703cbda\nparent aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785164839 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785164839 -0400\n\nstyle(code): simplify Auto classifier unavailable messages (#5079)\n\nWhen Auto cannot classify a gated action, the transcript now says so\nmore plainly—and when Auto itself stopped waiting, it names Auto's wait\nlimit instead of sounding like a provider outage.\n\nFor example, after Auto's default 20s classifier wait with no decision,\nthe UI shows:\n\n```text\nAuto classifier unavailable: no decision within Auto's 20s limit (action blocked)\n```\n\nA real classifier call failure still stays type-only, e.g. `failed\n(TimeoutError)`, so the two cases stay distinct. Underlying provider\ndetail continues to go to logs / Debug Console only.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T15:07:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6506e1594ce38e75d15b8c8aa5ce8852df811f7a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30"}]},{"sha":"aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFmZjE0MzVjZThkNTZjNjIzY2ZlZmZiMjczMWFkY2Q0YmYwNTdjMzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T14:53:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T14:53:13Z"},"message":"fix(code): require `AGENTS.md` marker for `/agent` discovery (#5076)\n\nMakes `/agent` listing fail-closed: only `~/.deepagents/<name>/`\ndirectories that contain a real `AGENTS.md` file are shown as switchable\nagents.\n\n---\n\n#4991 stopped the leak of `plugins/` and `conversation_history/` by\nexpanding a reserved-name denylist. That still defaulted to \"every\nsubdirectory is an agent unless named.\" Any new app-owned dir under\n`~/.deepagents/` would leak again unless the denylist was updated.\n\nDiscovery now requires the agent marker the product already stamps —\n`AGENTS.md` (created empty on first use when memory is enabled). Bare\nfolders, app state (`bin/`, `plugins/`, `conversation_history/`,\n`.state/`, and future siblings), directory symlinks, and symlink markers\nare excluded without maintaining a name denylist.\n\nRelated #4991","tree":{"sha":"3ba41d3c2a52e1040444f87caea74fb55037622a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3ba41d3c2a52e1040444f87caea74fb55037622a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ3DZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmnoQAGijugxQeGxv7O1F1FgxS6EP\n/u8+pisfwPA/VRnoiZKtC4F0i3+Ua78vui/+ujBvP6v9V/36LnyTbbdAc7PjvwYS\ncluwS4Jr6E1IDSxUWhAe9J7Adep8YlemKtyzc/+UaO6rQ06LpvUJvGM5SxFvI34y\ntu7NfA1u+Fo/OtcFJwtWx+oKFAcHXOLJufnsEcEPxt6caBbNzXoo61Ia0UK2zM0t\n0coBOJyhP1jt7vgw7+ofZTADs9f8/HOJSGtg/ZdoxCQBodNX/FioQlmtGkgpmpZM\njrTLYAPsJHowmdwT+N1dm4c29wN46VU6TKUBtuBRaeHT8Qfl3yLxY2a+xTnT02JO\n6hOfUJxOjvvN0G/Qdz9oJMrVQvLPmkUqDvYsMfZu6RZWerGBGG42QkS/NgVy0FrP\nO7+TzFvB7Mp1QoOwhiqdyL2+pOfl36gza7+KqEYbEVpxQpm29GPLcvvOmZ/Rc2sF\nFWVVSn9h0aZrczR7bbFxP/O85rXtFPCUbAbLhbREuWqKXenTwLzAxE28u0Zp6riy\nLFYoSdjKwLF6isMtEejtzRbiXr9gb2tssvzGbxzfLCu6Gti8f7szpXSxTTCUuf0E\nHSl5oqXrxegRrQdlPB/rtsEwq/6NiOVGH6JsQqGbgVDPIGQRO83143fA815sVuWp\ndN2dvRJ7ZzlDx3M8MUit\n=AXIF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3ba41d3c2a52e1040444f87caea74fb55037622a\nparent 7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785163993 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785163993 -0400\n\nfix(code): require `AGENTS.md` marker for `/agent` discovery (#5076)\n\nMakes `/agent` listing fail-closed: only `~/.deepagents/<name>/`\ndirectories that contain a real `AGENTS.md` file are shown as switchable\nagents.\n\n---\n\n#4991 stopped the leak of `plugins/` and `conversation_history/` by\nexpanding a reserved-name denylist. That still defaulted to \"every\nsubdirectory is an agent unless named.\" Any new app-owned dir under\n`~/.deepagents/` would leak again unless the denylist was updated.\n\nDiscovery now requires the agent marker the product already stamps —\n`AGENTS.md` (created empty on first use when memory is enabled). Bare\nfolders, app state (`bin/`, `plugins/`, `conversation_history/`,\n`.state/`, and future siblings), directory symlinks, and symlink markers\nare excluded without maintaining a name denylist.\n\nRelated #4991","verified_at":"2026-07-27T14:53:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aff1435ce8d56c623cfeffb2731adcd4bf057c30/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45"}]},{"sha":"7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdkNjllMzc5Njc4ZDg0OTFhYjYyYzllMjI5NDI2ZDUwYjczNjZjNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T14:44:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T14:44:55Z"},"message":"fix(code): remove plugin type-to-search caret flash (#5078)\n\nRelated #4842\n\nTyping a letter from the plugin list to start search no longer flashes\nan empty caret before the character appears.\n\n---\n\nAfter #4842, type-to-search focused the filter first and inserted the\ncharacter afterward. That left one empty focused frame (and relied on a\nshort timer to collapse selection after `select_on_focus`).\n\nThis matches the thread selector more closely by turning off\n`select_on_focus` on the plugin filter, writing the typed letter into\nthe value first, placing the caret at the end, and only then focusing —\nso the first focused frame already shows the character.","tree":{"sha":"4e0da8e22583cc6ac09b5f32708d722adaddb8be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4e0da8e22583cc6ac09b5f32708d722adaddb8be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ27nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+dUQABtLzbqyThvM+ErK5bwz91Dd\n6NV/bO3L4erotOjHCvlhL00uBR6icHl5mHnL/SM7JeeU68YISQqBwTPSQ46Eqqj8\nQ+4hHy1uzn4CtrPkLp5BV7nlrQKgCXKlRzCP+5HLWJhhP+Yo3Zbaz6M2fO2vaI1k\nezcQ5hUdCWkUL0maO4Jr+MV6kcno6fPa5oCoZbzxNG1873mwb8DsUb9ndMDLuK7L\nbuyobVpNx3F/TlsYYMvbkdp/Dc9qPRBoM1PzV7VK1RBYgi2aYXHwdbjVQQ6s+LgL\nZaD9Oar9BXRF/V91KCAoWxLQpWN7JYY7a9P4NLsbXGQ0hUUz/owTVgN74iDtQ8Sa\nDYjm2Ypq86nNNWoJMapfBHAg+Z4bZlriDVdUExMXR/s+ym8NZ37rDT4Uk49nOiUl\n9UglpBg/08SjR0AGLCbWoUQUFm0lUGZGbMZDyj3yYe+pyQ74DP7EOxAbBgGFjj1g\nC/rZBNMkYL1yZV0TlBiHww2n+s6MZDNFeoffm5Hd+QqkAvewMOkHhLRARwJLlE6N\nNUL/wfzn3ewfdvDOiWp9PBX+FdyQxdAkwa5jORMz59783WlyjyhXP3T6GmRU1zPv\ngCKVKGJeWyhD5VgAmp3iGtQ7qCONR/Gj0c+pm14VzpgZ6EAQPLew0OI9mmwUosrB\nnT1u45t02mEBUX1tppJI\n=oyYe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4e0da8e22583cc6ac09b5f32708d722adaddb8be\nparent 98af36f0fd0b31e7a6e85673ee5668c40efc5b4c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785163495 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785163495 -0400\n\nfix(code): remove plugin type-to-search caret flash (#5078)\n\nRelated #4842\n\nTyping a letter from the plugin list to start search no longer flashes\nan empty caret before the character appears.\n\n---\n\nAfter #4842, type-to-search focused the filter first and inserted the\ncharacter afterward. That left one empty focused frame (and relied on a\nshort timer to collapse selection after `select_on_focus`).\n\nThis matches the thread selector more closely by turning off\n`select_on_focus` on the plugin filter, writing the typed letter into\nthe value first, placing the caret at the end, and only then focusing —\nso the first focused frame already shows the character.","verified_at":"2026-07-27T14:44:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d69e379678d8491ab62c9e229426d50b7366c45/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu