90b3f95fb5219b5d9074c7f01a1937","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYt1QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACq4QAKRtKpzVeuay5KsU3fPp3DDv\nVMhDcYGYjpfYSQcavm3Wwm6+RgRdDCpcrg0wmj/oTEGk6JGOElAaWtzQC4gb4o/T\nxST24x+mFgNpPQcq8FP8qxbv6tSP4j/7a8ovDobK6KBFliwjkE+W2iXYYhJ58tKb\nR1oVWb37SAnxMsKZ3fYRFHwctqwM0H8cK0Id645SCNODBLJxLAdvHWhoX3lbLisX\nxAjQQn9SddL7LRrOI9mYLwWrf5SNe0nAKI2u9RsS2pzFpvSmW95N1AXetIYP+/Zq\nsc6tWKs3HiJmPIt9jhbkh+jIiG53VfRImVePrpj6rHi5mOXHe40KTsuF9yqu6HmS\nw1SrT5czMNBsCX7JNT/peJ1BMpah2dIfymE5COOLOfQ6M7SOEMJfY7hxihj/WutS\nxVN4BeqEEnbqo07hM/QovmPyKtzMsst3oJ5Pu4GGLDMW6L8rakegDTSSNrKr3I2V\n1yX0lKSmg0NGgLZHYuAXl5H4uT1GN9Wt7ZPQ/HSbhQwnoY6zLULTb3HlNw8ImuSk\nlCDDCRZRZdSNh1BGFI0PXZ43pYWqUPJdEyEAqZ4sKjg4ASQVSCrBLS4kbf7Igjkt\nNmfZO1lx0QdCORfVsQ2piYY0/2EQ/wrhGtWYO7TV1oIHkLcywprhx7DwsuU4+uKz\nPQi9OsSA7K8P9iNaSVPO\n=9yDl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7b760adaee30e6e89f535011616afb67eaced93b\nparent b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784864080 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784864080 -0400\n\nfix(code): trim `web_search` and `fetch_url` tool descriptions (#5016)\n\nShortens the model-facing `web_search` and `fetch_url` tool descriptions\nby dropping provider branding, response-field inventories, and generic\n\"synthesize for the user\" instructions that do not change tool behavior.\n\n---\n\nTavily remains visible in user-facing setup and approval copy; only the\nLLM tool schema text was trimmed.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T03:34:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/170b4a6c4590b3f95fb5219b5d9074c7f01a1937","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/170b4a6c4590b3f95fb5219b5d9074c7f01a1937","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/170b4a6c4590b3f95fb5219b5d9074c7f01a1937/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e"}]},{"sha":"b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI0ZDM5YTQ0YTExYTQyMzU2ZjMwMjA4ZjFmNDViZDgyMTE1MWY1N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T03:26:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T03:26:34Z"},"message":"refactor(code): drop redundant goal-tool system prompt injection (#5023)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer appends the static “Goal and Rubric Tools”\nblock to every system prompt. Goal/rubric guidance still reaches the\nmodel through tool docstrings, durable state notices, and request-only\nnotice pinning when history no longer has the current notice in view.\n\n---\n\nThe static system-prompt block duplicated guidance already present on\n`get_goal` / `get_rubric` / `update_goal` and in the goal-state notice\npath. Dropping it keeps the durable notice write and the\ncompaction-style request pin, without mutating the system prompt on each\nturn.\n\n`GoalToolsMiddleware.wrap_model_call` now only re-pins a current\ngoal-state notice into request messages when needed, and returns the\noriginal request otherwise.","tree":{"sha":"92ca038d0dccf1eb0066bd485fb87817b168114b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/92ca038d0dccf1eb0066bd485fb87817b168114b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYttqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY18QAK9C5usP/12Guj2ICZhaBnO0\n395bDp4Nja0mKTKK8oddqsNQu8SlBI0Li05PbDSdKFmJolgBblP+POtrm7liVHoQ\n76QGQyzGLxVRqQrxkFNA3vWpk3QheYmsKlP+T8qZu5jUZvnhNs2d47KZt5gaN+0D\nzKoywc+Y8k9wtBms9GDoPfYaSIy0V7bsvmlVT0YFnkH2krnW9XONXQpNDWxV/h2S\nlliEvbz+q5Ng4V5jqflIx/23l4iLG8B2JZ9N6UkIQtR/vdQJU7wnTG1TFQLHjeHh\nfCnzZKEQh76FO3Q2sLHe0vwfG5DYGoSJwbPDwZ7SLpFPNznuXXBoMqcWqiDJgHGy\nMO07aamIoKt91/0Svdhv7io9bRkKWaS7umi3jqUh6xNRVrkXLGvwgr8h+UEqQIHB\nGH8HuyRQXR+XByFKE5fJvR9YMlLelrmERUUQ9wrBVxJrIBdA+NbhRkMRRofy4i3A\nyNdOcU5Dpc5EC6f5sT/lFMc4dQx/ARWNPbtC7nVnOfOKt0NV/K1FaJkK4sTcz4pK\nJwfpjxAUdxE9jl+rzDEkEG05TBQd7xLwStLyrdZto+qhpJad0rn0JahevVWMBkLt\nvyxXWhR2WC+U6zAnSTBEo84tSNhgG6RMo2l+TywZtg3Rjrcud+HIEOgyGDUSCUq/\nV9lDw+0JDTUYZF7I0505\n=GHxQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 92ca038d0dccf1eb0066bd485fb87817b168114b\nparent f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784863594 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784863594 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): drop redundant goal-tool system prompt injection (#5023)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer appends the static “Goal and Rubric Tools”\nblock to every system prompt. Goal/rubric guidance still reaches the\nmodel through tool docstrings, durable state notices, and request-only\nnotice pinning when history no longer has the current notice in view.\n\n---\n\nThe static system-prompt block duplicated guidance already present on\n`get_goal` / `get_rubric` / `update_goal` and in the goal-state notice\npath. Dropping it keeps the durable notice write and the\ncompaction-style request pin, without mutating the system prompt on each\nturn.\n\n`GoalToolsMiddleware.wrap_model_call` now only re-pins a current\ngoal-state notice into request messages when needed, and returns the\noriginal request otherwise.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T03:26:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4d39a44a11a42356f30208f1f45bd821151f57e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8"}]},{"sha":"f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY2Y2FmNTI0ZWVhNmVkZTI1YjE1NTdkNGQ0NTg4ZGViY2FkZDE1Zjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T03:17:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T03:17:12Z"},"message":"refactor(code): remove `get_rubric` source metadata (#5024)\n\n`get_rubric` no longer returns source provenance. Models only see active\ncriteria and grading status; goal-backed vs sticky lifecycle decisions\nstay in app state logic.\n\n---\n\nProvenance still exists internally for notice fingerprints and\nprecedence (`rubric_source` in projected goal state). This change\nremoves only the model-facing `source` field from\n`RubricSnapshot`/`get_rubric`, so the LLM is not asked to interpret\nsticky vs goal vs invocation labels.\n\nCriteria resolution is unchanged:\n- public `rubric` when present\n- else actionable goal rubric\n- else standalone sticky rubric\n\nCompletion, `update_goal` gating, and paused/complete goal withholding\nremain in app code.","tree":{"sha":"a695aa59ff230b3c48d4a4f7902f756da3369c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a695aa59ff230b3c48d4a4f7902f756da3369c66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYtk4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwYMQAH+a2dwuY+XrENe53WII8xib\nDONtUxgsVYFX5PlQEiiJ6JqvKrV73lH5mRZh06wyxwGMe76DfM0a2lTbXw1vVgKr\ngbLc9fBGLVdp11C0JpdHwcV13Si3v4sMqFrusSkU6UuZLqtN/7Xl91EaPgb8Ia3r\nJAUZsiBoautEW9Vb8PsvD/RhFmtyb/Uf1soMSiErP8G7esZ+oYWLhaqjLAx8Zw37\njvDY5XRON361MNQHu0h2e2Qk0HREl3thxs7cd6lpDd46ib5XSMWq5Exb+rZKDl2q\nLbPvsHg8xPG+4xZOeZp8/XC1C1kVxFfb+yln209XzYY+vKfVIvHf/ePsSEGJN4YN\nrZbD6nphm5kCugxx3sh7knk4Xt60JBULun3HLkfOV8PKAbC32EeNUuwXBl8MMQ+l\nzQ1KgDb4rr+zG3cLOo8fYK90FR4wVOG1VGL5nmnoh/nh+s/zWzMq4hFk34je+2gZ\nLEg1Nh1tBjuiaHS9xn+KflZWMieASfJlxERCURFlraCy2SfxMhQ4zCCYd75BMWaJ\nkJA/qN9Poa8GLGlW5avzqStqaW+uMkAUAYJiZjw95QZLfSMEtFc8+DSbEW4oVc4U\nfp49m5v/+c1aWsAqdEvqls0hE3R8YGo61TInE+yPBVczUAc0NyKylTTza5Bsmvle\nOtvtoDrZQfgbYCDjj95U\n=9zx+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a695aa59ff230b3c48d4a4f7902f756da3369c66\nparent ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784863032 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784863032 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): remove `get_rubric` source metadata (#5024)\n\n`get_rubric` no longer returns source provenance. Models only see active\ncriteria and grading status; goal-backed vs sticky lifecycle decisions\nstay in app state logic.\n\n---\n\nProvenance still exists internally for notice fingerprints and\nprecedence (`rubric_source` in projected goal state). This change\nremoves only the model-facing `source` field from\n`RubricSnapshot`/`get_rubric`, so the LLM is not asked to interpret\nsticky vs goal vs invocation labels.\n\nCriteria resolution is unchanged:\n- public `rubric` when present\n- else actionable goal rubric\n- else standalone sticky rubric\n\nCompletion, `update_goal` gating, and paused/complete goal withholding\nremain in app code.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T03:17:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f6caf524eea6ede25b1557d4d4588debcadd15f8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf"}]},{"sha":"ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZmYjdhYWJlMjVkM2Q1YWQ3YzVmY2UxMzlmM2JjM2UxNGUyNDVhZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T03:17:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T03:17:04Z"},"message":"fix(code): ignore LangSmith default US endpoint as custom target (#5022)\n\nWhen LangSmith profiles or env vars include the default US SaaS URL\n(`https://api.smith.langchain.com`), dcode no longer treats that URL as\na custom keyless upload target.\n\nPreviously, that default looked like a self-hosted/custom endpoint, so\nkeyless redaction setup could still run, client kwargs could forward a\nredundant `api_url`, and orphaned-tracing disable could skip even though\nno real custom ingest target was configured.\n\n---\n\nProfiles and configs often surface the stock US endpoint even when the\nuser never chose a custom target. The SDK treats that the same as\nleaving `api_url` unset, so upload-target checks and client construction\nnow ignore it whether it comes from env vars or the active profile.","tree":{"sha":"921ca19c4e75fc1076d625b71edadfaf276ab69d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/921ca19c4e75fc1076d625b71edadfaf276ab69d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYtkwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA88oQAKq4lvcuCiatHQvC6HZiWdes\n0Uc3+j6EkUdRJYosyS9VKumQOL7QL3in+MHYjKnBOQZWtNxmteOWWXpk42iKPJXG\npeujQNTFjVHV52XlQyfWWkx0hSExK1QIjR/aiACaseZtodMpjJo9cjfoIbKpnqtw\n48RvHyFIUmT3l/Wj8w7oWXvfxksZq2BoPgC0D6D+AVlgpKFxgdf1Qe9bmRJSPnOf\nL6wvh7BqFF+mpTSF3nPKQxZbmqXPHYnYZULa9LOOdo25g5udYNGzg1bOTgAWzduR\nNj3VbuHDQWyaCey0uOsCx9MeuMvyOdX8QHEQswEDb3hKOdfuYiQHHNdcu8ypuDMn\nxKz+RjUT4o2/onitzKnBKLm1sCiOtjBB9QZjw5g6cdFGnS8ZvEiEdjTgsUDG7ill\nCs2CNIFvEO7uJXOK7Npn3mRt/A/AEaPXWRuIebYBezBd8b1Uf4PKiHGcF/uuiSLw\n/uOi2Lv0VbzGCtlvPmeL9tG7sgxm6MReLaH8G1q0hU8Q6jjC5B1BrOWltA2S0sOl\ncfLsoeVMbiXKUS+eLhhnyyNZSx+JODBM1z9TBi6nbwvcKoaSEfJM7jbwCZRxMcXV\ntew1cYnhV/Hca4RTk941TqiD44KkCs9We25X+5XcwgEhz6pRp5VNdRMQd/d/sL6Z\nbItwC9ukctLx89wMfrvp\n=T5iu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 921ca19c4e75fc1076d625b71edadfaf276ab69d\nparent e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784863024 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784863024 -0400\n\nfix(code): ignore LangSmith default US endpoint as custom target (#5022)\n\nWhen LangSmith profiles or env vars include the default US SaaS URL\n(`https://api.smith.langchain.com`), dcode no longer treats that URL as\na custom keyless upload target.\n\nPreviously, that default looked like a self-hosted/custom endpoint, so\nkeyless redaction setup could still run, client kwargs could forward a\nredundant `api_url`, and orphaned-tracing disable could skip even though\nno real custom ingest target was configured.\n\n---\n\nProfiles and configs often surface the stock US endpoint even when the\nuser never chose a custom target. The SDK treats that the same as\nleaving `api_url` unset, so upload-target checks and client construction\nnow ignore it whether it comes from env vars or the active profile.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T03:17:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ffb7aabe25d3d5ad7c5fce139f3bc3e14e245adf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c"}]},{"sha":"e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU2M2NkZGY1YjE2ZWRhMGQ1NzI3ZjZkMzZkYWQ4NzQ2MGRkNmRiMGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T02:58:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T02:58:15Z"},"message":"style(code): tighten Auto mode first-run notice copy (#5021)\n\nTighten the one-time Auto mode enable notice: drop the “not a separate\nsecurity reviewer” aside, and say you’re asked to approve when review\nkeeps failing instead of referring to a “normal approval prompt.”\n\n---\n\nKeeps the same facts (routine gated actions, model review against the\nliteral request, not a sandbox, once per machine) with less jargon.","tree":{"sha":"43e8bbb8e16ddf6331d5dc2e5b051db64f022b41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/43e8bbb8e16ddf6331d5dc2e5b051db64f022b41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYtTHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6uYQAIZ6HDS8z+614MWVize19JGA\n2ISN+SYW9iekxOe7KUmosucmLdY05n8UxElTWcmFlw6fyZJI4Q/Ig3RUB8gwffAq\nVq0KFxoGCS+FNC4/UtRDbXjzEB6BvbOFH0FO4zEqtSZNA7ioH+6xabIzf5orPAAm\n+3zZjn4Znw/msQawHlSsK1IA4wxrpjjUkJbKlIS2cygju/5JIhE38FzlgWInB2In\n/8P//AfUZfjFpkJHyH2nHewsC/b/AEtKqO+6tdhASteU6uqeIy77zcUwJLz4HK2J\ndqQM7nXp9/MaML8TK13zUWHtanZMdmjp+efOh4e41bohGMfl06ywXz2rdnJyVrCr\nNh0c8AU0HOml6GWKTjcg/xvhqcVQHAvCj17pe81vJcwkfUYKQRJ0tg7iBO0mNpFn\n1DqyzZQtdYXcJ2qQmzOUmHc4bREYXplsAPQ7D+RGqPB1P0KAZt8EkGbCjjRJXvyb\nJAs0nVKIPaGnzuIyh4mO/eS7lOuv+zJEWocqf3/3ot90yh3z2FfWv9K34bzAgjJR\nsiPwUhZhWNNL2gtCVbzImYqIYM+x4Ts8sDnIaMxFSGkBBNHwVKWc1i/tGwcDc7pE\nGOuWWbE4w3lsLxuYZCl6Fuk69kfLe5fdi8MyAus4DcHHH4u1XLBIpN1J9gEh48h6\n9Wv4Q4fRKdsw8BInyzwV\n=xMcs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 43e8bbb8e16ddf6331d5dc2e5b051db64f022b41\nparent 4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784861895 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784861895 -0400\n\nstyle(code): tighten Auto mode first-run notice copy (#5021)\n\nTighten the one-time Auto mode enable notice: drop the “not a separate\nsecurity reviewer” aside, and say you’re asked to approve when review\nkeeps failing instead of referring to a “normal approval prompt.”\n\n---\n\nKeeps the same facts (routine gated actions, model review against the\nliteral request, not a sandbox, once per machine) with less jargon.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T02:58:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e63cddf5b16eda0d5727f6d36dad87460dd6db0c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda"}]},{"sha":"4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjY2I4NzMyNWYzZjk3ZTQxNjY4MzIzM2M5NDQwNWUzZWUxMDVjZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T02:56:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T02:56:38Z"},"message":"fix(code): put field descriptions on first-party tool schemas (#5019)\n\nFirst-party Deep Agents Code tools like `web_search` only put argument\ndocs in the tool description string. LangSmith and model tool schemas\ntherefore showed argument names/types without per-arg descriptions,\nunlike SDK filesystem tools and `js_eval`, which use\n`Field(description=...)`.\n\nPut model-facing parameter documentation on the JSON schema properties\nfor built-in dcode tools, and keep injected runtime parameters out of\nthat schema.\n\n---\n\n- Annotate model-facing tool parameters with `Field(description=...)`\n(or reuse existing FS `args_schema`s when wrapping grader tools).\n- Keep zero-arg / injected-only tools argument-free\n(`get_current_thread_id` via `get_config()`, goal state tools,\ncompaction).","tree":{"sha":"1ea3afdd73222ed9604b3d6ec8428db56661246b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1ea3afdd73222ed9604b3d6ec8428db56661246b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYtRmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANwgQAIfvnXQgTXWCVxGvv7iduWUB\nzDhUxE5nGLq3eBdbT5EKEVbg4DAm3a/FVmbtceFpkPckRhA/gB8QhypTALEUYjUb\n8RsqbZgvZmb8zCVsf3qnkMGTjKf1Ud0jbqXL5QE+SIrunPmRh5DmwIRhfo8ZEMz4\nkx2wF/5tAZviY9WkdzAk2F8wBHv5bEeOOnHpjsXTTw3b0JddBd8qmbadQ+qhN2Du\n8yJmx6AceJjq2fOlVTD3FV+cZbd2eLquRJgpJFbcdVGoAmOU+t5yqLdh8XIpN1NM\n84m2WhgjeGFED0BUAkQkM0Kjlw55zm9pQOnAfbhe+odpCxpEpLHQl0X7kD0sQiVX\nEGWROXi/MjPGOo8zzZpAmS2Er01NnDQotwxt5k4h216PocW1AAajqmW0xtTw+0z8\naaYzy8iN2SEu3QaRr/FHBbUUVPMkt3LtolKNXl66gRrPwpe11QsvPilV9p1RNKrT\nsauQxFU3PcpnFa070ea10UhKFtIlUb4iv2Vz8Cu5MiQM7X36r/6NSsF9MxnXzniM\n00CycFiuSlc+x61PIFoIw244npSV2AucOgUP2XIqSuxK2neOrLXwdf2IPfA0kTtJ\nqOMyc2qaR8IzQqNfmaFt3CRMiLzSJi2XCTkYpaBvlVDm892pAdpc+xhdnYEWe1ne\npEnDwgRock2/YQybrpKU\n=Akgd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1ea3afdd73222ed9604b3d6ec8428db56661246b\nparent c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784861798 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784861798 -0400\n\nfix(code): put field descriptions on first-party tool schemas (#5019)\n\nFirst-party Deep Agents Code tools like `web_search` only put argument\ndocs in the tool description string. LangSmith and model tool schemas\ntherefore showed argument names/types without per-arg descriptions,\nunlike SDK filesystem tools and `js_eval`, which use\n`Field(description=...)`.\n\nPut model-facing parameter documentation on the JSON schema properties\nfor built-in dcode tools, and keep injected runtime parameters out of\nthat schema.\n\n---\n\n- Annotate model-facing tool parameters with `Field(description=...)`\n(or reuse existing FS `args_schema`s when wrapping grader tools).\n- Keep zero-arg / injected-only tools argument-free\n(`get_current_thread_id` via `get_config()`, goal state tools,\ncompaction).","verified_at":"2026-07-24T02:56:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ccb87325f3f97e416683233c94405e3ee105cda/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59"}]},{"sha":"c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMyZGJkMTc2ZjA2ZmYxYTI5NjM3MTA3MTAxYWU2MTM0NGEwOWZjNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T02:47:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T02:47:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): show Auto enable notice modal only on first global enable (#5012)\n\nAuto mode now shows a short first-run modal explaining that a classifier\nreviews gated actions and that this is not a sandbox. After the first\ndismiss on a machine, later toggles and launches stay quiet; the status\nbar remains the ongoing mode indicator.\n\n---\n\nWhy: the previous toast was watery and repeated on every switch/startup,\nwhich trained people to ignore it. A one-time in-TUI modal is harder to\nmiss than a toast without becoming a YOLO-style pre-launch gate. Auto is\nalready on when the modal appears; Enter/Esc only continue.\n\n- Persist `auto_notice_shown` / `auto_notice_version` in the existing\ninstall-local `approval.json` (merge-write with YOLO ack fields)\n- Save the notice after dismiss (failed write fails open and may re-show\nlater)\n- All successful Auto entry paths (mount already-in-Auto, inline enable,\nShift+Tab toggle) go through one helper","tree":{"sha":"a4b553012c20cfe6a75feb7b7916a95a161797bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a4b553012c20cfe6a75feb7b7916a95a161797bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYtI0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfQcQAEeOVsWAVW2tndD3H1LNMh7W\nFeJJy0YVx8su6UAb90pKJZvX5Z/RxROp4M6Ehm67/o/poSX1Etkys8CIhefjkLDo\nTMwyrOjUF20liDWdzGmlBQ9PleL/SQI9qJkvQE4FIVyXOBIEOFKmvZGvINjCfq+2\nNGXthFe08tZ7u15+H6wWa1agyzZ0BuHnH8careT6Q7xSZF6lu7xNjlgmnjGjcLnS\ncsWpWAfi/0GN4uzNVcAdovwweS9BVYtAb4Evuus8P8wQ37XuNxnLjeV5ez99LgmA\noKSAFlDTIsBlA4yPhsYa1akhJ9OULEDc+pWEW54BJkwY+N3zn44hstne60HPGXML\nNM2shbGlG4gYMC3tQZSsS0zuZOS5mFwagMjoLYsokkOsPG2hJI6GyeUhSYeSNGPR\nWSPT0ftCdf/Qa2sNyR8spGuiHI8tN9T3fdbPAIdW0m4Wh875U3MSvomxLRGWmWno\nSpcGgRRL5PB/XqCCDHiz28vnWdeNOrgnh2e1fiJQlDgIvaVymGI4/keGg7oTfsWa\n4wV+NKg3USUvkxSmSf8vDg5TdO/xlLn6BuZxX8xD9mVDXjbDdt2oJjYnp3NdPwVh\nRCuBo26v5CYGu0i99GlhDC0u2O2UoPV0Q1lOCD9TUq0IRamz98T8cYFWZ/hMSYj0\nyW1jaRUL+0N75WQ0r1Wc\n=BxEe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a4b553012c20cfe6a75feb7b7916a95a161797bc\nparent 9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784861236 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784861236 -0400\n\nfix(code): show Auto enable notice modal only on first global enable (#5012)\n\nAuto mode now shows a short first-run modal explaining that a classifier\nreviews gated actions and that this is not a sandbox. After the first\ndismiss on a machine, later toggles and launches stay quiet; the status\nbar remains the ongoing mode indicator.\n\n---\n\nWhy: the previous toast was watery and repeated on every switch/startup,\nwhich trained people to ignore it. A one-time in-TUI modal is harder to\nmiss than a toast without becoming a YOLO-style pre-launch gate. Auto is\nalready on when the modal appears; Enter/Esc only continue.\n\n- Persist `auto_notice_shown` / `auto_notice_version` in the existing\ninstall-local `approval.json` (merge-write with YOLO ack fields)\n- Save the notice after dismiss (failed write fails open and may re-show\nlater)\n- All successful Auto entry paths (mount already-in-Auto, inline enable,\nShift+Tab toggle) go through one helper","verified_at":"2026-07-24T02:47:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c2dbd176f06ff1a29637107101ae61344a09fc59/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a"}]},{"sha":"9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk1MDAzMDZhMTdmOTBkYzJmMjc4OTdjMzY0YzI0Y2FmZmZiYzQ3NGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T02:43:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T02:43:26Z"},"message":"fix(code): dedupe Auto classifier-unavailable transcript spam (#5013)\n\nAuto no longer repeats identical \"classifier unavailable\" (and duplicate\npolicy-denial) notices once per tool call when a single tool-call batch\nis blocked; the transcript now shows one note per batch.\n\n---\n\nWhen the authorization classifier times out on a multi-tool batch, Auto\nstamps every call in the batch with the same `classifier_unavailable`\ndisposition and reason, then repeats an identical `Auto classifier\nunavailable: …` transcript note for each call. This makes a single\ntimeout flood the transcript with N duplicate lines.\n\nThe classifier-unavailable condition (and often a uniform policy denial)\nis a batch-level fact, not a per-call one, so the transcript event\nshould be emitted once per batch. This tracks the events already emitted\nwhile synthesizing denials and skips duplicates. Each tool call still\ngets its own error `ToolMessage`, since every call structurally requires\na response.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f6fd1ba4-b89e-1096-7a14-377f51d16e59)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"02ec15a61245c22757c78dabe3d7aacd115591f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/02ec15a61245c22757c78dabe3d7aacd115591f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYtFOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4OcQAEGs4sDXoOICPBsuJ0mLXG4N\nUf1NBk3gNyWQnaaoHjwW+sIDVyxBciatpKYoPm3xYwAQR/kcoT/tQFEeAHqrOpwf\njPfvaQwmKEXyCMDnbbLOF07xlUaUf46TtD5czRy4NMdpmLGPBtA8w2tojEGFe8WP\nIZYvzeYrky8cc8de8/MQZYf/hRNkQzgIvp5DjGiOkG7FuPxIAAQzFyEzzsY30K7Z\nEQIiF9UStifEBr3TMmnE/KIXaxyeZ0eF2XuWZJP81GXVpiLwuJ34EwQNxEsnXtFz\nRw0y6DLIwc22Ksrfd9PJyExBZNydolVsZ+SDyU8ClYcHfTtuKj6u7Ktsl7j5/KX9\n/3mF3iR7dQQL6SKKvZdOOa0JL3hFLV7tBXop3FRIZfmfdfnju3I4QjAjHXgjZ+rw\n3s+RArp67YBizsOF9Pw96dy+SsFTloaI8iemEPMtmsZ2fQPQAvTobP01n6SUzX13\nAvOyRRNxMCNS+lQGwtVdKX3z+Du/WpSpf2a/xyNHJfH9yyZ213hPNJcwVPB1cK15\nDwXkBXa46hosvw1Pc3g8CokeUOh8Q84dD+Ai76YcOtlMivbXIgdRIfIRO/vA8wdT\n6FgYShvbYOJkfqEqDD5CUNQ2z9tyNm0mm0ieey1Edq2Y8P1bsbwmBi9HnsWzdDSW\n9EAyopVSZei7G0dY0MvI\n=y0Wb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 02ec15a61245c22757c78dabe3d7aacd115591f6\nparent 728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784861006 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784861006 -0400\n\nfix(code): dedupe Auto classifier-unavailable transcript spam (#5013)\n\nAuto no longer repeats identical \"classifier unavailable\" (and duplicate\npolicy-denial) notices once per tool call when a single tool-call batch\nis blocked; the transcript now shows one note per batch.\n\n---\n\nWhen the authorization classifier times out on a multi-tool batch, Auto\nstamps every call in the batch with the same `classifier_unavailable`\ndisposition and reason, then repeats an identical `Auto classifier\nunavailable: …` transcript note for each call. This makes a single\ntimeout flood the transcript with N duplicate lines.\n\nThe classifier-unavailable condition (and often a uniform policy denial)\nis a batch-level fact, not a per-call one, so the transcript event\nshould be emitted once per batch. This tracks the events already emitted\nwhile synthesizing denials and skips duplicates. Each tool call still\ngets its own error `ToolMessage`, since every call structurally requires\na response.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f6fd1ba4-b89e-1096-7a14-377f51d16e59)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T02:43:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9500306a17f90dc2f27897c364c24cafffbc474a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7"}]},{"sha":"728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcyOGRiZTdkZjYyYWQ5OTYwZjIxY2FiZDZlNmMzN2U4ZDlhNjZkYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T02:27:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T02:27:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): authorize Auto actions from active goal/rubric directives (#5017)\n\nIn Auto mode, active `/goal` and `/rubric` content now counts as\nauthorization for ordinary work that those outcomes imply.\n\nPreviously the Auto classifier only trusted chat text and validated\n`ask_user` answers. Setting a quality gate like “make sure tests pass\nand no new warnings,” then saying `hi`, still looked unauthorized, so\nshell/file work needed for that gate was denied as scope escalation.\nActive goals behaved the same way once later turns were just\ncontinuations or greetings.\n\nAuto mode now treats the user’s accepted goal objective and criteria,\nplus an independent sticky or one-shot rubric, as the stated coding\noutcome—even when the latest chat message does not restate them. Paused\nor completed goals, agent status notes, and unaccepted goal proposals\nstill grant nothing. High-risk actions continue to need explicit,\nunambiguous authorization.\n\n---\n\nThis closes a gap between goal/rubric slash commands and Auto\nauthorization: those controls define what the session is trying to\nachieve, so the classifier should not ignore them when the latest prompt\nis only a greeting or continuation.","tree":{"sha":"da1716ed17b80b05bb9eb6e407f600d4f9cd4c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/da1716ed17b80b05bb9eb6e407f600d4f9cd4c66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYs2fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW6IQABrMJXf3+XuwpgxG7IfhmbXf\ncXS5IxSo+9Bb0MB7WbtwhoXUzwjNcarH+mc1gGo8vueYH6EexG+kgvmPvyp4EPRl\nyDiXGf5Q/5vNL0uWfmSTThgSxQdmFOsObc90m67jgWjTb8SD5+GEAiMrSm6pvfP5\n/0txwPwLcSadwvjt6iNrgLhhdMylTIP7XCd/UhKJXfMXm9COHJsSaLq8j4IZaWKq\niyvOUy4r0eN1e1RIEsGjIY3xNnKz1XF946xsE1nHmfzPvfYKbm6RcgaCTrrvwgwH\njDejs15ffRMLx7wDWk2S6AXQKmBALJ1sUsIsuSTJIDyns5mzgBVxd5Wb9GQ0W8du\nB1bALz3a/bqkl0ubMANfIRdEHTwMalWwrToDaJiuR9JgxpkO7pi1WxEFDDd2xDFe\nH4/iBcrpjKN3aIN1UPme8LPdLTVgPimva76niDdZAKMllhcQdwyN3ALnwj3iob0j\nbjcthUOS3dhZKB0pb7WQZCcJLEwTq95Aza2GwSHM1yF6EsiG2Lz6CM5Z0c7Xz40F\nzhJ2a3Nt94OZvsHWh63HRgbRPr2k0pExsrLq21bVPUfYfpjRIBaTE2nx8GQEalA5\nbE0+GwHQEAXj5Ju2Hl0bWySUOj9TAV36aHpeUXfKkrahPBRCBc+HQfD6Ff17nlKt\nSfVLdF/NqKeZDOjLj/gl\n=lTHJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree da1716ed17b80b05bb9eb6e407f600d4f9cd4c66\nparent 1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784860063 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784860063 -0400\n\nfix(code): authorize Auto actions from active goal/rubric directives (#5017)\n\nIn Auto mode, active `/goal` and `/rubric` content now counts as\nauthorization for ordinary work that those outcomes imply.\n\nPreviously the Auto classifier only trusted chat text and validated\n`ask_user` answers. Setting a quality gate like “make sure tests pass\nand no new warnings,” then saying `hi`, still looked unauthorized, so\nshell/file work needed for that gate was denied as scope escalation.\nActive goals behaved the same way once later turns were just\ncontinuations or greetings.\n\nAuto mode now treats the user’s accepted goal objective and criteria,\nplus an independent sticky or one-shot rubric, as the stated coding\noutcome—even when the latest chat message does not restate them. Paused\nor completed goals, agent status notes, and unaccepted goal proposals\nstill grant nothing. High-risk actions continue to need explicit,\nunambiguous authorization.\n\n---\n\nThis closes a gap between goal/rubric slash commands and Auto\nauthorization: those controls define what the session is trying to\nachieve, so the classifier should not ignore them when the latest prompt\nis only a greeting or continuation.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T02:27:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/728dbe7df62ad9960f21cabd6e6c37e8d9a66da7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa"}]},{"sha":"1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFhM2Y0NmI4NTg2MTc3OWVkNDRlODgwY2M3OTIxY2RkNmYyOGZkZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T02:21:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T02:21:27Z"},"message":"fix(code): improve `/rubric` help and empty-state messaging (#5015)\n\nMake `/rubric` easier to learn from inside the TUI: bare subcommands now\nteach with short examples, empty `show`/`clear` stop sounding like\nsuccess, and current-state text drops internal \"sticky\" jargon in favor\nof plain labels plus a `/rubric show` tip.\n\n---\n\nBare `/rubric set|next|file` previously printed only a one-line usage\nstring, so users often didn’t see the durability difference or a\nconcrete syntax sample. `/rubric show` with no criteria simply said “No\nrubric set,” and `/rubric clear` reported cleared even when nothing was\nactive. Bare `/rubric` also referred to a “Sticky rubric,” assuming\nusers already knew the internal sticky vs next distinction.\n\nThis keeps grading behavior the same and focuses the help copy on:\n\n- lasting criteria vs next-turn only\n- when grading happens\n- how to inspect or clear what’s set","tree":{"sha":"af9eb9773a8b5125f17ae820170ade1ad9ff4fbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/af9eb9773a8b5125f17ae820170ade1ad9ff4fbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYswnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+20QAH+6dGpe6dEQL0dzz804Xc65\nugVzyheMiEHGRHu7wzmixGefewq4Mtep8RWQQ/qkvCFdWeZ9Yvb3SNjmpnK5Q0QZ\neF3KI07N6PvmMvlHJrV4DdBUmF/7V6gTF+isCNusMmkVkSoaKR7EMnyHm1xx6zwH\n/bj0qqwSN/tAVzwlfewoRhzb/MwJLk9MglKmcSLQ619pelI0+cztgaHFFME7pmmy\n+mLkMGiDqZ6sdBlhq4OyFvwmBRSo6hPBJoIVuAIPeRDcBPFmS96So7f5gUQgcNxn\nAPjACsDsyTPJcLICMEE4VqL94ezmVINM7UnBl/+MIAP/c4OD0gGs+Rd2ZTm81g4Y\nkUhzDYHVRsMfFcUkxd/T6bTrJRQxApLauW3/rrzF6vnl5WHiKfWWXePVcCaX65fy\nKM39GjvtJtniPVFBTk/n6l664nbiRWx34nNDsIjeJmg3gHhU7SCPj3vQZnj56C2G\n0CL5Kk59zHY5WbfvRp/tLIvb+xH2VCB6KUONaCEuLyIAZIr03be8Ni+L1Jp/eCl0\nFLAWXLc+LxGMCqIqbwcyDzMQzcqKhGrwt91PBzJwhNggP6CzqapXqdpLwxb66tt3\nJEBI6zfhLAzlFqOoQ4iPAedtkmeLIIlFL/RCXnVEY+KNvf79r80G8qST7s2rCMdI\nIwMZqHAfyidL2NppuwpI\n=4l7G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree af9eb9773a8b5125f17ae820170ade1ad9ff4fbe\nparent 6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784859687 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784859687 -0400\n\nfix(code): improve `/rubric` help and empty-state messaging (#5015)\n\nMake `/rubric` easier to learn from inside the TUI: bare subcommands now\nteach with short examples, empty `show`/`clear` stop sounding like\nsuccess, and current-state text drops internal \"sticky\" jargon in favor\nof plain labels plus a `/rubric show` tip.\n\n---\n\nBare `/rubric set|next|file` previously printed only a one-line usage\nstring, so users often didn’t see the durability difference or a\nconcrete syntax sample. `/rubric show` with no criteria simply said “No\nrubric set,” and `/rubric clear` reported cleared even when nothing was\nactive. Bare `/rubric` also referred to a “Sticky rubric,” assuming\nusers already knew the internal sticky vs next distinction.\n\nThis keeps grading behavior the same and focuses the help copy on:\n\n- lasting criteria vs next-turn only\n- when grading happens\n- how to inspect or clear what’s set","verified_at":"2026-07-24T02:21:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1a3f46b85861779ed44e880cc7921cdd6f28fdfa/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113"}]},{"sha":"6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZkNjYzMmZhMzk4MjJmMWI3NzRmY2FiZDYxZWQzNzFhOTA0MjcxMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T01:39:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T01:39:33Z"},"message":"fix(code): inject OpenAI `prompt_cache_key` for any OpenAI-provider endpoint (#4995)\n\n`dcode` now attaches the per-thread `prompt_cache_key` to every model\nwhose provider resolves to `openai`, regardless of base URL, so reliable\nprompt-cache prefix routing also applies through the LangSmith gateway\nand other OpenAI-compatible endpoints — not just `api.openai.com`. A\ndefault-on `models.openai_prompt_cache_key` opt-out is added for\nendpoints that reject unknown request fields.\n\n---\n\nPreviously `ConfigurableModelMiddleware` only injected\n`prompt_cache_key` when the resolved `ChatOpenAI` base URL was\n`api.openai.com` (or an official regional subdomain). Any\nOpenAI-compatible proxy — including the managed LangSmith gateway\n(`gateway.smith.langchain.com/openai/v1`) that dcode is provisioned to\nuse — was classified as a custom endpoint and silently dropped the key,\nso consecutive turns over a stable ~58-59K-token prefix missed prompt\ncaching and were billed at full input price (observed ~7x per-turn cost\nspikes).\n\n`prompt_cache_key` is an optional, additive OpenAI request field: it\nsharpens prefix-cache routing on model families that support it and is\notherwise inert. Rather than maintaining a hostname allowlist,\n`_is_openai_model` now treats any model reporting `ls_provider ==\n\"openai\"` as eligible and attempts the key unconditionally. Endpoints\nthat reject unknown fields can opt out via the new\n`models.openai_prompt_cache_key` config option\n(`[models].openai_prompt_cache_key` in `config.toml`, or\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OPENAI_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY`, default on). A user-supplied\nkey (on the model or per-invocation) is still preserved, and the\nFireworks session-affinity path is unchanged.\n\nVerified end to end that a model created with the gateway base URL now\nserializes `prompt_cache_key` in the Responses payload, and that the\nopt-out suppresses it.\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/09eb0978-379d-0b80-9beb-73aa2ef6ab79)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebc38cc955398f3df0c0c5adcfa3d716c3a60984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ebc38cc955398f3df0c0c5adcfa3d716c3a60984"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYsJVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMc0QAD6ZZGKSHlYtLWsbTivspsgN\nnG6oOYFBPi5zYYKK7adwEuJv/rRfUgFUeW+xVEF0ScILfp34hx9C0MQK9sytZHmI\nqCUA6m7gVKKnsFymBF5yiEfPENf5+I9KCyd9d7flv9OoY3UqNHFEFokJnTx1lFd2\nDJSu+4W6HYsi383VoMNoBCsrR3aDmIXC/Wsejx77yi9a3VMqMCVAylgXqCezJJyD\n0HGiHvtELr7HbvneD6UB3p/6HzGQGTG8h/npl/S5fGbfGouQMMXixIWTPBiH2tjz\n3kYH3GuiJnCngjSbvDckOhcZI1g/i3nGYZ18SAi7d0NvHOAtDmRaqTFZfYVaYhUN\noA1eHjBES/xMIsqyq4PKkoSroatcMsHqGMRROBPVxjUaxS3hrSt1UygepxKH67MA\nL5ijvtQRuBjFC8NWKZS/WfPnTBY4X5s6wD1c93JHwSDJqIlGgIcpd1aI2HChVQCp\niNiRJJ7BBsj9S3/UUCN74FzLBFDeNuRNbFncgsMIW+dI87cC3ySgVFh9mP+YfAE8\n3p4Hl9loCOFFtYcUEw+ggM74ETuRuH/VoMWWlQPa6r5wAHLrxrFFHxx43H98PsHm\n1ZkTIbXcz3ecyVWmQAFomZTF377RHBYDjfzZu9KXqhUi70Au8HzQ890rIXzV4zQ3\nK8AKfhhsdI7xXv203Rgx\n=ZEyx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ebc38cc955398f3df0c0c5adcfa3d716c3a60984\nparent bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784857173 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784857173 -0400\n\nfix(code): inject OpenAI `prompt_cache_key` for any OpenAI-provider endpoint (#4995)\n\n`dcode` now attaches the per-thread `prompt_cache_key` to every model\nwhose provider resolves to `openai`, regardless of base URL, so reliable\nprompt-cache prefix routing also applies through the LangSmith gateway\nand other OpenAI-compatible endpoints — not just `api.openai.com`. A\ndefault-on `models.openai_prompt_cache_key` opt-out is added for\nendpoints that reject unknown request fields.\n\n---\n\nPreviously `ConfigurableModelMiddleware` only injected\n`prompt_cache_key` when the resolved `ChatOpenAI` base URL was\n`api.openai.com` (or an official regional subdomain). Any\nOpenAI-compatible proxy — including the managed LangSmith gateway\n(`gateway.smith.langchain.com/openai/v1`) that dcode is provisioned to\nuse — was classified as a custom endpoint and silently dropped the key,\nso consecutive turns over a stable ~58-59K-token prefix missed prompt\ncaching and were billed at full input price (observed ~7x per-turn cost\nspikes).\n\n`prompt_cache_key` is an optional, additive OpenAI request field: it\nsharpens prefix-cache routing on model families that support it and is\notherwise inert. Rather than maintaining a hostname allowlist,\n`_is_openai_model` now treats any model reporting `ls_provider ==\n\"openai\"` as eligible and attempts the key unconditionally. Endpoints\nthat reject unknown fields can opt out via the new\n`models.openai_prompt_cache_key` config option\n(`[models].openai_prompt_cache_key` in `config.toml`, or\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OPENAI_PROMPT_CACHE_KEY`, default on). A user-supplied\nkey (on the model or per-invocation) is still preserved, and the\nFireworks session-affinity path is unchanged.\n\nVerified end to end that a model created with the gateway base URL now\nserializes `prompt_cache_key` in the Responses payload, and that the\nopt-out suppresses it.\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/09eb0978-379d-0b80-9beb-73aa2ef6ab79)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T01:39:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6d6632fa39822f1b774fcabd61ed371a90427113/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407"}]},{"sha":"bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJkMDNlOGExY2E0YjM4ODgzZTExMTQ4ZDU2MTRhNDQ0Y2RlZmE0MDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T01:38:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T01:38:19Z"},"message":"fix(code): log underlying Auto classifier failures (#5011)\n\nWhen Auto mode's authorization classifier can't run, application logs\nnow include the redacted exception detail and traceback so you can see\nwhy the classifier was unavailable.\n\nPreviously the unavailable path only logged that a classifier failure\noccurred. The agent/UI reason stays type-only.\n\n---\n\nThe unavailable logger path now includes a sanitized `Type: message`\ndetail and attaches the exception via `exc_info=True`. Secrets still go\nthrough `sanitize_auto_reason` before logging.","tree":{"sha":"f68b3b317e9760dcc8cc97382eece84c0ef2b4ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f68b3b317e9760dcc8cc97382eece84c0ef2b4ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYsILCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmCEQAJJovbWVshJdrmW0RzK6gqC4\nTNkTv0CKlJj9+yKoGElhzW7zVZnkH4pGt9NppVrG4p/x7cKVi8qmE2UgFGF3tTWD\nIBKOSezW7RHGz0Hz6oGocHL8drePnAyi2LBX1E4PBUY22bJGQDn7Qu3WhCbW2jSA\n9FKCR6JNOEH33dDQdjuOY4iu4wmR5iF3sbEIUr3cKwI834iC9QYoeTB+0fkE/SSD\nR4VauqghfUbI0UF8Ozsd8cSExBVteyaBE3dFazb6vPSdX9TuDlUu1LVFtChXJU1z\nnGaaUXmhXRIcDYUYCvaXibAVatLZap8nmsbRnKZIphZOTOkOtoL/QlT4bOZrJTQx\npExTV8pIURAnEjg8t1KOlP5hHvi7bF4s4sO5HAr1RIvsVHrhOIsv1742SIdTVfgA\nKL7BUCGbRRQpQ+6tDesx59u8aHiFUGmggLA8/IW5GbTKbSNN6tWbbWh1NOeiOTs4\nOUoXHMzGfmbXxRchDO7c6cByBZM/qND+0vyLtFJ6bjcKHqdoVEiLhSlcs/jjZYpj\nvZtW2XFOSIFOJ1e3+/hj71URksYlF5A2g7/mJQQ5i6IPE+6XuBlZlT/MWxpmhMAs\nwzNo0RkZBKoNt/9YZeED5FGsreft6wed9543uYYAznVgD/EPDPjSgug/w92PODwA\nRK1sUdsXdSchgAXf9iCv\n=VVsy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f68b3b317e9760dcc8cc97382eece84c0ef2b4ca\nparent 761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784857099 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784857099 -0400\n\nfix(code): log underlying Auto classifier failures (#5011)\n\nWhen Auto mode's authorization classifier can't run, application logs\nnow include the redacted exception detail and traceback so you can see\nwhy the classifier was unavailable.\n\nPreviously the unavailable path only logged that a classifier failure\noccurred. The agent/UI reason stays type-only.\n\n---\n\nThe unavailable logger path now includes a sanitized `Type: message`\ndetail and attaches the exception via `exc_info=True`. Secrets still go\nthrough `sanitize_auto_reason` before logging.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T01:38:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd03e8a1ca4b38883e11148d5614a444cdefa407/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe"}]},{"sha":"761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc2MWY1ZjA4ODJkZWUxODZmMjcwMGYzYzkwMzgyOWE1NTQyNjI2ZmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T01:25:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T01:25:23Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): trim built-in tool descriptions (#5009)\n\n## What\n\nShortens the LLM-facing description strings for the `task` tool and the\nfilesystem tools (`read_file`, `grep`, `edit_file`, `glob`, `execute`):\ndrops worked examples and step-by-step tutorials, keeps the one-line\npurpose and the load-bearing constraints (grep is literal-not-regex,\nread-before-edit, absolute paths, multimodal content blocks,\noffloaded-result paths). No behavior change — string literals only.\n\n## Token impact\n\n**Offline (`o200k_base`, default-agent tool schemas) — isolates the\ndescription trims:**\n\n| tool | before | after | Δ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| task | 1,664 | 389 | −77% |\n| read_file | 728 | 494 | −32% |\n| grep | 688 | 555 | −19% |\n| edit_file | 273 | 257 | −6% |\n| glob | 217 | 172 | −21% |\n| write_file | 177 | 177 | — |\n| delete | 146 | 146 | — |\n| ls | 111 | 111 | — |\n| **total** | **4,005** | **2,302** | **−43%** |\n\n(`execute` is also trimmed; it only binds with a sandbox backend so it\nisn't in the default set above. `write_file`/`delete`/`ls` were already\nlean — one-line purpose plus short usage notes, no example/tutorial\nprose to cut.)\n\n**Online (real `usage_metadata`, gpt-5.5, default-agent \"hello\" turn):**\n\n| | input tokens |\n| --- | ---: |\n| deepagents 0.6.12 | 5,395 |\n| this branch | 1,895 |\n\nThe 0.6.12→branch figure (−65%) reflects the full default-agent\nfootprint change since the last release — the lean base prompt and\n`write_todos` opt-in (both already on `main`) **plus** these description\ntrims. The offline table above isolates the trims' own contribution.\n\n## Eval — no quality regression\n\n### Pytest evals (gpt-5.6-luna, excluding memory)\n\n[Run\n30029746997](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30029746997)\n(this branch, trimmed) vs [run\n29603036224](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/29603036224)\n(pre-trim `main` baseline):\n\ncorrectness **0.81 = 0.81**, solve_rate **0.635 ≈ 0.634**. Per-category\nscores are identical except `file_operations` (0.90 vs 0.95) — a ~1-test\nmove within noise (the runs have different test counts, 145 vs 138).\n\n| category | branch | baseline |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| conversation | 0.36 | 0.36 |\n| file_operations | 0.90 | 0.95 |\n| langchain/middleware | 0.86 | 0.86 |\n| retrieval | 1.00 | 1.00 |\n| summarization | 0.40 | 0.40 |\n| tool_use | 0.90 | 0.90 |\n| unit_test | 0.89 | 0.89 |\n\n### Unified (gpt-5.6-luna, lite, bare)\n\nTrimmed agent vs the canonical `UNIFIED_SCORECARD.md` baseline,\n**avg@k** (measured with the Harbor `virtual_mode` fix applied so the\nharness scores correctly):\n\n| category | trimmed | canonical |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| autonomous | 0.173 | 0.156 |\n| conversation | 0.209 | 0.182 |\n| context | 0.930 | 0.900 |\n| **macro** | **0.437** | **0.413** |\n| **micro** | **0.408** | **0.371** |\n\nTrimmed matches or slightly exceeds canonical on every category\n(rollouts=10).\n\n## Testing\n\n`deepagents` unit suite green (2,324 passed); smoke-test tool-schema\nsnapshots regenerated.","tree":{"sha":"d6c53e4f6ef989d853aab4d7c7434d45f561f543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d6c53e4f6ef989d853aab4d7c7434d45f561f543"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYr8DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlA