t\nisn't in the default set above. `write_file`/`delete`/`ls` were already\nlean — one-line purpose plus short usage notes, no example/tutorial\nprose to cut.)\n\n**Online (real `usage_metadata`, gpt-5.5, default-agent \"hello\" turn):**\n\n| | input tokens |\n| --- | ---: |\n| deepagents 0.6.12 | 5,395 |\n| this branch | 1,895 |\n\nThe 0.6.12→branch figure (−65%) reflects the full default-agent\nfootprint change since the last release — the lean base prompt and\n`write_todos` opt-in (both already on `main`) **plus** these description\ntrims. The offline table above isolates the trims' own contribution.\n\n## Eval — no quality regression\n\n### Pytest evals (gpt-5.6-luna, excluding memory)\n\n[Run\n30029746997](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30029746997)\n(this branch, trimmed) vs [run\n29603036224](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/29603036224)\n(pre-trim `main` baseline):\n\ncorrectness **0.81 = 0.81**, solve_rate **0.635 ≈ 0.634**. Per-category\nscores are identical except `file_operations` (0.90 vs 0.95) — a ~1-test\nmove within noise (the runs have different test counts, 145 vs 138).\n\n| category | branch | baseline |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| conversation | 0.36 | 0.36 |\n| file_operations | 0.90 | 0.95 |\n| langchain/middleware | 0.86 | 0.86 |\n| retrieval | 1.00 | 1.00 |\n| summarization | 0.40 | 0.40 |\n| tool_use | 0.90 | 0.90 |\n| unit_test | 0.89 | 0.89 |\n\n### Unified (gpt-5.6-luna, lite, bare)\n\nTrimmed agent vs the canonical `UNIFIED_SCORECARD.md` baseline,\n**avg@k** (measured with the Harbor `virtual_mode` fix applied so the\nharness scores correctly):\n\n| category | trimmed | canonical |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| autonomous | 0.173 | 0.156 |\n| conversation | 0.209 | 0.182 |\n| context | 0.930 | 0.900 |\n| **macro** | **0.437** | **0.413** |\n| **micro** | **0.408** | **0.371** |\n\nTrimmed matches or slightly exceeds canonical on every category\n(rollouts=10).\n\n## Testing\n\n`deepagents` unit suite green (2,324 passed); smoke-test tool-schema\nsnapshots regenerated.","verified_at":"2026-07-24T01:25:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/761f5f0882dee186f2700f3c903829a5542626fe/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c"}]},{"sha":"1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE3MDlkYmY5YjI3NzY2YWFjY2UxYTVhOWMxNzM5NmIzNjU0ZjAyNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexander Olsen","email":"aolsenjazz@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-24T01:21:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T01:21:29Z"},"message":"fix(code): make Auto mode generally available (#4957)\n\nAuto approval mode is now available in the local interactive TUI without\nsetting `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL`; sandbox and headless sessions\nstill fall back to Manual.\n\n---\n\nThis removes the experimental environment gate across CLI startup, app\neligibility, server graph construction, and agent middleware while\npreserving the local-only safety constraints. Verified with focused unit\ntests plus package lint, type, formatting, and import checks.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e0c9c9a9-85ca-7dc8-d759-d89431bc5276)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"afbffb56fd9337205e74c4db8c8d7aa23cdaca6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/afbffb56fd9337205e74c4db8c8d7aa23cdaca6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYr4ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAok0QAH3DnApXc/NMaQYwSUpuTzXb\ntXVpzPoNfVCku71wQA9oKvpnJdv3KLeVq1DJ9+4/Wbm2iwFCs05xDRM+aUwHQFz2\nFBFk9UGH4rTpLvLNYn4M+HXVedfTyMrPGdU69S5kquOkdFL4WgPviuSGD2ehxR2T\nQ413fmChT3WgkMfePcOGizjNELHJqv7XYOgqkqRV7N2urjvUXs684WyLPJVMG9hq\nEkn4uANZgEBPQz87m19lq+WsygDJqqXRShAwgjWPKVJYTtRLTTyAvEO6wO9JrYtV\n6tSsHF6GEyGSRKsUMJSBgCBo07IR6qgUhr8DcG9VP+pUTcNJgxxMlDnXZWgIV+Pi\nejbMyCzwIdhay8axU4dPQbGhcWWmgZmtsfteXUT+nT9emHOLImC0r57Qi6qhs6qR\nC0VG157/z1hcTH474Ms7Yy7ToSkXI8+3eTcmhFOl1WIT2fxuPQIGRwXWDMOrf97L\nIHw0OwRKD57o4M4WI7f7JlUEzDZq5de7/bq0J/WSk4Fd4ethddHiHDghW3juwRJK\nG7KY2L1Dhwk36WHf1QlUUatMrxTtYw9uqyuKaRjJdLg84mDSNH/zgxYGxvO48m90\nxneM8f7LK4xTwMWwrUm3nw9Kybx1ykY6v/pvZW/JgeRFCJj4o9MW14U50HxqXvUR\nws5zpCUoLT/l3hZ2/bpl\n=dHy9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree afbffb56fd9337205e74c4db8c8d7aa23cdaca6d\nparent 313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97\nauthor Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com> 1784856089 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784856089 -0400\n\nfix(code): make Auto mode generally available (#4957)\n\nAuto approval mode is now available in the local interactive TUI without\nsetting `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL`; sandbox and headless sessions\nstill fall back to Manual.\n\n---\n\nThis removes the experimental environment gate across CLI startup, app\neligibility, server graph construction, and agent middleware while\npreserving the local-only safety constraints. Verified with focused unit\ntests plus package lint, type, formatting, and import checks.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e0c9c9a9-85ca-7dc8-d759-d89431bc5276)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T01:21:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1709dbf9b27766aacce1a5a9c17396b3654f026c/comments","author":{"login":"aolsenjazz","id":13665641,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjY1NjQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13665641?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz","html_url":"https://github.com/aolsenjazz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97"}]},{"sha":"313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMxM2Y5NTIwY2VmMjhjMTA1YWE1M2VhYzY0NTE3NmQ0MjJlYzRhOTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T00:44:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T00:44:28Z"},"message":"fix(code): flag empty env override shadowing LangSmith key in `/trace` (#4996)\n\n`/trace` now gives an honest, targeted notice when tracing is off\nbecause a present-but-empty `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY` (or\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`) is shadowing a LangSmith key,\ninstead of sending you to `/auth` as if nothing were configured.\n\n---\n\n### Background\n\nPer `resolve_env_var`'s precedence, a present-but-empty prefixed\noverride deliberately shadows the canonical env key, and — because\n`apply_stored_service_credentials` skips the `/auth` bridge onto\n`LANGSMITH_API_KEY` when the prefixed var is present — a `/auth`-stored\nkey too. That suppression is intentional and unchanged; the only problem\nwas surfacing: `get_langsmith_project_name` returns `None` in this state\nand `/trace` collapsed it to the generic \"not configured, run `/auth`\"\nhint even though a key is available.\n\n### What this adds\n\n`langsmith_key_shadowed_by_empty_override` returns a\n`LangsmithShadowResult` that distinguishes three states, and `/trace`\nrenders each differently:\n\n- **A key is shadowed** → names the offending variable and how to fix\nit. The notice only fires for an override that gates the *effective*\nkey: if a key already resolves under the normal\n`LANGSMITH_API_KEY`-before-`LANGCHAIN_API_KEY` precedence, no override\nis to blame (tracing is off for another reason, e.g. a missing flag) and\nthe generic hint stands. The wording no longer promises tracing will\nswitch on — it points at the flag too — and no longer calls an\nenv-supplied key a \"stored\" key.\n- **The credential store is unreadable** (corrupt file) → a\ncorruption-specific hint rather than the generic one, and the underlying\nerror is logged.\n- **Neither** → the original \"run `/auth`\" message, unchanged.\n\nThe shadow check is a best-effort diagnostic, so its call in\n`_handle_trace_command` is now guarded (command echo first, `try/except`\nfallback) — it can never crash `/trace`.\n\nThe env-var precedence semantics are untouched; this is scoped to\nsurfacing.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d32e941a-8cf2-d7a9-c1f7-3e8d1ff111cd)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e30835ac7fa44ba0c8d9719b1841d892d4ad5a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e30835ac7fa44ba0c8d9719b1841d892d4ad5a07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYrVsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7VYQACfmorUQZ1EimUXhqpknDrdA\nYGVArLJTzHHLqrHu/EiGHTkeC6zoYM6BuUgwaTFtQbIu0tV9ipBgHsXFBN3YW5z1\n1/I0rA42ytNhfLbOHO+tivEJRA8bATHhy1tVfA2ZkSSTD0aiGhJst8Q580iJhEQy\nhlE79BO6/mAPhwyVrAhA60GUffrkpb/fmQJ3QuJTy472weBYTkXUCHo5EhQZVtCQ\neMPH7YwRk2h+3+w1NWNHE6aI7ipbez2o0PfilCWNAin3XabJUBpKTBLgtRJ4ADqB\nCdE2ILc8HlRFPHi5oC4mBqRbPxBfxeLeBGYRoT0Qr3BMYUWTnY1HRbnUxn87S2iq\nbuvaiZynDprvimphdOztlKIn5frnYr/pJO35B2SkI/MwV6soWgJk47xdoEvuNk1N\nbvQuJGyvVlo4JbwNWLws4vxR9e4doTds9tIiVZ+cJHbMUs/i9JZyF35n6jflxZYB\n+m8tjWF1mR59qmj6a/JfFVLcgapri6OojWdybENutn1vdJEkdyvt+kQzStsiyacK\nqzOF3IuaF2+Gcc0eztK/YQwwipCHQzDvs5EwwMLy9v3vksgHCdHmbcVtK/fiTQla\nEx4DkHcQTOEMUAhI1ghyzx2a8YMkzX5Ynf9FQXLYNx0RUEn1sFZdgRO3ZcrMcb74\n+eZ8mutoRrloGqjQxUGk\n=KhHe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e30835ac7fa44ba0c8d9719b1841d892d4ad5a07\nparent 976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784853868 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784853868 -0400\n\nfix(code): flag empty env override shadowing LangSmith key in `/trace` (#4996)\n\n`/trace` now gives an honest, targeted notice when tracing is off\nbecause a present-but-empty `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY` (or\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`) is shadowing a LangSmith key,\ninstead of sending you to `/auth` as if nothing were configured.\n\n---\n\n### Background\n\nPer `resolve_env_var`'s precedence, a present-but-empty prefixed\noverride deliberately shadows the canonical env key, and — because\n`apply_stored_service_credentials` skips the `/auth` bridge onto\n`LANGSMITH_API_KEY` when the prefixed var is present — a `/auth`-stored\nkey too. That suppression is intentional and unchanged; the only problem\nwas surfacing: `get_langsmith_project_name` returns `None` in this state\nand `/trace` collapsed it to the generic \"not configured, run `/auth`\"\nhint even though a key is available.\n\n### What this adds\n\n`langsmith_key_shadowed_by_empty_override` returns a\n`LangsmithShadowResult` that distinguishes three states, and `/trace`\nrenders each differently:\n\n- **A key is shadowed** → names the offending variable and how to fix\nit. The notice only fires for an override that gates the *effective*\nkey: if a key already resolves under the normal\n`LANGSMITH_API_KEY`-before-`LANGCHAIN_API_KEY` precedence, no override\nis to blame (tracing is off for another reason, e.g. a missing flag) and\nthe generic hint stands. The wording no longer promises tracing will\nswitch on — it points at the flag too — and no longer calls an\nenv-supplied key a \"stored\" key.\n- **The credential store is unreadable** (corrupt file) → a\ncorruption-specific hint rather than the generic one, and the underlying\nerror is logged.\n- **Neither** → the original \"run `/auth`\" message, unchanged.\n\nThe shadow check is a best-effort diagnostic, so its call in\n`_handle_trace_command` is now guarded (command echo first, `try/except`\nfallback) — it can never crash `/trace`.\n\nThe env-var precedence semantics are untouched; this is scoped to\nsurfacing.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d32e941a-8cf2-d7a9-c1f7-3e8d1ff111cd)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T00:44:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/313f9520cef28c105aa53eac645176d422ec4a97/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc"}]},{"sha":"976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk3NmM1NGIyZTEzOTIyODIwNDRkOTg5MGE0YTVkNWQ2NTVmM2U4ZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T00:35:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T00:35:59Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep finished calls on live tool-group line (#4927)\n\nThe `dcode` tool-group progress line now keeps already-finished tool\ncalls visible (in past tense) while a step is still running.\n\nWhile a step is still running, the collapsed tool-group summary now\nkeeps calls that already finished visible in the past tense next to the\nones still in flight (e.g. `Ran 2 shell commands, running 1 agent…`),\ninstead of shrinking to only the running calls.\n\n---\n\nPR #4809 fixed finished calls being wrongly reported as still \"running\"\nby rebuilding the live line from only the in-progress members. That\nover-corrected: completed work vanished from the line entirely until the\nwhole step settled, so expanding a `Running 1 agent…` group could reveal\nseveral already-finished commands and agents.\n\nThis reconciles both concerns. The live line is now composed of a\npast-tense summary of the finished (successful) members plus a\npresent-tense summary of the still-running members, so nothing is\nmislabeled as running and nothing silently disappears.\nFailed/rejected/skipped tools are still evicted to standalone rows, and\nthe fully past-tense line shown once everything settles is unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f22422f0-4fb1-785e-f8d3-34c0b9e3ddd8)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b3cdcd2b9eaa15c0ca18f6c94fd27cd402986e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6b3cdcd2b9eaa15c0ca18f6c94fd27cd402986e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYrNvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOgoQAA6+MeIiOzDkcfLtlU1MeGwZ\nicsQ/ITEqyBQ/Z5aeaPzmI+LxMsiAR12AqmGZQJKDzrXuHkZEFPgawYWq0Ao6U1q\nyJpw8Q2tiysssvlrVeLE00x/5VqajLqlRg+8dhFtS+5/Fgg8evpelD1tks/hu+6L\ne0QSRDTWKruW3xl+5NxRtGb04fxvl3GvGfObr1tQjjGvcwCQbQX09XYkP3LpdyxY\nyiDQ3SGT/cFyUAYSs0JMnpQGTsww2DHGIX1WXcnF4QWEu0YLDhUemNHbuAYdD0h3\nfmIOJEauTidSbHphWEcZuba+RHMibcVCeR7M7pNPmVzFAwnEk/2e/JPm01jiN/H5\nEtbuiSdYrW5tgq0/pS1BKfi4CHknmrkgZ5+ddNPcrgbxWn35IfDgXQoO5c6lyfPa\nk1axINrRWmHxRAyUqgyAGIUS2zfaEyVfHsgqqhhqDRnaKzaQt8Th5/m3W23cVClx\nxHFalpod/GMiFCBMHCebROEvB4iBKkGqJ54f2Vn/dljZN1OrPTW0Y7ALZIHE9yOO\nqW87k78ycgT9rUG6ftZEwoiSXo8Uocpr/zVQdx+TWV1PbXpBRdkthOe/QnWRhVH4\nZPYtgcdNtJyXNNM+shs4afqSRyqU0BXcGwOdWO/dpwf/cXXthYX8Ou8wJa+Luycq\ntWC+FSTzyR5K9BfOKMNd\n=4Kfr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6b3cdcd2b9eaa15c0ca18f6c94fd27cd402986e5\nparent 52b8993489a9b6b92be077fe835743ef7704b6a0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784853359 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784853359 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep finished calls on live tool-group line (#4927)\n\nThe `dcode` tool-group progress line now keeps already-finished tool\ncalls visible (in past tense) while a step is still running.\n\nWhile a step is still running, the collapsed tool-group summary now\nkeeps calls that already finished visible in the past tense next to the\nones still in flight (e.g. `Ran 2 shell commands, running 1 agent…`),\ninstead of shrinking to only the running calls.\n\n---\n\nPR #4809 fixed finished calls being wrongly reported as still \"running\"\nby rebuilding the live line from only the in-progress members. That\nover-corrected: completed work vanished from the line entirely until the\nwhole step settled, so expanding a `Running 1 agent…` group could reveal\nseveral already-finished commands and agents.\n\nThis reconciles both concerns. The live line is now composed of a\npast-tense summary of the finished (successful) members plus a\npresent-tense summary of the still-running members, so nothing is\nmislabeled as running and nothing silently disappears.\nFailed/rejected/skipped tools are still evicted to standalone rows, and\nthe fully past-tense line shown once everything settles is unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f22422f0-4fb1-785e-f8d3-34c0b9e3ddd8)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T00:36:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/976c54b2e1392282044d9890a4a5d5d655f3e8dc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/org