":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce"}]},{"sha":"5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDViYzc3MTRmZTU1YTczYWM0ODkyZGViMTc4NTUyMmVhMzEwNjA3Y2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T00:21:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T00:21:18Z"},"message":"fix(code): restore `\"Server log preserved at:\"` notice on exit (#4999)\n\nWith `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` set, `dcode` again prints `Server log\npreserved at: <path>` to stderr after it exits.\n\n---\n\n`perf(code): coordinate async shutdown teardown` (#4831) moved server\n`stop()` into the deferred `_graceful_exit()` coroutine, which runs\n*before* `super().exit()` restores the terminal. The `Server log\npreserved at:` print inside `ServerProcess._stop_process_locked` then\nfired while Textual still owned the alternate screen and was discarded\non exit; the outer `run_textual_app` `stop()` is idempotent, so it never\nre-emitted the line.\n\nThe fix decouples *closing the log file* (must happen during `stop()`)\nfrom *announcing the preserved path* (must happen after the terminal is\nrestored). `_stop_process_locked` now records `_preserved_log_path`, and\na new `emit_preserved_log_notice()` prints it exactly once. It is called\nfrom the terminal stop sites that run after the terminal is restored or\nwith no TUI active (`run_textual_app` finally, `server_session` finally,\n`start_server_and_get_agent` finally, and `__aexit__`), and deliberately\nnot from the hidden in-session teardown or the `/restart` path. Because\nthe emitter clears the stored path, the interactive path's double\n`stop()` still yields a single visible line.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4ca951ec-5223-29f3-0312-2a0d17e26dcc)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4ca951ec-5223-29f3-0312-2a0d17e26dcc/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"39cd2e42e00813d3f4f528af22ad5270922adf91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/39cd2e42e00813d3f4f528af22ad5270922adf91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYq/+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA1sQAA4Hh4uoMWTnZFzIbRDrWBYp\nusAspu5zzMEj5PFkyWFTrV91Q69Um4phKm3P6XeLmHpfvavk8cvekTqOnlSaRFqn\nE5bJE3CjzyMpwH045KLQGHeCAF1U9psvRjn4r9UfsjbKKcOWjkLrQihYKYlqlkzH\nEysuYjnUJIaPu1UJmxtf+17ncoL+45fpls/BLewiwOHgCtimYteLqHUWjiVByVlL\ns0db9Eh0uumFP3nljylVDZchKkY6Xdxhkpg25/hTeLNZ+EX6+Uz09gH9v/1O828I\nDMANMIogxO6vUAdRa0LZrI/CUEuFlV5fRi8DtZ7F9N8e4KqQAix3pUkZNk5fNa/C\n+E03ic8XC4KzCeB/caVDtJ3ZFBgaX1L9q2ko3xTLhsNn4eIScMYTizhUkt7YjUzT\nIObiyazpCwQX2N+P8mwmHCGk9eH33gOy6/uxhE8w5Z9lX3L6fKNgnSQi+Cjs8Gx9\niKctoyLnamZWs9sZw4veor4u3RCTrlWG1X5MAR1aQH81giScP2KqT2JQvXA02QqB\nY+/7pedhIWO+bH4+AdFeL/vuDgfdMUJxqIeo1IJA8WchAAodFnnJs7qSLVBfUEJ5\n/3DbTPJPzUYKvzdFhgqMYxD2ItRjqlZlh8LO8tRvDxkJ0drM7FNmSqR10qsMl4KG\n5FjBW7wuqLn/UJqdGl46\n=YaAa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 39cd2e42e00813d3f4f528af22ad5270922adf91\nparent 654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784852478 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784852478 -0400\n\nfix(code): restore `\"Server log preserved at:\"` notice on exit (#4999)\n\nWith `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` set, `dcode` again prints `Server log\npreserved at: <path>` to stderr after it exits.\n\n---\n\n`perf(code): coordinate async shutdown teardown` (#4831) moved server\n`stop()` into the deferred `_graceful_exit()` coroutine, which runs\n*before* `super().exit()` restores the terminal. The `Server log\npreserved at:` print inside `ServerProcess._stop_process_locked` then\nfired while Textual still owned the alternate screen and was discarded\non exit; the outer `run_textual_app` `stop()` is idempotent, so it never\nre-emitted the line.\n\nThe fix decouples *closing the log file* (must happen during `stop()`)\nfrom *announcing the preserved path* (must happen after the terminal is\nrestored). `_stop_process_locked` now records `_preserved_log_path`, and\na new `emit_preserved_log_notice()` prints it exactly once. It is called\nfrom the terminal stop sites that run after the terminal is restored or\nwith no TUI active (`run_textual_app` finally, `server_session` finally,\n`start_server_and_get_agent` finally, and `__aexit__`), and deliberately\nnot from the hidden in-session teardown or the `/restart` path. Because\nthe emitter clears the stored path, the interactive path's double\n`stop()` still yields a single visible line.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4ca951ec-5223-29f3-0312-2a0d17e26dcc)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4ca951ec-5223-29f3-0312-2a0d17e26dcc/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T00:21:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bc7714fe55a73ac4892deb1785522ea310607ce/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486"}]},{"sha":"654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY1NGMxMWJmZmQ2OTBhNmY1MzAyNmFiZjBjMTA4NGMxOGQ4MWU0ODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-24T00:01:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T00:01:02Z"},"message":"ci(infra): move OpenWiki gateway URL to environment variable (#5007)\n\nRead the OpenWiki gateway base URL from the `openwiki` environment\nvariable instead of hardcoding LangSmith's URL in the workflow.\n\n---\n\nThe scheduled OpenWiki job already uses environment-scoped secrets for\ngateway auth. Pointing `OPENAI_BASE_URL` at `${{ vars.OPENAI_BASE_URL\n}}` keeps endpoint config alongside those credentials so the destination\ncan change without a workflow edit.\n\nSet `OPENAI_BASE_URL` on the `openwiki` GitHub Environment (previously\nhardcoded as `https://gateway.smith.langchain.com/openai/v1`).","tree":{"sha":"c4ee54fc9e8f41868698327abe480a452e6978c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c4ee54fc9e8f41868698327abe480a452e6978c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYqs+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5RwQAGeuRuCJSAdmCAag6fyyrbUl\nvzh1Qq2zTbx85YiyDD0Zs2LYjpwivcScG+Pk8SKOhcV9cnwZJT97C6EJ55/pwsZ2\nX3Ha01p9QG23GbcM5uOfIZscV1TE1TA1tQ0XgDBYFfe56J2x5fBbTVzo2JBAPmuy\nlkF5/bEL6sNWwW9U1sepZoGpLcGOwDJGH5c5fgsAIjZfSa8fAw57GiyZvV4TP75Q\nmRFU8OXKCQ1FLv8yGOmv5d4gIt9nGahUE8HrFLx1X34nDRl8O333yutQoAjQYF2L\nqGhErSBXYBIV6Uatj30NQToe4CA0rqF1XLv7ef2rSOgdVPVXK1ZX8xswG0m1aEXa\nmdIOm+31AQ5RndH3jyMlgP9sT2EVVQO4L1BY34SSC/6Z3dH08gQB+/Tj6KJF6U5I\nkeexbniMfz6dfcQBwiuAzKW8Gk0CF78McWY+6nrjZwJ7kbPNJvCASVesyStAhgvu\nB2w+0o7Jq/bRfqFjRtn/ACSJcxNB3WQAbVBSrURie6xkF0VHqWsfkzrCqyYDGaXL\nsDsLo3CowXRFtrXMCPOdfksIyx04OGlAY85T5RifumAAvNF99IUS9qfi/42sM+wY\n80ibGpw9qTCizEXOcYz8DwtCoTVrcaStXRmP8oJI539usO9PeIFb2AuSu/Q3py3Y\nPx/9JcBgk9VB8WeCiVNt\n=gsNP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c4ee54fc9e8f41868698327abe480a452e6978c0\nparent 67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784851262 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784851262 -0400\n\nci(infra): move OpenWiki gateway URL to environment variable (#5007)\n\nRead the OpenWiki gateway base URL from the `openwiki` environment\nvariable instead of hardcoding LangSmith's URL in the workflow.\n\n---\n\nThe scheduled OpenWiki job already uses environment-scoped secrets for\ngateway auth. Pointing `OPENAI_BASE_URL` at `${{ vars.OPENAI_BASE_URL\n}}` keeps endpoint config alongside those credentials so the destination\ncan change without a workflow edit.\n\nSet `OPENAI_BASE_URL` on the `openwiki` GitHub Environment (previously\nhardcoded as `https://gateway.smith.langchain.com/openai/v1`).","verified_at":"2026-07-24T00:01:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/654c11bffd690a6f53026abf0c1084c18d81e486/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e"}]},{"sha":"67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY3NDczYjk1ZmVkM2Q1NmQ1OWY3YmY2Yzk2MTExMDA0ZGRiNDVjN2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T23:11:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T23:11:54Z"},"message":"fix(evals): pin virtual_mode=False in the Harbor bare adapter (#5008)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe SDK's `LocalShellBackend` `virtual_mode` default flipped from\n`False` to `True`. The Harbor bare adapter (`make_bare_graph`)\nconstructs `LocalShellBackend(root_dir=..., inherit_env=False)`\n**without** pinning `virtual_mode`, so it silently began virtualizing\nsandbox paths.\n\nThat broke context-retrieval evals: the agent's filesystem tools resolve\npaths against a virtual root instead of the real sandbox paths the tasks\nuse. On gpt-5.6-luna lite, context **avg@k dropped ~0.90 → ~0.09**\n(largely hidden by pass@k, which saturates with rollouts).\n\n## Fix\n\nPin `virtual_mode=False` in the bare adapter. Harbor runs each task in\nits own isolated container rooted at the workdir, and the tasks operate\non real sandbox paths — path virtualization is unnecessary (isolation\ncomes from the container) and actively breaks file/retrieval tasks.\n\n## Result\n\nWith the pin, gpt-5.6-luna lite context returns to canonical (**avg@k\n0.967**, pass@k 1.00), matching the scorecard.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnified lite eval (gpt-5.6-luna, bare, docker) on this fix: context\npass@k 1.00 / avg@k 0.967 vs 0.70 / 0.09 without it.","tree":{"sha":"a7e0fdfdcc0fd1a74603fc39129d865e3f6ca74e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a7e0fdfdcc0fd1a74603fc39129d865e3f6ca74e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYp+6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjQIQAH41zwRAiPC8v/SptK7exDn+\n2XurysJS4YjCp1UFiKIcxjc6S079qu7b/mcyGpBCEqytzdw7IH7k2F3/yU33Qi05\nd7MuMix99tfi7DoUuN7Bl6yp/2jy4rO6EVaAJfnuT7MUikQ5QNbSruZBbw9sJbYt\nEKtAGS85UZc7vw/AF0DdgrQ99Y1ZmRYfPsfi1whKshop43cS2DXsQzEueufuLh2Q\nbDqiDa2oJUYYvJtvEysD36hQlciNo8X438FywM3n1NJauV8HNeQOb2615ZGt+o92\n8GevnGhsyQWCfn2Bi4jdHvhsN+wcr5RHUIrvBvHioEWQGAn2ZI5h2rtmlmRE4tNm\nhlnkRULz5SV0eq1gvKDW3rOxvLuyMdwSRkwzL6Rk8U2R/GzEZoDLL2H/N+N9Ks8F\nyKLt9oxzf752x3ZkaPk7mYAGS7o7RPIOPZrSlM2sCscKBaCJWOqJcH5ofdz4gXLP\n2LzWiGV1sPJ7ckrV5RAH5ABT2xTbZ/LApmUBLRFkb18SYiYbvGSCgqFlM2CBHVLt\nIEMqCII4K+MPFXewsmGIdiNHzeObk1ohwjbE8mYVv0jTuIYsRFyT7Z1a1dJJK/U0\nzHeWKwB9sxENyF2oKN6CU9K9o5dVmCllwkJH7Z5sPa1n34l2rWVhWyjAv91ZJhNZ\nppFp+k/C36WpHsPuF4aq\n=FNI3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7e0fdfdcc0fd1a74603fc39129d865e3f6ca74e\nparent d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784848314 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784848314 -0400\n\nfix(evals): pin virtual_mode=False in the Harbor bare adapter (#5008)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe SDK's `LocalShellBackend` `virtual_mode` default flipped from\n`False` to `True`. The Harbor bare adapter (`make_bare_graph`)\nconstructs `LocalShellBackend(root_dir=..., inherit_env=False)`\n**without** pinning `virtual_mode`, so it silently began virtualizing\nsandbox paths.\n\nThat broke context-retrieval evals: the agent's filesystem tools resolve\npaths against a virtual root instead of the real sandbox paths the tasks\nuse. On gpt-5.6-luna lite, context **avg@k dropped ~0.90 → ~0.09**\n(largely hidden by pass@k, which saturates with rollouts).\n\n## Fix\n\nPin `virtual_mode=False` in the bare adapter. Harbor runs each task in\nits own isolated container rooted at the workdir, and the tasks operate\non real sandbox paths — path virtualization is unnecessary (isolation\ncomes from the container) and actively breaks file/retrieval tasks.\n\n## Result\n\nWith the pin, gpt-5.6-luna lite context returns to canonical (**avg@k\n0.967**, pass@k 1.00), matching the scorecard.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnified lite eval (gpt-5.6-luna, bare, docker) on this fix: context\npass@k 1.00 / avg@k 0.967 vs 0.70 / 0.09 without it. ","verified_at":"2026-07-23T23:11:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/67473b95fed3d56d59f7bf6c96111004ddb45c7e/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7"}]},{"sha":"d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3MDdjMDIzMDQ3Yjk3YjkyZjgwYjJmODZmY2ZjOGEyZmVlNjE1Yjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T22:08:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T22:08:11Z"},"message":"chore(evals): regenerate stale `uv.lock` (#5003)","tree":{"sha":"0e4a5b7b905440ad0c8b32a9e1618a3934561409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0e4a5b7b905440ad0c8b32a9e1618a3934561409"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYpDLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANA8QAHP9qXUmprS9sQE3rXH3cXdd\nppnlSUV/6cB7M8h4YXgkxD5gaZ0dhKsNFcUvrcHGICJvgl1nsFSgB2R+dE+Buiwf\nzxxFnMEA6QcPpKYIzzPnoM+gU9FBvCfrRWd2NZYxM6/N67ApaPjkjfvK0BOdjikX\nDeXBJazh0gRzVCPZc78pJ2MkbUfgNoh34BtJM0cIpD1GtFOM8BcWhRJO7n58JYJf\n19iioCR+vXUSTlYHuFKC2UWiGTJSOPdta6FHuMdnrs4z0+MbQ6wSlC6dKvn7v8JU\n6GShUC+XQz/7h3G85FzW6xyLOotjVovZ8fYLYw/dYvfgfT2Ef93kg0V1MJrqKU9h\n5OOL1ItU4edW5s1FhMCwMi5xn0Betf8PNY/hwd93Nmh4Lofy655lgvOhj0025nFO\npnHuBKB7osDzWzC3B+0uDLwtgPdib2RcC9BV9TQJ2jdP3ahdjC878xn7r07C210c\nf8uAE6OZo4F1ru8tPyV1bzASF3E7li698BxSdovmmY9MSr7eKdXbMYAJMOzcuvev\nANOHd41dDp4D2KWTp7oI4qYrpaov7/z3VkEhTinM7nZZLimdyIBGN2QiSqgLqPZv\nNE6YH8oFtMJWPPfDYYgvHso9ZNLhe2zHKsgxGMiQLroQSYrHpnx0+9HZ2HPPdo2t\nMTYcmkIpB7AhdpdRWU/p\n=ZHYh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0e4a5b7b905440ad0c8b32a9e1618a3934561409\nparent 37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1784844491 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784844491 -0400\n\nchore(evals): regenerate stale `uv.lock` (#5003)","verified_at":"2026-07-23T22:08:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d707c023047b97b92f80b2f86fcfc8a2fee615b7/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e"}]},{"sha":"37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM3YWRkZmM4YmI1NTMzZDY2NzBkMTRkZWZlYTM4NzcwYzhkNTRkMWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T21:43:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T21:43:03Z"},"message":"feat(code): configure Auto goal criteria acceptance (#4940)\n\nAuto mode now reviews generated goal acceptance criteria by default,\nwhile users who prefer uninterrupted goal setup can opt into applying\nthem automatically. Manual mode always reviews and YOLO remains\nautomatic.\n\n---\n\nUsers who have not already configured a preference see a one-time\nselector the first time they create or amend a goal **in Auto mode**:\n\n- **Review before applying** is recommended and preselected.\n- **Apply automatically in Auto mode** enables the uninterrupted flow.\n\nA Manual or YOLO user is prompted the first time they create or amend a\ngoal after switching to Auto. Explicit environment or TOML settings\nsuppress the selector, and a versioned state marker prevents it from\nreappearing once answered.\n\nConfigure the Auto-mode preference in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[goals]\nauto_accept_criteria = true\n```\n\nOr set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_GOAL_AUTO_ACCEPT_CRITERIA=true`. The environment\nvariable takes precedence over TOML, invalid environment values fall\nthrough to TOML and then the safe `false` default, and the preference is\nresolved live on each proposal decision—so file or environment edits\napply the next time a goal proposal is created, amended, regenerated,\nrestored, or mode-resolved, not only after relaunch. If the preference\ncannot be resolved, it fails closed to review and logs.\n\nNew, amended, regenerated, restored, and mode-transitioned goal\nproposals all resolve through the same live policy so the selected\nbehavior is consistent throughout the session.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example: Manual user later switches to Auto</summary>\n\n1. Mason works in Manual and runs `/goal ship OAuth`. No preference\nselector appears, because the setting only affects Auto.\n2. Later he enables Auto, then runs `/goal add refresh tokens` or `/goal\namend include passkeys`.\n3. Because Auto still has the built-in default and no marker, he gets\nthe one-time selector with **Review before applying** preselected.\n4. His choice is saved to `config.toml` and the versioned marker is set\nso the prompt does not return.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example: File edit takes effect on the next proposal\ndecision</summary>\n\n1. Mason is already in Auto with review selected.\n2. In another editor he sets `auto_accept_criteria = true` in\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml`.\n3. Nothing changes immediately.\n4. On the next create, amend, regenerate, restore, or mode-resolution of\na goal proposal, dcode re-reads the preference and auto-applies.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example: Same live policy across proposal paths</summary>\n\n- **New:** `/goal ship login` drafts criteria and either reviews or\nauto-applies under the current Auto/YOLO policy.\n- **Amended:** `/goal amend also require passkeys` regenerates the\nchecklist and resolves it the same way.\n- **Regenerated:** feedback on an open review produces a new proposal\nthat uses the policy in effect when it arrives.\n- **Restored:** resuming a thread with a pending proposal resolves that\npending state through the same gate.\n- **Mode-transitioned:** enabling Auto or YOLO with a mounted review\nre-resolves that pending proposal immediately under the live policy.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\nOther nits:\n\n* Removed `/goal accept` and `/goal edit` subcommands. These were\nredirect-only handlers that pointed users to the inline review prompt;\nthe review prompt's own keybindings are the real actions, so the\nsubcommands were a discoverability dead end.\n* Simplified the `/goal` usage text to describe what `/goal` does rather\nthan enumerating per-mode behavior. The mode-specific behavior is\ndiscoverable through the app and the first-run preference screen.\n* Removed the \"Goal criteria automatically accepted without manual\nreview.\" toast that fired on auto-accepted proposals. YOLO's contract is\nno prompts, and opted-in Auto users already know they opted in, so the\ntoast was noise for both.","tree":{"sha":"ca14a83c7a896566b0ee15f40c20195482a3d327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ca14a83c7a896566b0ee15f40c20195482a3d327"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYornCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyKEQAISywhy+8YJRC52XGGDva/t4\ncaCNX8uOS+B3LKVQxlRjfpEvQE4Q7f6VVhA8MkSTDRM1U/pwCR89c+nyGgfC0HCn\ndojCWecrKxQQXYRbmy8ZDyPCDEYOBgI5S5snydLguNWXgmFc1Nx90pKUJWiGETKL\nkgVcfmYfD5N4A6Z/MLeoCr9MST/w1N7c0WyLdlLOvFvVC+p9sFnklmGiVhZjmgyb\nX/xMdDC9i1NipQNK4uENo9e9Skl8whWvOB41cELvZgiwehUEMcdOY+AAgMUCqGuz\nl7i9eIacEMKp02WsN5NYyJvcmdo1pWwA+IuDaWMR+o3OiI9mPCKQV+JqLIoSFtP6\nVqk+jD//86/fcr8OZoHMtT6m4E9pFnszw5jnu4DbgKFuhXqJ8UbXmyhZmYi3qDyE\nllqDcs84eHDha6buGlnsXryZER+tX6KuJIj6sCjyMwA1GLiFiyQqNvvF1prmVgYl\n+L1ABL1Ok/DGv6dWHFIq1l8QT639PMFkO+wmfQZ9wYU9CUxPHTvjpWE1YKo3R+i7\nzJPDFxioaUhbXFR/nsGr43P8GeuqT0E/Cu5uB46rkGSBwca6mFjOs29BuxUSG5AF\n99OiEJbCrFKJrxQP9zMAj8WDbFDH0KVNA/K+GDlPp8N39+BRE2c1oQRCAd6lLsXu\nQ56ApEYmVytK6tb7SVoC\n=DY8W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ca14a83c7a896566b0ee15f40c20195482a3d327\nparent 861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784842983 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784842983 -0400\n\nfeat(code): configure Auto goal criteria acceptance (#4940)\n\nAuto mode now reviews generated goal acceptance criteria by default,\nwhile users who prefer uninterrupted goal setup can opt into applying\nthem automatically. Manual mode always reviews and YOLO remains\nautomatic.\n\n---\n\nUsers who have not already configured a preference see a one-time\nselector the first time they create or amend a goal **in Auto mode**:\n\n- **Review before applying** is recommended and preselected.\n- **Apply automatically in Auto mode** enables the uninterrupted flow.\n\nA Manual or YOLO user is prompted the first time they create or amend a\ngoal after switching to Auto. Explicit environment or TOML settings\nsuppress the selector, and a versioned state marker prevents it from\nreappearing once answered.\n\nConfigure the Auto-mode preference in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[goals]\nauto_accept_criteria = true\n```\n\nOr set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_GOAL_AUTO_ACCEPT_CRITERIA=true`. The environment\nvariable takes precedence over TOML, invalid environment values fall\nthrough to TOML and then the safe `false` default, and the preference is\nresolved live on each proposal decision—so file or environment edits\napply the next time a goal proposal is created, amended, regenerated,\nrestored, or mode-resolved, not only after relaunch. If the preference\ncannot be resolved, it fails closed to review and logs.\n\nNew, amended, regenerated, restored, and mode-transitioned goal\nproposals all resolve through the same live policy so the selected\nbehavior is consistent throughout the session.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example: Manual user later switches to Auto</summary>\n\n1. Mason works in Manual and runs `/goal ship OAuth`. No preference\nselector appears, because the setting only affects Auto.\n2. Later he enables Auto, then runs `/goal add refresh tokens` or `/goal\namend include passkeys`.\n3. Because Auto still has the built-in default and no marker, he gets\nthe one-time selector with **Review before applying** preselected.\n4. His choice is saved to `config.toml` and the versioned marker is set\nso the prompt does not return.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example: File edit takes effect on the next proposal\ndecision</summary>\n\n1. Mason is already in Auto with review selected.\n2. In another editor he sets `auto_accept_criteria = true` in\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml`.\n3. Nothing changes immediately.\n4. On the next create, amend, regenerate, restore, or mode-resolution of\na goal proposal, dcode re-reads the preference and auto-applies.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example: Same live policy across proposal paths</summary>\n\n- **New:** `/goal ship login` drafts criteria and either reviews or\nauto-applies under the current Auto/YOLO policy.\n- **Amended:** `/goal amend also require passkeys` regenerates the\nchecklist and resolves it the same way.\n- **Regenerated:** feedback on an open review produces a new proposal\nthat uses the policy in effect when it arrives.\n- **Restored:** resuming a thread with a pending proposal resolves that\npending state through the same gate.\n- **Mode-transitioned:** enabling Auto or YOLO with a mounted review\nre-resolves that pending proposal immediately under the live policy.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\nOther nits:\n\n* Removed `/goal accept` and `/goal edit` subcommands. These were\nredirect-only handlers that pointed users to the inline review prompt;\nthe review prompt's own keybindings are the real actions, so the\nsubcommands were a discoverability dead end.\n* Simplified the `/goal` usage text to describe what `/goal` does rather\nthan enumerating per-mode behavior. The mode-specific behavior is\ndiscoverable through the app and the first-run preference screen.\n* Removed the \"Goal criteria automatically accepted without manual\nreview.\" toast that fired on auto-accepted proposals. YOLO's contract is\nno prompts, and opted-in Auto users already know they opted in, so the\ntoast was noise for both.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T21:43:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37addfc8bb5533d6670d14defea38770c8d54d1e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381"}]},{"sha":"861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg2MWU4ZTc4YzMwMTE3N2MyYzIzMTg3ZWY0OTM1ZTU5ZDJhMTkzODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T21:42:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T21:42:46Z"},"message":"test(infra): harden workflow credential contracts (#5006)\n\nCredential-scoping regressions now fail with precise assertions instead\nof passing when secret names, conditions, and references merely appear\nsomewhere in the same workflow step.\n\n---\n\nThe static contracts now parse workflow YAML and compare the complete\nintegration and disabled-release `env` mappings. This binds each secret\nto its exact package condition and credential reference while rejecting\nunexpected additional entries, including an accidentally unconditional\nsecret.\n\nA separate reachability contract records `libs/code` and\n`libs/partners/quickjs` as deliberate free-text override targets and\nverifies every credential condition still points to an existing package\npath. The dormant integration workflow and its current matrix are\notherwise unchanged.\n\nThe same parser-based approach replaces whitespace-sensitive extraction\nfor the GitHub App, release, and OpenWiki contracts. A release comment\nexplains why Deep Agents Code intentionally receives no provider\ncredentials there, and two setup comments now refer to the plural\ncredentials they list.","tree":{"sha":"db7a293df9623965b29d31de78ebc1fbcb9ad3b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/db7a293df9623965b29d31de78ebc1fbcb9ad3b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYorWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4I8QAEu03HdEXPMaWoS9E8DkS5Uy\nOAoQwbpbIzihp4zepMONi0PrRbPzVQ4l8fYQYVPg3Ps7tWbv0PWw1Fha7AqDkWGp\nH5fqR/8E82yY2dHblVPBSh4od8mwLhfmcoIbAMu/NMe+W824zCBemGenqcePAqrJ\n4A0cuM89FfASpQ5puWdlsm0+5+Njn8+ITHNQvA4+Eo1pZ27tnbqLqtKPh1CN6+UQ\njzeWm1C7yev531Dpv9nhtAD4CJ0Q72rMWkZaTcTbwcDFzD18dl6FW1K+a4co/2As\nERc2aThrmwC7Rn3QdYgw3MutU/8cVTxSqpDkPA6GJDlwp7LNDk88KqIU2U2mXtg1\nSdtZAJCiQDES0m1SF/fRwvorUwd7+pS8gjciHlm/4RBytv9+Mfd8jL2Rk93IGP9n\nq5NeDw1xNTqJFuG0oa5kif3B78TQJF81jzN6132qBkAONpjlp8FHaCZCczUB4ncQ\nGmP+v0v0YWFevqPvTMPYNxSiVPOWts2QegS9CCsRdUPB4fPpD2RwPniVPJG+TDP1\n3iZGqI8Yvqt4pGfQGyW9yaOHC6fY0P+JkzknN5qlcWwQ2MeGszR50cn8U2ygcFY+\nbJE2qVb9LY4ef6PHOcnI6PKe2v7c5WqknznoZ7aeuZnjbwrxkIrudCGfcIzdTCDz\nwwpPNz+exwtEjsm+u5+C\n=qz3W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree db7a293df9623965b29d31de78ebc1fbcb9ad3b0\nparent a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784842966 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784842966 -0400\n\ntest(infra): harden workflow credential contracts (#5006)\n\nCredential-scoping regressions now fail with precise assertions instead\nof passing when secret names, conditions, and references merely appear\nsomewhere in the same workflow step.\n\n---\n\nThe static contracts now parse workflow YAML and compare the complete\nintegration and disabled-release `env` mappings. This binds each secret\nto its exact package condition and credential reference while rejecting\nunexpected additional entries, including an accidentally unconditional\nsecret.\n\nA separate reachability contract records `libs/code` and\n`libs/partners/quickjs` as deliberate free-text override targets and\nverifies every credential condition still points to an existing package\npath. The dormant integration workflow and its current matrix are\notherwise unchanged.\n\nThe same parser-based approach replaces whitespace-sensitive extraction\nfor the GitHub App, release, and OpenWiki contracts. A release comment\nexplains why Deep Agents Code intentionally receives no provider\ncredentials there, and two setup comments now refer to the plural\ncredentials they list.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T21:42:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/861e8e78c301177c2c23187ef4935e59d2a19381/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46"}]},{"sha":"a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE2OGRkMDY4ZmZjZjljMjEyOGEyODBjODZiMDA0MTliODYwOTZkNDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T20:30:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T20:30:24Z"},"message":"ci(infra): scope GitHub Actions credentials (#5004)\n\nGitHub Actions now exposes stored credentials only to the automation and\npackage tests that need them, and OpenWiki is ready to read its API keys\nfrom a dedicated environment instead of repository scope.\n\n---\n\nThe GitHub App Client ID is not sensitive, so token-minting workflows\nnow read it from the repository variable while the private key remains a\nsecret. Integration-test credentials are selected by matrix package,\nincluding wiring the previously unavailable Daytona key. The disabled\nrelease integration step keeps its future credential wiring but applies\nthe same package-level isolation.\n\nOpenWiki now targets an `openwiki` environment. Repository-level\nfallback keeps the workflow working during migration; after environment\nsecrets are configured and a manual run succeeds, the repository copies\ncan be removed.","tree":{"sha":"7a97792112bddfe44d4cbef9efca00f0bd6d43d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7a97792112bddfe44d4cbef9efca00f0bd6d43d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYnngCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoj4QAKzDaMr614l52P3eG5EZgHf2\nXITISRS90e6+eZOzMk1OOfxGaImTxvsmyDvIe37uuZUHbWzE98GcnboZdSEGaFHy\nddv5qtBs5s8hFqza0k1vqyuo5mMrizTbHUk8xISnnwu17ooAa6oREolBSmtZDtsY\nUGRUlYudjDm3u16HraWRgwtzpvh1qborVE9J+TkqmAX5bmeDc2Z9/1rtE7vdjJFN\nZ8w9axT0p+Y/YBlGfXeXrKGfOr73k1uyZE0OWpAiTG0yMPR7EUOFkRCdkP+lfY7u\nyoYuPvuMhuil5g1STaINtVwbwOsmIpfoyg9uv58ShuOSjmT8hlGk+2sg3QGuw6cr\n1k0W0bfiWfznY/Ohx6RCplhXaTxbto9bw55nx8TNbP44T6n8hAx9U919ZWbwC341\nx8g56bnCQmE1VqBtjF7gQvuiXa5YBm9O4syl3w3/vqV+76pveQDwS0ZDlf8dPOgx\ntwT0ApLbTT45TdqLqy+wXPXwSy5q1bCrtUGr/ngS4ZBIjMxr256PJq5Omn4I9o5Y\n7Pydk3hDbKRcs2kug/tkKZ/kqZNkGm210DF/jEoYWjlDbjECQ3D8u5vl283uJ6ok\nSSJo1ybj+5EHIxDhgDbr2VExzX8ur90DOqWNqbDl+F962OkU3wB7vzQDvQ3WKZKM\nmuX1N0kHjmlPgHan+yym\n=/AVC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7a97792112bddfe44d4cbef9efca00f0bd6d43d6\nparent 5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784838624 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784838624 -0400\n\nci(infra): scope GitHub Actions credentials (#5004)\n\nGitHub Actions now exposes stored credentials only to the automation and\npackage tests that need them, and OpenWiki is ready to read its API keys\nfrom a dedicated environment instead of repository scope.\n\n---\n\nThe GitHub App Client ID is not sensitive, so token-minting workflows\nnow read it from the repository variable while the private key remains a\nsecret. Integration-test credentials are selected by matrix package,\nincluding wiring the previously unavailable Daytona key. The disabled\nrelease integration step keeps its future credential wiring but applies\nthe same package-level isolation.\n\nOpenWiki now targets an `openwiki` environment. Repository-level\nfallback keeps the workflow working during migration; after environment\nsecrets are configured and a manual run succeeds, the repository copies\ncan be removed.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T20:30:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a68dd068ffcf9c2128a280c86b00419b86096d46/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e"}]},{"sha":"5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDViODMyZWFhMGVhMGNiY2U5NzAwMDdjNWQ0YTI3ZTJhZWYzMDU3N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T18:00:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T18:00:51Z"},"message":"fix(infra): place `Released from` after attribution (#5001)\n\nWhen a release is cut from a non-default branch (pre-release throwaways\nor a `vX.Y` line), the generated GitHub release body now puts the\n`Released from … at commit …` provenance line immediately after\n`Released by`, instead of above the user-facing notes area.\n\nThat keeps branch/commit ship metadata with the attribution footer, and\nleaves the space under the pre-release warning free for curated notes.\n\nAlso updates the pre-release enrichment guidance in the release docs so\nagents insert notes after the warning and before the attribution\ndivider.","tree":{"sha":"76b19a280e4f4082f75dca7fc0bc4c6eab59badf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/76b19a280e4f4082f75dca7fc0bc4c6eab59badf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYlbTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADz4QAAWav2mF89Qqt2kloN9if1UF\nbfRs4Cq1j4UyIp3cri0XpdpMR84RpU+jYt/8/YP0tKqhk7OZK49KiB1QBeSUf6gt\nvvl3aY2dW6yg+yFG/07EFaVZWLLYv6v/DV56EGzZ0HpOLn4HK3xrCERoKjyp8PQN\nFkXnUm2CejOM2WSYaRRlL3Hb6jcu168iEns9J4EYNlqxQWc5VuMpHLd5MHqADHey\nb13naE01vEt4JxJGn3b8OSsTatBzYwLxkAHSRf1Le1MRwJ3o7WGrHDmxxNey31Bt\ndXhnQTmXC/0hxufua9R5zupk/7dN70f/AeVQnhoREbv+a+5OPnlIqiMab9qo7a9x\nP2uhYQDf0WemwraxXWWG/4p0ZF+GEm0lej4KVpNxVA+SPuC5Sl46mmUWTfrjpJBF\nCGPu5Ra2MLjEIKSlhEC41+isvGWGD/TofZf3pBT5p0+2FIexywp8+bF4yxIKNK6R\niNRKdO8r/cbtzMdy5uy4r0bud4GLA86mB50YO1+2BsHnyteUvPbbNSjNYQLMIcAV\nruvhHxL8vHUeIvB8lTieG2hRapyuQ0k2l9aBpnfSFzJJ+0X3392lzKu5AlKUql34\nL6itIaVjFs6NCP/SxRooFrfZ1ijD9L9/z7jPyMAe22yv14jC3ctkZhl2Ywr5Kpqg\njI8IKDFTPPvlt1RCCVCs\n=A07c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 76b19a280e4f4082f75dca7fc0bc4c6eab59badf\nparent ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784829651 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784829651 -0400\n\nfix(infra): place `Released from` after attribution (#5001)\n\nWhen a release is cut from a non-default branch (pre-release throwaways\nor a `vX.Y` line), the generated GitHub release body now puts the\n`Released from … at commit …` provenance line immediately after\n`Released by`, instead of above the user-facing notes area.\n\nThat keeps branch/commit ship metadata with the attribution footer, and\nleaves the space under the pre-release warning free for curated notes.\n\nAlso updates the pre-release enrichment guidance in the release docs so\nagents insert notes after the warning and before the attribution\ndivider.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T18:00:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b832eaa0ea0cbce970007c5d4a27e2aef30577e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd"}]},{"sha":"ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNhODZmYmVjY2ExYTQzZmFjYjQyODEzOTc3NjBjNWU1MmVkYjFkZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T17:57:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T17:57:33Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Hooks v2 session transcripts (#4918)\n\nDepends on #4917\nCloses DCD-70\n\nHooks v2 now materializes private versioned transcript projections and\nexposes them through a session-scoped client runtime.\n\n---\n\nThis is 3/3 in the DCD-70 stack.\n\n- Adds deterministic per-thread and subagent JSONL projections with\nredaction, path-safe identities, private permissions, atomic writes,\nrevisions, and retention.\n- Adds a client-owned runtime that freezes one snapshot and materializes\nreal transcript paths immediately before command execution.\n- Keeps lifecycle call-site and server/client dispatch wiring out of\nscope for the following tickets.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 101 passed\n- `make lint`\n- `make check_imports`\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4917\n    - **feat(code): add Hooks v2 session transcripts** :point_left:\n      - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4971\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"a95860b800716e2fe47e5ffc7b1616fe5209940e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a95860b800716e2fe47e5ffc7b1616fe5209940e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYlYNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiEcQAGeoDmuU77BoTAm0VrgFrZ9L\n6ktsHZYOsIepVvosYMDp6mobV8i1aPbqskYRuiHIugvu6ZsMjmVorsvBCNNS8rbJ\nYIjUfLf5V/XpdT2zYwzO8sdNMDsGNIejyKZ3Gf3HlucOH3Lqa2SLOCHthoXKSH+l\nQQQOMcYi0yJf+ZYVJtg637J1VbpY9fbBVzu8c6hjRZJCCN5gr481cRoaHbuYTXXJ\nGx/dkjG2l7PDOAmqb6hIVD2L03gWpB4QaWIKCawlLOP2b1DSZtspRbqz3EX9KOfX\nl6qiVvfcFQc2Taum8qiRMK1F0O2xe23KEyJTfQYeE9LDZhZJZd0iD6bVSvL75ahx\nVklQGK+1vcUnu3DokFlq33IdOMDkGGx4z6i5r5D99lfgQAlOuXK2Kz0yULldlCfW\nCtYqh5PZ4priFejcbq2TtAsYhljflG2KZ3J2xx46OOJ1a0TNBR/XXCZAtMcMwODr\nNYY47WB7AGNztyfcL083UzuiAcTsJ9nyVCDSvl4blOsmaBRcq6QH231bC5uIG4zP\nnInFsFmRdZPEN5n1kxfMNS6nJvZw2A0ezWMI7zjGTt5g5I3wG91ueVbYj/KkcRkM\n4ew94Q7SM0CvDVLsvCqEzYktvH97/Mrlrm03BtQSnGObA7DBFoFJ/DOF/8lJWVRO\nUepbCtW39qE50GNYfjBS\n=d6OA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a95860b800716e2fe47e5ffc7b1616fe5209940e\nparent 9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784829453 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784829453 -0700\n\nfeat(code): add Hooks v2 session transcripts (#4918)\n\nDepends on #4917\nCloses DCD-70\n\nHooks v2 now materializes private versioned transcript projections and\nexposes them through a session-scoped client runtime.\n\n---\n\nThis is 3/3 in the DCD-70 stack.\n\n- Adds deterministic per-thread and subagent JSONL projections with\nredaction, path-safe identities, private permissions, atomic writes,\nrevisions, and retention.\n- Adds a client-owned runtime that freezes one snapshot and materializes\nreal transcript paths immediately before command execution.\n- Keeps lifecycle call-site and server/client dispatch wiring out of\nscope for the following tickets.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 101 passed\n- `make lint`\n- `make check_imports`\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4917\n    - **feat(code): add Hooks v2 session transcripts** :point_left:\n      - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4971\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T17:57:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ca86fbecca1a43facb4281397760c5e52edb1ddd/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38"}]},{"sha":"9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhZjkwYWUzNTBjODFhZTVhMmI2ZjZlODM1ZTgyZDkyN2I3ZTBmMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T17:55:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T17:55:06Z"},"message":"chore(code): bump SDK pin to 0.7.0b1 and dependency minimums (#5000)\n\nPins Deep Agents Code to `deepagents==0.7.0b1` and refreshes dependency\nlower bounds so dcode installs stay on current supported releases.\n\n---\n\nThis keeps the code package aligned with the published 0.7 beta SDK line\nand bumps package minima that have newer stable releases, including:\n\n- `langsmith[sandbox]` `0.10.10`\n- `langchain-aws` `1.6.3`\n- `aiohttp` `3.14.3`\n- `langchain-openrouter` `0.2.7`\n- media extra `av` major 18 (matching the SDK video extra)\n\n`ty` stays on `0.0.61` with an upper bound below `0.0.62` because newer\n`ty` releases panic during full-package typecheck in this repo. A few\ncall sites were also narrowed so dict/`list.index` inputs stay\ntype-checkable.","tree":{"sha":"127661d737740de451df601acd8a870ab6bcb2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/127661d737740de451df601acd8a870ab6bcb2e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYlV6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX9wQAAhJHj+iM6GDP1NLFcrJYA5O\n5MV4SBtSDBOQGano4Y69mMV82lODeT655Mpfaw6OvDDfp1M22sZNaaO9qBgU0jb1\nK35e5UvVVJcUN2vkpHQqlsKJkihXLKwznT2Q4XJaMpLm5WcWOh1ZgjRfhHGWFZxv\ngr5OAmw1tjZCKXEKc0RIKLpz5VLsn1d26PWqz1lerisnbzX4XFVD/CNvFXvlLGQT\n1ShrXxhP1Vz9mtnY2TZEMQei3WzRXw6xLJvm9r+kp8DiuG3WsNdfT7NTW9FIvuqQ\n7fMgYd0MFtmp0b/lSyB4/VPyB3rdxniXiJXC+fD6g4Rb4LBN0Lx72eJGXU4rUI3Y\nWgnk7zYdZniwcEp/0Zz4PI8lJqF9OHcQ8b6h1M51wbBBslNlm32oKpkpnJIg1HZd\nCzisj6jU4s+kJuKFJI4aLyBErIJa4t6NFs09Xrg+qNMVgtQQ5LSNIM8GgQav8Qd7\ncOaSd+ihERXPI4GsQiN3C51iOiHLRd90qxfb53yb99uOqxa2fcGvspLV+Y6qGIt2\nGbE6Ww871zdMIHstgZU0KnPGUEe87GZi/Nt4CmHfPhIpPHShHJkFjRtoFZjeWPwg\nbG3Hf+VY0Zl/FmHJMXoEUdm64yB1Sfty7SFhv9oW6qR86koRDj2TrupsVrfHvwPc\npVn3qRsdfn/q+8W4Dw/F\n=smqa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 127661d737740de451df601acd8a870ab6bcb2e3\nparent d9f54fc09925171c6c0a933abd33507f85e8851c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784829306 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784829306 -0400\n\nchore(code): bump SDK pin to 0.7.0b1 and dependency minimums (#5000)\n\nPins Deep Agents Code to `deepagents==0.7.0b1` and refreshes dependency\nlower bounds so dcode installs stay on current supported releases.\n\n---\n\nThis keeps the code package aligned with the published 0.7 beta SDK line\nand bumps package minima that have newer stable releases, including:\n\n- `langsmith[sandbox]` `0.10.10`\n- `langchain-aws` `1.6.3`\n- `aiohttp` `3.14.3`\n- `langchain-openrouter` `0.2.7`\n- media extra `av` major 18 (matching the SDK video extra)\n\n`ty` stays on `0.0.61` with an upper bound below `0.0.62` because newer\n`ty` releases panic during full-package typecheck in this repo. A few\ncall sites were also narrowed so dict/`list.index` inputs stay\ntype-checkable.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T17:55:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9af90ae350c81ae5a2b6f6e835e82d927b7e0f38/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdr