users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e"}]},{"sha":"94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk0OTYyYTVmNTg4Y2U4NDk5MWFkMzgyYjc3MTMxNTVkNmE1YTIzMWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T15:42:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T15:42:59Z"},"message":"feat(code): raise agent recursion limit to 2000 and make it configurable (#4994)\n\nThe `dcode` main agent's LangGraph `recursion_limit` was hardcoded to\n`1000`, which long-running sessions were hitting\n(`GRAPH_RECURSION_LIMIT`). This raises the default to `2000` and makes\nit user-tunable via a `--recursion-limit` CLI flag, a\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_RECURSION_LIMIT` env var, or\n`[runtime].recursion_limit` in `config.toml`, resolved with precedence\nCLI > env > `config.toml` > default.\n\n---\n\nThe default now lives once in `config_manifest` as\n`RECURSION_LIMIT_DEFAULT`, consumed by both the `config.config`\nrunnable-config fallback and the new `runtime.recursion_limit` manifest\noption, so `config`/`config get` surface it automatically.\n`create_cli_agent` resolves the effective limit at build time via\n`resolve_recursion_limit`, which validates the value against an\ninclusive floor (`25`, the LangGraph default ceiling) and ceiling\n(`100_000`) and logs a warning and falls back to the default for\nout-of-range or malformed values, so a bad override can never break runs\nor request unbounded traversal. The CLI value threads through\n`ServerConfig` (mirroring `rubric_max_iterations`) to the server-side\nagent build.\n\n`goal_rubric` recursion limits are unrelated and untouched.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `runtime.recursion_limit` resolution: env wins, `config.toml`\nfallback, default, and out-of-range/malformed fallback (incl.\nfloor/ceiling bounds).\n- `ServerConfig` round-trip + `__post_init__` validation for\n`recursion_limit`.\n- `--recursion-limit` argparse parsing (positive int; rejects\n`0`/negatives) and help-screen drift.\n- Regression: `config.config[\"recursion_limit\"] == 2000 ==\nRECURSION_LIMIT_DEFAULT`.\n- `make format`, `make lint` (ruff + ty + commands-catalog) all pass.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/bd7380f1-04cf-20c3-c2f7-d0e05211f2ee)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/bd7380f1-04cf-20c3-c2f7-d0e05211f2ee/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"15188b52eca489f93b8fb2da84b61a1004aaa032","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/15188b52eca489f93b8fb2da84b61a1004aaa032"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYjaDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYTMQACG974jj6jgAcapivHinHykf\nTQdUaZ5eyxUabuSnXYZxftpfYZsDmtLadLIPTCb8AlDgJ44iguCRq4Pu9h9OoQ9w\nWUqWZBooQJXnaRN288vPeOPExhG9pdCMzVyrRsXEmops4cQGaUT0D1u+zmehmXzV\nkaktWC1uYmsRCx1sueqcmJxnMeWjuvKS7C4DSk+rVZ1BCE1K53l1JB8tsb9YRFX0\nwgz9e1WRu2zVzc+6klVWU9j1WtJwwX5mdf2ghi/SqeHMkvqrhR0jqVEb5a74Zd83\nzpBkVh5QoEhwQCwqb1mfCXKwsbAY/rFS44cNwV+8s2AYsu5C86ixzfmP/o021mI+\nTH9u7AkbUHs64L0XHvg70yobXsDAUUS1r7mWuDrMh3/qBIDzfgftnqczYX40o1bR\nbwAp+63E4kyYjzzsFINWiVwOUbrUJkxjvQ+K6gR9TCeKADh1Bq2OcZMcatTchpct\nHu2USPz5Yt9aOjSCAh1dP14jo4LI4L9rOecibJO8lhCeZrnjzshNhAxSD2zUXEdY\nQB7aOws8+ee7wH8H3i8x7Fk2/sTnB7qiMzRzU/L/Wi/HshQGi4Xg9mTQo9wvpbvu\nbvnYHsSODLDqBpcQbMwDqnssUAjp9s9CEEyQNDuwXMYCsBzR0D+B+pw6lrBhxQqm\n+05C1jb2wi9uexDfQnST\n=Wsxq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 15188b52eca489f93b8fb2da84b61a1004aaa032\nparent 03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784821379 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784821379 -0400\n\nfeat(code): raise agent recursion limit to 2000 and make it configurable (#4994)\n\nThe `dcode` main agent's LangGraph `recursion_limit` was hardcoded to\n`1000`, which long-running sessions were hitting\n(`GRAPH_RECURSION_LIMIT`). This raises the default to `2000` and makes\nit user-tunable via a `--recursion-limit` CLI flag, a\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_RECURSION_LIMIT` env var, or\n`[runtime].recursion_limit` in `config.toml`, resolved with precedence\nCLI > env > `config.toml` > default.\n\n---\n\nThe default now lives once in `config_manifest` as\n`RECURSION_LIMIT_DEFAULT`, consumed by both the `config.config`\nrunnable-config fallback and the new `runtime.recursion_limit` manifest\noption, so `config`/`config get` surface it automatically.\n`create_cli_agent` resolves the effective limit at build time via\n`resolve_recursion_limit`, which validates the value against an\ninclusive floor (`25`, the LangGraph default ceiling) and ceiling\n(`100_000`) and logs a warning and falls back to the default for\nout-of-range or malformed values, so a bad override can never break runs\nor request unbounded traversal. The CLI value threads through\n`ServerConfig` (mirroring `rubric_max_iterations`) to the server-side\nagent build.\n\n`goal_rubric` recursion limits are unrelated and untouched.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `runtime.recursion_limit` resolution: env wins, `config.toml`\nfallback, default, and out-of-range/malformed fallback (incl.\nfloor/ceiling bounds).\n- `ServerConfig` round-trip + `__post_init__` validation for\n`recursion_limit`.\n- `--recursion-limit` argparse parsing (positive int; rejects\n`0`/negatives) and help-screen drift.\n- Regression: `config.config[\"recursion_limit\"] == 2000 ==\nRECURSION_LIMIT_DEFAULT`.\n- `make format`, `make lint` (ruff + ty + commands-catalog) all pass.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/bd7380f1-04cf-20c3-c2f7-d0e05211f2ee)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/bd7380f1-04cf-20c3-c2f7-d0e05211f2ee/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T15:43:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/94962a5f588ce84991ad382b7713155d6a5a231e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f"}]},{"sha":"03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAzYTY1MWM1ZjkwYmNmOTYyMjA4NmUxZjhkODFiNDYyYTM3NmNiM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T15:36:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T15:36:26Z"},"message":"ci(infra): apply `pending-deletion` when warning old PRs (#4998)\n\nThe old-PR cleanup workflow already comments when a PR reaches the\nwarning threshold. It now also adds a `pending-deletion` label at that\nsame point so those PRs are easy to find and filter before they\nauto-close.\n\nAlready-warned PRs that are missing the label get it on the next run.\nPRs with `do-not-close` are still skipped entirely.\n\n---\n\nEnsures the repo label exists (yellow) alongside `do-not-close`, applies\nit with the warning comment, and backfills it when a prior warning run\nnever labeled.","tree":{"sha":"3859d1f26624e4e9bd9e6f13a62e3a2c576addba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3859d1f26624e4e9bd9e6f13a62e3a2c576addba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYjT6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxH0QAHXALU2EsPUkfFCWnQMnypRB\nlVQtE9tna+qkgx8OdDKuLAeFmIIbvuqagxDfNnfBH1nFRUvNnXA4ybSLFTDBma6N\nnkAtheOktHO3R8WiFiey7R7+Pl5snyNDo1Vuv0ewn1WKvHt8zNOhfVR5xTZkrc94\nODNrxdCFPaLmPE8NMPnAkRxu6xEByLQqnhOglB5YMCVBB9zBiakaGb3L/1fEzjJz\nBxa1K35dYy32NRXfctrQp3I8xmP0IhI28PhYRqxekAcI8ipuQBr/CumclIppm6yq\nGnqVZSWvdjAmZ3vmRq5gqxZbNXdVlv4GBNLdzbN+NoH18IQWxd1HpKR6g78mcCMM\n1iIO5idhRFV+8N6HSR/0KiKVdW7d1AFODkYd4PDPbeBqX20a/kU/1d2UaSulV227\ndCym2x0EsmBd2X3fcXouygZl1YLgXv8atSEUZG+e7s4szPqrfkUwzrDF9luKqOzI\nM7ngECUOATtGktYCuJlkXarZTCiITxYyRiZROYz+nyMYmhLEs0uxi+aI0vLmsjhG\nFa4xIzwAD422TIkoIRhNGiRfoxs4UOfNO+14ljL9wngzT/Lm3uYiOtcjAgTYcjKQ\nRPi+1j4AOzvkWvS7b3ZL70A4zK8LcodGbFT5OoNZNmacgoOJgFDlMN1gW9Fvm07I\nnuOvtFZw1fEZSgA2WqHw\n=HJoB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3859d1f26624e4e9bd9e6f13a62e3a2c576addba\nparent 3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784820986 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784820986 -0400\n\nci(infra): apply `pending-deletion` when warning old PRs (#4998)\n\nThe old-PR cleanup workflow already comments when a PR reaches the\nwarning threshold. It now also adds a `pending-deletion` label at that\nsame point so those PRs are easy to find and filter before they\nauto-close.\n\nAlready-warned PRs that are missing the label get it on the next run.\nPRs with `do-not-close` are still skipped entirely.\n\n---\n\nEnsures the repo label exists (yellow) alongside `do-not-close`, applies\nit with the warning comment, and backfills it when a prior warning run\nnever labeled.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T15:36:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/03a651c5f90bcf9622086e1f8d81b462a376cb3f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad"}]},{"sha":"3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM2MDZlM2YzZmEyZmFhYzk3ZjMwMTQxZjllZTU0ZTM3NjMxZDE2YWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T15:24:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T15:24:02Z"},"message":"fix(code): consistent modal backdrop dimming for selectors (#4990)\n\nSome full-screen modals set `background: transparent` on the screen\nroot, which strips Textual's default translucent `ModalScreen` backdrop\n(`background: $background 60%`) and leaves them without the background\ndimming that the model and thread selectors inherit. This restores\nconsistent dimming across these modals.\n\nAffected modals fixed: `/agents` (`AgentSelectorScreen`), `/effort`\n(`EffortSelectorScreen`), and the notification settings dialog\n(`NotificationSettingsScreen`). `ThemeSelectorScreen` intentionally\nkeeps its transparent backdrop so its live theme preview isn't tinted by\nthe dim overlay.\n\nEach fix is covered by a test asserting the screen backdrop alpha is in\n(0, 1) under a non-ansi theme.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e92ee808-0b56-174a-a975-f1caa58dcc59)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f2b8c7c874c60cfd95de2080b406d2c74020a86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9f2b8c7c874c60cfd95de2080b406d2c74020a86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYjISCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADKMQAFmA3Khk3JimxcJCVB8EF7dI\nLG0OuuXnX2OECkM4vLlAk8Jhmyvd06CD6+sZdgRJ3tsS7nYA3SUxFmcQ7kwW+tEj\nTTIrlrjYUoSL3BhZDrS5bPnm/6S/2OmciVhp2obHdzUZsd/lK88RBs4SwLA6L0G8\nevueuHXrFqRCSDbMybU0HlcPujX/Lpnz89/zLUUunlUnlh0LQZq03IWURFbMfN9r\nQGEd9LV+0lb6F92AmNMUSTqGuTUDul54KwZXmFd2MoMGYX5U4MoMbpVzd6DOnMOz\nKu4PCKyBxX5RVnZWUAoW1onMlQDig8QpM2qMpSgbjQLRIoC8cnTiwwzY3z/Ji/Dd\nIy9IHuY6a050yg39GQDjvshMtYNXFXq7q2vdjBHdso/pYC6s0Z15Eu1wRMWMc9Xn\nKpCXigIBHYaB6NHu3dWVWPdSMaI60ZAZ7LQCSzsxJoQ5ADPKHsXn5O5sFO4HOjaQ\nlojdbrEerXfANTAnhlPtrhLGZ3QrDpFIaAakmeD7qsvuGKJwr/4zHSdD3KsghE0x\nFU5gGoZiQwLJ+aV0PeYsK+J0jO4YK76dyPPc+VbYAUPatZnLs3OEhB9IFBs1HM+8\nIIRGTaEu1RmuoVyEkuHN3PAK3ITEFLbCKcRvhTEXBds/nf1MyHJ2q2yQBq8mGuoD\niw+HiUuYX5VUcxE1ZiTf\n=iqIj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f2b8c7c874c60cfd95de2080b406d2c74020a86\nparent db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784820242 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784820242 -0400\n\nfix(code): consistent modal backdrop dimming for selectors (#4990)\n\nSome full-screen modals set `background: transparent` on the screen\nroot, which strips Textual's default translucent `ModalScreen` backdrop\n(`background: $background 60%`) and leaves them without the background\ndimming that the model and thread selectors inherit. This restores\nconsistent dimming across these modals.\n\nAffected modals fixed: `/agents` (`AgentSelectorScreen`), `/effort`\n(`EffortSelectorScreen`), and the notification settings dialog\n(`NotificationSettingsScreen`). `ThemeSelectorScreen` intentionally\nkeeps its transparent backdrop so its live theme preview isn't tinted by\nthe dim overlay.\n\nEach fix is covered by a test asserting the screen backdrop alpha is in\n(0, 1) under a non-ansi theme.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e92ee808-0b56-174a-a975-f1caa58dcc59)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T15:24:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3606e3f3fa2faac97f30141f9ee54e37631d16ad/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4"}]},{"sha":"db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRiMjY2ODhlZWUzMjIzMmExYjczZTk4Y2MwMjY0MmI1YmY0MTY1ZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T15:23:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T15:23:57Z"},"message":"fix(code): omit `plugins/` and `conversation_history/` from `/agent` picker (#4991)\n\nFixed the `/agent` picker listing the app-owned `plugins/` and\n`conversation_history/` directories as selectable agents.\n\n---\n\nThe `/agent` switcher scanned `~/.deepagents/` and listed every\nnon-hidden subdirectory as an agent. App-owned `plugins/` (installed\nplugin state) and `conversation_history/` (offloaded per-thread\narchives) are not agents and were incorrectly surfaced. This reserves\nboth alongside `bin/`, deriving each name from its owning module\n(`plugins.store.DEFAULT_PLUGIN_DIRNAME`,\n`offload.CONVERSATION_HISTORY_DIRNAME`) so the reserved set stays a\nsingle source of truth.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d725141-181b-fa99-add4-a78056113b7a)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d77e1ab2f0ddd7d5630c9631a5057e0e60648ebd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d77e1ab2f0ddd7d5630c9631a5057e0e60648ebd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYjINCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS2YQACJE9bW3wKC3H2juugUjtM/J\nDJZ5eB0Moqv3Ly/RtSW8GXmMJje0Pp5k0qrB5KILtBj8ExOCiSUkENKOcRP4MBbi\nJ7326ltmCu7FK8KlYEZmAt+Dblo9rHYWInwZ3OD1PNPHUQfmt6nKxRsTPhXn9RlQ\nCmcTwn+n6Z+E8ebgmtP+Xyy1UI0kUULkn6Z0H4n7hSvo6UgMXJ/PEnKBUBPxgxym\nnwjewQS50/58hAHZ0cXugD0kw5dXFnZk9KpabBzvPd3YXZaPkFk3kQI1NRMoZhoo\nt8N6xJnRe0PLeOd9fRIH9tFGILy384kHplfIhCh8OyljxxVI9jxuNR//vKNtBAet\nXI8WTbYz85oueEUpfHB+SkSQt4NtVX/xvV8rqjAjIcBH+OIblWd4SpVyr5vC8UFk\n+PvyZLdc/RXC0tVu5Tz1/z1i+u8AT9NPg1sZpB9OHs5e0EHbu7tUjfpfu4gCiy2t\n5qOXQZFEfc5sot/vlJNyF455OJsNUGFxYheonPLoufwR+bM1e2Uf3sw9sY8wCTOc\nVrMgJirzewBOkQF3qhSbbt0TdGPrghcOGNJAUgXJcDCEVqtfWDi9JErPF5QqCGmS\n6TaHUgXp7Iz79BPGD/9FIY3Gz1j8Hd7+o6nMNmCmepOy5QhGOzZcDSwnsURwB4DB\n+LZds8xtokAsn6Mx+HBB\n=40ud\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d77e1ab2f0ddd7d5630c9631a5057e0e60648ebd\nparent 9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784820237 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784820237 -0400\n\nfix(code): omit `plugins/` and `conversation_history/` from `/agent` picker (#4991)\n\nFixed the `/agent` picker listing the app-owned `plugins/` and\n`conversation_history/` directories as selectable agents.\n\n---\n\nThe `/agent` switcher scanned `~/.deepagents/` and listed every\nnon-hidden subdirectory as an agent. App-owned `plugins/` (installed\nplugin state) and `conversation_history/` (offloaded per-thread\narchives) are not agents and were incorrectly surfaced. This reserves\nboth alongside `bin/`, deriving each name from its owning module\n(`plugins.store.DEFAULT_PLUGIN_DIRNAME`,\n`offload.CONVERSATION_HISTORY_DIRNAME`) so the reserved set stays a\nsingle source of truth.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4d725141-181b-fa99-add4-a78056113b7a)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T15:23:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db26688eee32232a1b73e98cc02642b5bf4165f4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxM