-ai/deepagents/commit/9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154"}]},{"sha":"9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkzNDA1MThhMjZjNDI4N2Y5YWQwYzU0M2VkYzliNjkxMDZjMTUxNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shrikar Seshadri","email":"146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-23T14:35:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T14:35:03Z"},"message":"feat(sdk,code,quickjs)!: make the `ToDoListMiddleware` list opt-in (#4929)","tree":{"sha":"407715a6e8b158995a84cdee0e0ca3be76ca920c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/407715a6e8b158995a84cdee0e0ca3be76ca920c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYiaXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARMQQADhc2OB9PrNgyCq+xwNaUvLY\n28pewmDeoz9KY5X2fejpLbt7xlijk59nnxrdGL9uSQXLzJt3Hznv6HkuP1PAsSSq\ngF/JqU2o74zLAT9ij2UJDUwBSskym6JwoyD7/MWIROF+HWCb6ErjA1u5JkA4mleD\nR2rEW5kSrjnDdLLrZjGfFQtnHyCTkDQ6GDHbyxXceLoAlLYR0EUGhU94/7oJbgZO\noPAoC826CMLaHscly0bhuWpus/6NGCjdJvmg0rcPRlHVZV5WyAohWs013LbavG5j\nb8LEuqq4vzWuilMMqicuhPYElVJJpExDwi2paL0ZmztWjDCwPsNOZBWchO3p6KOi\nW27g3cQg8wsN/gxx73M7vIFLFZGIc0GDAAkhTr9PtiT7R9OnuJRXqwM+6eAtv3aI\nULMvkSSt3BfhTvEgfjQMPUTtsRpuWxjHJQF52gYpQXi30nTTzBLVp8QULNLSSiyG\nnGzXQR5jDqo7VeT6jt4Dh/ZPrGwGdZ82RHMYV8NXkNIaWCXcrmXpOqA/VZmin6IA\nUsZJLACnSQesKPu6gWJd4OIwrjtU63JAWpL+x9yL+qrFhwJFnqvS9o9mYIz0IFOn\ncJ5rDFDqbuLr7GSzy4xhRj1Qq2y7rfdVYBVWm0AUxS0TWp3oLvF4Kg0Vuqh/sFF2\nlhoLRYQP1jAmqM8fy0Yt\n=xIih\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 407715a6e8b158995a84cdee0e0ca3be76ca920c\nparent 9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979\nauthor Shrikar Seshadri <146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com> 1784817303 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784817303 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk,code,quickjs)!: make the `ToDoListMiddleware` list opt-in (#4929)","verified_at":"2026-07-23T14:35:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9340518a26c4287f9ad0c543edc9b69106c15154/comments","author":{"login":"davibinboi","id":146694785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL5igQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146694785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi","html_url":"https://github.com/davibinboi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979"}]},{"sha":"9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5NzU4NzRkODk3YWRhODk3OWMwODQxNDVlYjczMGUxNWM5Y2Y5Nzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T13:37:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T13:37:27Z"},"message":"fix(code): avoid redundant Auto approval prompts (#4993)\n\nSupersedes #4946\nSupersedes #4947\n\nAuto mode no longer interrupts users when an action is already covered\nby their explicit `ask_user` selection or when the agent is performing\nthe built-in conversation-compaction operation.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, Auto mode could ask users to approve an action immediately\nafter they selected it in an `ask_user` prompt. It could also pause\nautonomous work to approve `compact_conversation`, even though\ncompaction is an internal maintenance operation without an externally\nconsequential effect.\n\nThe two cases now follow separate trust rules:\n- Server-created, same-turn receipts allow the authorization classifier\nto consider only the user's selected answer for the exact subsequent\naction. The receipt is bound to the LangGraph execution thread, the\nactive turn, and the originating `ask_user` tool call, and is validated\nagainst the full checkpoint history so it survives conversation\ncompaction. Only the latest `ask_user` exchange in the turn is admitted;\nmodel-authored questions, unselected choices, and prior answers are\nexcluded. Invalid, stale, ambiguous, or overly broad consent continues\nthrough the normal approval path.\n- The trusted built-in `compact_conversation` operation is\ndeterministically allowed without classifier or human review. The\nexemption is guarded by exact tool-object identity, not by name, so a\ncaller-supplied tool with the same name cannot exploit it. At most one\ntrusted compaction call is allowed per action batch; duplicates are\ndenied without classifier review, and that denial is preserved across\nall fallback paths.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\nTargeted Auto-mode, ask_user, agent-wiring, and Textual-adapter tests:\n\n```\nuv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/test_ask_user_middleware.py \\\n  tests/unit_tests/test_auto_mode.py \\\n  tests/unit_tests/tui/test_textual_adapter.py::TestExecuteTaskTextualTurnMarkers \\\n  tests/unit_tests/test_agent.py::test_cli_context_schema_fields_mirror_typed_dict \\\n  tests/unit_tests/test_agent.py::TestCreateCliAgentInterpreterWiring \\\n  --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket --benchmark-disable -q\n```\nResult: 135 passed.\n\nFull package unit tests:\n\n```\nmake test\n```\nResult: 10617 passed, 4 skipped, 6 pre-existing failures in\n`TestLangsmithSecretRedaction` (env-dependent, fail on clean\n`origin/main`).\n\nLint, format, type check, and commands catalog:\n\n```\nmake lint\n```\nResult: All checks passed.\n\nA real LangGraph interrupt/resume test\n(`test_real_agent_resume_forwards_ask_user_receipt_to_classifier`)\nverifies the full path: `ask_user` interrupt → checkpoint resume →\nreceipt minting with real `execution_info.thread_id` → classifier sees\n`same_turn_user_answers` → action executes without a second HITL prompt.\n\nA compiled-graph identity test\n(`test_compiled_agent_preserves_canonical_compaction_tool_identity`)\nverifies the canonical `CLICompactionMiddleware` tool object survives\n`create_deep_agent`'s middleware merge into the compiled `ToolNode`, and\nthat `AutoModeHITLMiddleware._trusted_compaction_tool` references that\nsame object.\n\nThe 6 `TestLangsmithSecretRedaction` failures are pre-existing and\nenv-dependent (real LangSmith credentials in the local environment);\nthey fail identically on clean `origin/main` and are unrelated to this\nchange.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"b435999091197d550fbadd0c48d8b66bfa616c6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b435999091197d550fbadd0c48d8b66bfa616c6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYhkXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/VEQAHgywijZ26KrpeYp9gA9NIEg\nudtXqcmSvBEirwu/ZtygaZyEG1sgH7Yj+8eBmiFWPBToSAM1zXAdHrfNlpduZIfP\nrAOUjhif2b4iBMfEZrCwL3t/f/goqXLzUay+8jMsfgUe5NBwWCzEfTgh6ZgwkHrP\nHdCH9Natd3YNhsVceM/wj54BvjDC2tYsKuZ4HswHBMACtSOhfPaPnvO4B1X127vC\nZVbdvsB8TSKMgzhYWhCc+DWN4buCZFYaESYzbCgxXXXXcqgHcc26rOJrR2jQpdN3\nTG4NcVdEb+mbYzu4ZsMRyWB0lsBoki7apRegD3BW2yt0vILmkJGqkxxf/ePaoDlC\nddWsXGkoaQ7ib1CBQDtwOrw3CSJTLNaFhSmFtSDuCmYNJti8lAGaE2mSJvo+FeqC\nfmJwN9sM+agq9tzOjZFz9YurUgt2BHh9j/dy67cIfSmRekpiP1K8rg35xmeDQczU\nXdHOcrYbZsurWS//ujQ6E7+SbbKlaVucyoBVYuic83V0czTeQ/4jcGwQ+F4CLM22\nd3szW4RXMLdwsy1z1JLtFRXMLH/oRcPI6Wg5vANxpkNSwEVFqIgL2q8NeK4wtrpE\nbTVtko+rObzVI0wcbDZsWPYxwjlnfdeaOMCU/72Kqi/HZGc+KhVQ4AfxKpYnC5ME\nZW7uXr6lUHDCkepKCr+e\n=aOm9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b435999091197d550fbadd0c48d8b66bfa616c6a\nparent 0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784813847 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784813847 -0400\n\nfix(code): avoid redundant Auto approval prompts (#4993)\n\nSupersedes #4946\nSupersedes #4947\n\nAuto mode no longer interrupts users when an action is already covered\nby their explicit `ask_user` selection or when the agent is performing\nthe built-in conversation-compaction operation.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, Auto mode could ask users to approve an action immediately\nafter they selected it in an `ask_user` prompt. It could also pause\nautonomous work to approve `compact_conversation`, even though\ncompaction is an internal maintenance operation without an externally\nconsequential effect.\n\nThe two cases now follow separate trust rules:\n- Server-created, same-turn receipts allow the authorization classifier\nto consider only the user's selected answer for the exact subsequent\naction. The receipt is bound to the LangGraph execution thread, the\nactive turn, and the originating `ask_user` tool call, and is validated\nagainst the full checkpoint history so it survives conversation\ncompaction. Only the latest `ask_user` exchange in the turn is admitted;\nmodel-authored questions, unselected choices, and prior answers are\nexcluded. Invalid, stale, ambiguous, or overly broad consent continues\nthrough the normal approval path.\n- The trusted built-in `compact_conversation` operation is\ndeterministically allowed without classifier or human review. The\nexemption is guarded by exact tool-object identity, not by name, so a\ncaller-supplied tool with the same name cannot exploit it. At most one\ntrusted compaction call is allowed per action batch; duplicates are\ndenied without classifier review, and that denial is preserved across\nall fallback paths.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\nTargeted Auto-mode, ask_user, agent-wiring, and Textual-adapter tests:\n\n```\nuv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/test_ask_user_middleware.py \\\n  tests/unit_tests/test_auto_mode.py \\\n  tests/unit_tests/tui/test_textual_adapter.py::TestExecuteTaskTextualTurnMarkers \\\n  tests/unit_tests/test_agent.py::test_cli_context_schema_fields_mirror_typed_dict \\\n  tests/unit_tests/test_agent.py::TestCreateCliAgentInterpreterWiring \\\n  --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket --benchmark-disable -q\n```\nResult: 135 passed.\n\nFull package unit tests:\n\n```\nmake test\n```\nResult: 10617 passed, 4 skipped, 6 pre-existing failures in\n`TestLangsmithSecretRedaction` (env-dependent, fail on clean\n`origin/main`).\n\nLint, format, type check, and commands catalog:\n\n```\nmake lint\n```\nResult: All checks passed.\n\nA real LangGraph interrupt/resume test\n(`test_real_agent_resume_forwards_ask_user_receipt_to_classifier`)\nverifies the full path: `ask_user` interrupt → checkpoint resume →\nreceipt minting with real `execution_info.thread_id` → classifier sees\n`same_turn_user_answers` → action executes without a second HITL prompt.\n\nA compiled-graph identity test\n(`test_compiled_agent_preserves_canonical_compaction_tool_identity`)\nverifies the canonical `CLICompactionMiddleware` tool object survives\n`create_deep_agent`'s middleware merge into the compiled `ToolNode`, and\nthat `AutoModeHITLMiddleware._trusted_compaction_tool` references that\nsame object.\n\nThe 6 `TestLangsmithSecretRedaction` failures are pre-existing and\nenv-dependent (real LangSmith credentials in the local environment);\nthey fail identically on clean `origin/main` and are unrelated to this\nchange.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T13:37:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9975874d897ada8979c084145eb730e15c9cf979/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a"}]},{"sha":"0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBjNDAxNmUzYzhhNzI5M2ZkZjFhMjRlMTIzNDA3NTkwNjhhMmJiOWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T12:54:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T12:54:10Z"},"message":"fix(code,evals): unify goal activation signaling (#4980)\n\nSupersedes #4412\nSupersedes #4944\n\nAccepted goals now transition into agent work through one coordinated\ninternal protocol: a durable notice records the authoritative goal\nstate, while a hidden continuation resumes work without replaying the\nobjective as another user message.\n\n---\n\nThe previous PRs addressed two symptoms at the same transition. #4944\nchanged how work resumes after goal acceptance, while #4412 introduced\npersisted notices that tell the agent when goal tools are relevant.\nLanding them independently would create overlapping internal-message\nlifecycles with separate persistence, restoration, summarization, and\ntranscript-filtering behavior.\n\nThis replacement gives the two message types explicit roles:\n\n- The goal-state notice is the durable source of truth.\n- The continuation is a one-time trigger emitted only after that state\nis available.\n\nIt also handles persistence failure without directing the agent to\nnonexistent saved state and keeps all internal goal-control messages out\nof user-visible and grader transcripts. Goal-specific filtering remains\nin `deepagents-code`; the replacement does not change the Deep Agents\nSDK.","tree":{"sha":"9c69d184df6b40231220cf5db5c30d0cdae0f35d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9c69d184df6b40231220cf5db5c30d0cdae0f35d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYg7yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj5YQAAynRmR0MP4nxuCrNuFKMjQP\n8Mr60wz/ubLuSOPN/fAfnaAuA96hFjcPXHWO7qseZlkduMApy04T4Q9sJdTyXc2W\ncPPIfzbf9m37nLnLM0ms0fll/51tHDoRmP6x0qw/bA9NiXwtManbPAGXmrA2vwEB\n+/Senj2SAqyMUS68MQOwzXEAxFBXXYDUUwu4ETNtvmiCQu02/TkZEewHGXZ4R9WK\nQWpPbvo2MtimOEJJyNFSaHcFCvFbT5UYlqyJToUJ17DszeJptxTeJWzLrsrxopcg\nWH00bc9AU+1Zw83Er5Bc7fQHGUMMBURDwIPOwzDXDuvuNgVBGdrsVDJIHBcgKKA1\nTea8uatuSEQNj+dKtSFlOs7dUJ4LfIJgsXfhvLqb8CA2i/nsLmksd+lcr2MLFFeq\nJ1ZlmJR3v11+BN2peHge1D/BrV/TbN3bAz9QC2QATcWhfZxuRV5uwGjGSeoTzP2x\njpPZ0demVGbge4m55u5PGmYL7CTuy1DnX1h33juwjPecAWkxyEIeBBZaQj6KZ9qr\nPvGGscm9jA+GiSBPez5saF8opyy/eLoShbJQFm+/8Q23w9GfkTwtu4ZmB/kdHflb\njFq9YhFjuwi80+/z6RoNJARtR53NqRtWSBO8lz5hcocZDhwitL1vAGdFBIacYvkb\n7zZ6cuO2xoJZpHVExDiM\n=cFQx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9c69d184df6b40231220cf5db5c30d0cdae0f35d\nparent 9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784811250 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784811250 -0400\n\nfix(code,evals): unify goal activation signaling (#4980)\n\nSupersedes #4412\nSupersedes #4944\n\nAccepted goals now transition into agent work through one coordinated\ninternal protocol: a durable notice records the authoritative goal\nstate, while a hidden continuation resumes work without replaying the\nobjective as another user message.\n\n---\n\nThe previous PRs addressed two symptoms at the same transition. #4944\nchanged how work resumes after goal acceptance, while #4412 introduced\npersisted notices that tell the agent when goal tools are relevant.\nLanding them independently would create overlapping internal-message\nlifecycles with separate persistence, restoration, summarization, and\ntranscript-filtering behavior.\n\nThis replacement gives the two message types explicit roles:\n\n- The goal-state notice is the durable source of truth.\n- The continuation is a one-time trigger emitted only after that state\nis available.\n\nIt also handles persistence failure without directing the agent to\nnonexistent saved state and keeps all internal goal-control messages out\nof user-visible and grader transcripts. Goal-specific filtering remains\nin `deepagents-code`; the replacement does not change the Deep Agents\nSDK.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T12:54:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0c4016e3c8a7293fdf1a24e12340759068a2bb9a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528"}]},{"sha":"9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhMjRiYWZjZDI0NWExOTc4NTY2NDFjODQ0ZGMyZWQ1MTI3NWE1Mjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T12:37:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T12:37:31Z"},"message":"refactor(sdk): correct prompt docs and harden rubric diagnostics (#4989)\n\nCloses #4977\n\n`create_deep_agent` now documents the system prompt it actually sends:\ncaller instructions first, followed by an optional profile base and\nsuffix. Rubric grading also continues if LangChain no longer exposes the\nprivate fallback model list used only for trace diagnostics; those\ndiagnostics report `unknown` instead.\n\n---\n\nThe SDK no longer suggests that `BASE_AGENT_PROMPT` is injected by\ndefault. The public harness-profile API uses the same `USER` → `BASE` →\n`SUFFIX` model and explains how profile content is appended to a\n`SystemMessage` without disturbing cache-control markers.\n\nWhen LangChain’s fallback table is available, rubric trace inference\nretains its existing provider-versus-tool prediction. If the private\nmodule or symbol is unavailable, grading still runs and only that\nprediction is omitted.","tree":{"sha":"b93acf842b41787cc45d3576e7a47007ed8e826a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b93acf842b41787cc45d3576e7a47007ed8e826a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYgsLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGhUQAD9b+64V3e3s3ZW39Y8S6CKG\nhdm+hhgpFTsCUHisMCyFz6KiwIkUiZ2T5OlCPP4TqJk989ANCkZGH6cHvMx5jOHi\noeEKqlj5zv65SSah8R7/tFMHkYJrRQFTG//X4TGSQLxNK81OdX/t90T36tlVND9H\nxttOPMjtnikUqEBchtw2Ev3mfI0ZHpaqecoZw7go0bjwvyaJfNg5yDm2+AhjqEpa\nlh56r6nwbSNy+mVPJ3ykRwvBsYjU/KuWysZ67lAX7kWhvxYjzTI6qeqlUqIrZTOI\nMVPGSEcS1oQoWTklJaiFGY5thyJlPaXCCeDVql57v3n9q0mPOfaa0A0G7rC4ldM2\n12hIgE/B3se1wmpYZo2XD/l4agu+/VhlzcJiPJR5SJyt/iCM3VXaXLN/dEeacKDo\ntjJ45eQJcc+tfyaVmGx79CbonDiWW4JeRgYTEcelrOccB3/SkNJKv03KSVqH7Qxz\ndOsaeCHPMkTULC5zgUeFmM14XcpXjRYdGIYqUXFOHv7iqJLXc4NHad/EiXMV75L2\nKBRfS5sKXPvYQ9aKA5+c3ABgl4SMh2zfpqtzh6ciREx/vJiR+xtmihZlcv6Aqo26\njwQG3LQ/s47ry6Sqb826c7wJ1uQ1810jIOR55OUpRKhouveXCh3G42sJqROO/maM\nWPsGzvreQwA/+J5+7OfU\n=A4bv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b93acf842b41787cc45d3576e7a47007ed8e826a\nparent 4b2ea36fbfceb6151f3b092e7c88da6052712a5d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784810251 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784810251 -0400\n\nrefactor(sdk): correct prompt docs and harden rubric diagnostics (#4989)\n\nCloses #4977\n\n`create_deep_agent` now documents the system prompt it actually sends:\ncaller instructions first, followed by an optional profile base and\nsuffix. Rubric grading also continues if LangChain no longer exposes the\nprivate fallback model list used only for trace diagnostics; those\ndiagnostics report `unknown` instead.\n\n---\n\nThe SDK no longer suggests that `BASE_AGENT_PROMPT` is injected by\ndefault. The public harness-profile API uses the same `USER` → `BASE` →\n`SUFFIX` model and explains how profile content is appended to a\n`SystemMessage` without disturbing cache-control markers.\n\nWhen LangChain’s fallback table is available, rubric trace inference\nretains its existing provider-versus-tool prediction. If the private\nmodule or symbol is unavailable, grading still runs and only that\nprediction is omitted.","verified_at":"2026-07-23T12:37:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9a24bafcd245a197856641c844dc2ed51275a528/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4b2ea36fbfceb6151f3b092e7c88da6052712a5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4b2ea36fbfceb6151f3b092e7c88da6052712a5d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4b2ea36fbfceb6151f3b092e7c88da6052712a5d"}]},{"sha":"4b2ea36fbfceb6151f3b092e7c88da6052712a5d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRiMmVhMzZmYmZjZWI2MTUxZjNiMDkyZTdjODhkYTYwNTI3MTJhNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-23T07:31:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T07:31:55Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/partners/runloop (#4984)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<u