utomerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T07:16:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f1105ec1b3930796b255467dd10e265300f6968","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9f1105ec1b3930796b255467dd10e265300f6968","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f1105ec1b3930796b255467dd10e265300f6968/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14"}]},{"sha":"c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM3YTYxODBiNmFkMWQ0NGRhMDFlMWQxMmM0NDIwYWJlZjRkZTNjMTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-23T07:16:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T07:16:27Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/partners/quickjs (#4985)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"4884c6a7db271ef28f34035c4f47b80555eb21c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4884c6a7db271ef28f34035c4f47b80555eb21c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYb/LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPhkQAHOV9skt3JJ1w3xtNeTlF2X9\nn5DItYUcpfgYr+F2YslcpCYw2vwH4UESOI1PTT+q7riGyQeFuPimifObE31zt4Wo\nrEzsG5t3kdc+Lvq1wEBWzOZivCCrYwS2erJ5npVZFsC/bbh0Byi6L8BPBbC8MDjj\nNqZMvBgUIZ/EZmMfEK5+80VGmz/jEXvAFFV7fP72ziGWOCM8z9dzBNBZzGamPGGy\n66d95PsighAZtqddYrzB20LkxvwePiqVInWehFfbobzsm6IWBuu9/mw+gSC44GBa\nw7ipC8TTVmcd06OtE9orndeoBlmjhEFN31CPbu7gUllyW2gEskXa4lSA07Kys3sA\nlkSYS8/iBcS3UwDP11TZ6w87ySg/oVr+tzvbmmgFQ0jXeUIeGpLeCs8NBV+gYpPV\nRXtHw5n3NDBUV7u2N4Fzurqnd+GMlbBe56BApWHbzNOSmrc0bE6rIIifmM2+q6rc\nVd/cxt/H6/TaiGl+wmyu5ObKLg9vIFad0F/xYrPkuVI8ymCgDQv15lAwluAGRlGP\nd7+giZvOQHVAsiCCF1AHSGOBLr1ct1VDEfw8ii5HI9k08W2wLUwSBrHI+2MPsUyU\n9IR8bfVkRbYF/9BsU10nWZu7JPP2XSh9U0HxkLUCJTd1UXzhhUxVLBgn1teJjNxu\nckiFQszpJXVlzcVCM652\n=vIsC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4884c6a7db271ef28f34035c4f47b80555eb21c1\nparent a50ac5459e04839e6bccd373dd337513b5569379\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784790987 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784790987 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/partners/quickjs (#4985)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T07:16:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c4420abef4de3c14","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c7a6180b6ad1d44da01e1d12c442