th large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"88e4e302a349e6bc2910f360bd01e775b92e9204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/88e4e302a349e6bc2910f360bd01e775b92e9204"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/70c285f1dedc788acf852449d5cf81fcdcdded63","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYb73CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWZQQAFfWNiHVlf1Axt+YCMfI1nO1\n6pAQ5ewXgyn5THL0q6FOTslXlCBtYctBXSFe8ziv8ooGXGVzXYa4eWRfve+D35np\nnIot3HAaPogJ2cqvjLt3HxfINHuodLQM0Lk8tCqcgFyHC1v3oS1MkiFaRkmhDYIX\nJupJgwV/ZMpgikdJVtuslyvultppe9hEJPam5BFcVspf5mCvYt6Chjc0haU7DsxS\nLSuKdmnZ2awARvuLMqf3xZ8HlWHLhoTzeyYt1vIr/uYg55BAYDRaxEufh9yM5Ep6\n8DlrDRdNIt5hYzvVTsHLbNBNWGEgrVuk/gy2dq04k8sCnjf5pgB1vn/guVmkowqp\n7sJbNuwLTSxVWI82idWGnLV1mLD06ABkLZzOoUL0gGT1TlVL4mThDjwIu+cl+x6A\nVtuIbSvNd2VDr/9ggA7BWow+/ePSTvkQNhWVMWxa9paDovF3PCPb5sOHDQEMQuFd\nLpR6YeC1NN5rVf7xRnPynFFMB73x0vutmyM98lxV8xSsy3A1p86NspbRoyRRh4K3\ndNtCA5G0+OClwKYFtd0WOMNL46re6S4EGc77CFQa+8yiuDEjM9kQCCFQCad/Tuo4\nQU+PnwhfsocuoJON3V4T2gjpzO9RkN7IzdVeltTgOhLjvfLAXL0RT6LJZlxf/QEB\nyKgygDeQp/EXsF2WZDKA\n=6vI3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 88e4e302a349e6bc2910f360bd01e775b92e9204\nparent fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784790775 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784790775 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/partners/modal (#4986)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T07:12:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70c285f1dedc788acf852449d5cf81fcdcdded63","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/70c285f1dedc788acf852449d5cf81fcdcdded63","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70c285f1dedc788acf852449d5cf81fcdcdded63/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c"}]},{"sha":"fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZiNzlkZDc0MGE5ZDJmNTRjNjMxMmU1ZGU3ODlhMjE3YzYzYjZhOWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-23T07:12:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T07:12:48Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/partners/daytona (#4987)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4845252fd03ab783b2bc80279f75d07e2f9565af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4845252fd03ab783b2bc80279f75d07e2f9565af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYb7wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATQkQAKXJndO6zbFI411DWgqKh0RE\nVv37W54G8D6wqxP2Ajjmio8gaIV1qt0ymjpTap1lFRIOHAWkkchUD3q5EeJqKs0l\nJ0gWascG715BeXRXZ9odPfGcaOVA8rsCFgVkmKpOHMvJ0K0xM1IaDrMSg6R9N3zd\njBMm5K9Izj53gjHSO0RmV8BEJsrkB4pMsPvf7atAIRSaRgqWKwCYYfXCvj9Bq7ZV\nIWshurikJXxaZoym3wYbx8LHRYPggxRgEu9ZN8KS+YKlx6gxHZpjtGbrAlfw7nty\n2xOrH7nG2FM9Rg8Zzhtau7hv1K+Doxpj8XeQFK6RXGFx6h32AaDiM8S5y54oqSpm\nrUAMpDvcjH4unsebAxZcpzexSCc7QHk64vGsAvttEk0Vtdwy8h1OQvSMMr3T+vH2\nZJZMzZOha8XiMlc5E+4jQmZErQ5A3N0o7JSYaSzlfs/qNDKHWreraFAhs7vfMjsJ\n50uu5ncHqBkoTlVmphB5mJCW/CnDSbe3bNdoXuylOMGfkMBt+dRfpRX/9t3AAPes\niawAEbqPqcUOTLB7uT4XmZnrW7l/t3a3QWsXlUYYipCV0wWN1YtNkZZo9PVX+TEG\n7kuclRx0QwvzfZkk/DGyeEtsTpEKp+BkGtp/dYayWSYfRwYMG+2HUwRxyvPvLb3l\nBQ5ygrIvHICzQGFfni0n\n=m2Iu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4845252fd03ab783b2bc80279f75d07e2f9565af\nparent 05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784790768 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784790768 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyasn1 from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4 in /libs/partners/daytona (#4987)\n\nBumps [pyasn1](https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1) from 0.6.3 to 0.6.4.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases\">pyasn1's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Release 0.6.4</h2>\n<p>This is a security release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders. A small\ncrafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume excessive CPU.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag IDs\nto 20 octets (140 bits). Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate\nto consume excessive CPU and memory.</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and CPU\nconsumption in <code>Real.__float__()</code> for values with large\nbase-10 exponents.</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All changes are noted in the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/blob/main/CHANGES.rst\">pyasn1's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Revision 0.6.4, released 08-07-2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-59885 (GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj): Fixed quadratic time\ncomplexity in the OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID decoders.\nA small crafted substrate encoding many arcs could consume\nexcessive CPU. Arcs are now accumulated in linear time; decoded\nvalues are unchanged (thanks for reporting, tynus2)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59884 (GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j): Limited BER long-form tag\nIDs to 20 octets (140 bits), matching the OID arc limit introduced\nin 0.6.2. Unbounded tag IDs allowed a crafted substrate to consume\nexcessive CPU and memory; longer tag IDs are now rejected with\nPyAsn1Error. Also fixed Tag and TagSet repr() failing on huge tag\n(thanks for reporting, mikeappsec)\nIDs due to the integer-to-string conversion limit (Python 3.11+)</li>\n<li>CVE-2026-59886 (GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r): Fixed excessive memory and\nCPU consumption in Real.<strong>float</strong>() for values with large\nbase-10\nexponents. Conversion no longer materializes huge intermediate\nintegers; values too large to represent as a Python float raise\nOverflowError promptly, and prettyPrint() renders them as\n'<!-- raw HTML omitted -->' as before. Also fixed base-10 mantissa\nnormalization\nto use exact integer arithmetic; mantissas larger than 2**53\ncould previously lose precision through float division\n(thanks for reporting, gvozdila)</li>\n<li>Pinned PyPI publish GitHub Action to an immutable commit\n[pr <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/pull/113\">pyasn1/pyasn1#113</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/72e4803405816c371ed3b2cb4be181c47f038406\"><code>72e4803</code></a>\nPrepare release 0.6.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/0c19eeb853731db1c717ff125ea001a1e558332d\"><code>0c19eeb</code></a>\nPin PyPI publish action to immutable commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/issues/113\">#113</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/45bdb19eb7df4b3780fe9c912c63e99bffc39dd9\"><code>45bdb19</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/628e36ecbb5277a3f01572ce418ef54271b165a5\"><code>628e36e</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/commit/e60c691cb91addb8fcefa2f537e85ede6fb1e886\"><code>e60c691</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/compare/v0.6.3...v0.6.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyasn1&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.6.3&new-version=0.6.4)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T07:12:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fb79dd740a9d2f54c6312e5de789a217c63b6a9c/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326"}]},{"sha":"05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA1ZGQwZDFiZWU3ZDc5YmU2YWM3ZjE4ZGIwZDA1YjUyMWU3NjAzMjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-23T00:39:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T00:39:06Z"},"message":"fix(code): harden Hooks v2 command execution (#4917)\n\nDepends on #4916\nRelated DCD-70\n\nHooks v2 command handlers now execute with event-aware policies, bounded\nterminal output, sanitized environments, and complete process cleanup.\n\n---\n\nThis is 2/3 in the DCD-70 stack.\n\n- Applies plain-output, exit-code, continuation, permission, and\ndeferred-field policies without discarding sibling diagnostics.\n- Validates terminal sequences and removes ambient secret and telemetry\nenvironment values.\n- Cleans up complete process groups on timeout or cancellation and maps\nnative/MCP tool calls only from trustworthy metadata.\n- Keeps materialized filesystem paths outside domain and transport\nstate.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 95 passed at\nthis stack layer\n- `make lint`\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - **fix(code): harden Hooks v2 command execution** :point_left:\n    - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4918\n      - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4971\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->","tree":{"sha":"6a8f67a34ed6a3b21fee16a22cd003fd5dbe0328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6a8f67a34ed6a3b21fee16a22cd003fd5dbe0328"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYWKqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjf0QAG6OAXQvDnhbiJwJSgB9jsSw\ntHo5AhutbWp2Kfz5dU7sMADf0I/3whv5ZrDSlMvgPBjSn/FT2taHcc+EB+wJj0ud\nAOzPty5+/GiJWMaESxrQxnqUHqx0LcRHQL6ct5ldKXHb1ncZ2pvV7IKEeFPj55db\nxYxukg5kpbEDx8ycJp/ZM9JflvEFlSdrswW3XJ9H1w5bj0zGSPJcNtrbr5DMOI76\nOqUm2zc6GV5eK1+D8Q6JfTdMB2xGKAufKFJ+SYjnqZXvRHo9BLhm5zJwLJkGn5l+\nLiiBaokNLGWjmlM4HXdH9zJhwiETziuPZLJpqdjYdwP895VqDZcA8W0BKByy2hDG\nU52OyKPdhMLRah2OvqENdtkXyDfSvCZktJUg87pSKKZNv+Hii3xTwrdyJqiL5Cq6\n4FKczfBBMI/CERGqj4mtZXncsG20ZcY5GF1bmxY+ebP+EEaErJ4vCR0ncGAfEOK6\n4C0so6hv2LHtOY6BgYI8t45qlNExWK/IydZXGs8izJJev0fI3boWjKYWQNOCDmNk\nsA3+WUSj1k7kn5syuigLtAdar314Tw32IFUZ2URSKfJmA0UwgxtaN3Gep0SYxcKr\nBIRYsx17cS1umpNavugR3TDf4uka1+WwR5wTB6P37RdMy4yfWQ7O41O/OmCB8SkW\np7zXzL1SEp1v2vjrYPJE\n=VjNx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6a8f67a34ed6a3b21fee16a22cd003fd5dbe0328\nparent add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1784767146 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784767146 -0700\n\nfix(code): harden Hooks v2 command execution (#4917)\n\nDepends on #4916\nRelated DCD-70\n\nHooks v2 command handlers now execute with event-aware policies, bounded\nterminal output, sanitized environments, and complete process cleanup.\n\n---\n\nThis is 2/3 in the DCD-70 stack.\n\n- Applies plain-output, exit-code, continuation, permission, and\ndeferred-field policies without discarding sibling diagnostics.\n- Validates terminal sequences and removes ambient secret and telemetry\nenvironment values.\n- Cleans up complete process groups on timeout or cancellation and maps\nnative/MCP tool calls only from trustworthy metadata.\n- Keeps materialized filesystem paths outside domain and transport\nstate.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 95 passed at\nthis stack layer\n- `make lint`\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - **fix(code): harden Hooks v2 command execution** :point_left:\n    - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4918\n      - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4971\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->","verified_at":"2026-07-23T00:39:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/05dd0d1bee7d79be6ac7f18db0d05b521e760326/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d"}]},{"sha":"add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFkZDk0ZmJhYjdkMWI3M2E4OGI1YjgzYTg0ZWEwY2FjYWFkYTllM2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shrikar Seshadri","email":"146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-23T00:06:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T00:06:37Z"},"message":"feat(evals): add comparison reports to A/B testing GitHub action summary (#4872)\n\n## Workflow\n1. Before running evals, the workflow creates the list `expected_leaves`\nof every test combination it expects. Each item, also called a `leaf`,\ncontains:\n  -  branch\n  - SHA: the exact commit from that branch\n  - model\n  - config: how the agent is set up, such as bare, dcode, or tau3\n- category: the type of evaluation tasks it will run (autonomous,\nconversational, or context)\n2. Harbor runs each planned combination seperately (unchanged), and each\nrun produces files containing:\n  - overall scores for that leaf in `summary.json`\n  - individual task scores for that leaf in `per_task.jsonl`\n3. Comparator script groups results together and determines which leaves\nto compare:\n- Cross-branch comparison: compare two branches while keeping the model\nand config identical.\n- Config comparison: compare two configs on the same branch and model,\nbut only for evaluation categories that both configs ran.\n4. Creates an artifact named unified-comparison, which reports:\n  - Which baseline and candidate are being compared.\n  - Changes in pass@k and avg@k for each shared evaluation category.\n- Counts of task-level wins, losses, ties, and missing results per\ncategory.\n- Whether the comparison is complete or affected by missing\ninfrastructure results.\n- Config pairs that were not compared because they ran no categories in\ncommon.\n\n\n## What this PR adds:\n\n- Adds deterministic cross-branch score deltas while holding model and\nconfig constant.\n- Adds within-branch config comparisons over only their shared\ncategories.\n- Never compares different models or changes the branch and config\nsimultaneously.\n- Recomputes category, macro, and task-weighted micro metrics over the\nshared comparison scope.\n- Reports per-task wins, losses, ties, and missing tasks from the\ncandidate's perspective.\n- Records config pairs without shared categories as `not_comparable`\ninstead of producing misleading deltas.\n- Verifies actual result SHAs against the immutable source allocation\nfrom prep.\n- Marks comparisons incomplete only when their coverage or per-task data\nis missing or untrustworthy (so AgentTimeoutErrors and\nNonZeroAgentExitCodeErrors with data will be counted as failures, not\nerrors).\n- Adds test coverage for the current bare/dcode/tau3 allocation,\nmultiple models and branches, incomplete data, SHA mismatches, and\nfuture conversation-capable configs.\n\n### Improvements from Nick's suggestions:\n- Changed post-run analysis to best-effort - missing or malformed data\nnow produces warnings and incomplete reports instead of stopping the\nworkflow.\n- Preserves trustworthy summary scores while excluding malformed\ntask-level data from comparisons (keeps them clean).\n  - Adds structured issues to leaf, unified, and comparison reports.\n- Always produces comparison JSON and Markdown, even when results are\nincomplete or nothing is comparable.\n- Continues analysis after artifact-download retries are exhausted,\npreserving any available results.\n  - Leaves Harbor retry and timeout behavior unchanged.\n  - Adds exact task filtering for small, targeted A/B runs.\n- Prevents optional UV-cache cleanup from falsely failing comparison\njobs.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The comparator reads the Harbor artifacts already downloaded by the\ncombine job\n- No config-routing changes. `expected_leaves` remains the authority for\nwhich configs ran which categories\n- Recorded agent timeouts and nonzero exits continue to score as failed\nrollouts rather than incomplete data\n- Single-subject runs do not publish an unnecessary comparison artifact\n- No retry/timeout controls or LangSmith usage/cost analysis yet\n- No LLM-based semantic trajectory analysis (could be added in the\nfuture)\n\n## Tests\n\n- All 618 GitHub script tests passed.\n- 90 focused comparison, aggregation, and workflow tests passed.\n- Ruff checks passed on all changed Python files.\n- Focused `ty` checks passed.\n- The modified workflow YAML parsed successfully.\n\n# Working Example:\n\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/29799438205","tree":{"sha":"1447d53c682799a719a79d134fae6ac1fcc363a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1447d53c682799a719a79d134fae6ac1fcc363a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYVsOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9nwQAA68vWyfd26b25pYaDh2S+fL\n5Dbwk0iR5GEidbgQcoX5OFjMd20bzHAX013gdj2IghFobQiXVYuFk17hJ0mzBDGP\nND0KbrYoS2HS8gw4Ial0Y2jlgk7SdrL5OJD1kQXL/pKH4+TKyNFlw1wb+rhW1FWI\nomAQSi1f55VJ3eoBAyTrVfBW5V3JTG1XodLAnXXKaj93wv5m1yxdnna/jUS3aLp0\nAnas4YIy6TsSDSBIaid1qSgGWoDcPDyfDSoX8eKFmpmTp9p/EADucxH+dJEXklPd\naMsQtMy4SVCLtMYe/uaqT7nVKBax3qTiQybs/nZTqFg4UGQSsWNR9ZEww6eJ0ywL\nYaXBWuQFgOTSNPbQcRsMZEuc91z5gEAZ4iW0NLTvvjCe7vvJB+Jvx/S8ohfSYL+O\nnY3f8Es43wjRzlgUaGWVfIjS4jQrJQaLDHp9J6W5YjpbRsu5wStQl13xnKonovtG\n4U1nhlUEvtVrAH0y4TLDe/OkduYfSJEXZbwGe5+9n2i61iuyH3HPi0ml1T/DGJyl\nkISryDnn/aiP+KK7Z/ixeRVR3IGsNnicrRrCRXcQa/I7BuE8LpIm9M0wni11N6CD\nL2vh6P2qxGWqYFQIIypYyxKBeINryXcs9xtLP/rTRnXFknQMNDfeCmoFdPTvBLOR\nVgKqvGDQt0FM2RiDocUY\n=6PG+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1447d53c682799a719a79d134fae6ac1fcc363a3\nparent 5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22\nauthor Shrikar Seshadri <146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com> 1784765197 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784765197 -0700\n\nfeat(evals): add comparison reports to A/B testing GitHub action summary (#4872)\n\n## Workflow\n1. Before running evals, the workflow creates the list `expected_leaves`\nof every test combination it expects. Each item, also called a `leaf`,\ncontains:\n  -  branch\n  - SHA: the exact commit from that branch\n  - model\n  - config: how the agent is set up, such as bare, dcode, or tau3\n- category: the type of evaluation tasks it will run (autonomous,\nconversational, or context)\n2. Harbor runs each planned combination seperately (unchanged), and each\nrun produces files containing:\n  - overall scores for that leaf in `summary.json`\n  - individual task scores for that leaf in `per_task.jsonl`\n3. Comparator script groups results together and determines which leaves\nto compare:\n- Cross-branch comparison: compare two branches while keeping the model\nand config identical.\n- Config comparison: compare two configs on the same branch and model,\nbut only for evaluation categories that both configs ran.\n4. Creates an artifact named unified-comparison, which reports:\n  - Which baseline and candidate are being compared.\n  - Changes in pass@k and avg@k for each shared evaluation category.\n- Counts of task-level wins, losses, ties, and missing results per\ncategory.\n- Whether the comparison is complete or affected by missing\ninfrastructure results.\n- Config pairs that were not compared because they ran no categories in\ncommon.\n\n\n## What this PR adds:\n\n- Adds deterministic cross-branch score deltas while holding model and\nconfig constant.\n- Adds within-branch config comparisons over only their shared\ncategories.\n- Never compares different models or changes the branch and config\nsimultaneously.\n- Recomputes category, macro, and task-weighted micro metrics over the\nshared comparison scope.\n- Reports per-task wins, losses, ties, and missing tasks from the\ncandidate's perspective.\n- Records config pairs without shared categories as `not_comparable`\ninstead of producing misleading deltas.\n- Verifies actual result SHAs against the immutable source allocation\nfrom prep.\n- Marks comparisons incomplete only when their coverage or per-task data\nis missing or untrustworthy (so AgentTimeoutErrors and\nNonZeroAgentExitCodeErrors with data will be counted as failures, not\nerrors).\n- Adds test coverage for the current bare/dcode/tau3 allocation,\nmultiple models and branches, incomplete data, SHA mismatches, and\nfuture conversation-capable configs.\n\n### Improvements from Nick's suggestions:\n- Changed post-run analysis to best-effort - missing or malformed data\nnow produces warnings and incomplete reports instead of stopping the\nworkflow.\n- Preserves trustworthy summary scores while excluding malformed\ntask-level data from comparisons (keeps them clean).\n  - Adds structured issues to leaf, unified, and comparison reports.\n- Always produces comparison JSON and Markdown, even when results are\nincomplete or nothing is comparable.\n- Continues analysis after artifact-download retries are exhausted,\npreserving any available results.\n  - Leaves Harbor retry and timeout behavior unchanged.\n  - Adds exact task filtering for small, targeted A/B runs.\n- Prevents optional UV-cache cleanup from falsely failing comparison\njobs.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The comparator reads the Harbor artifacts already downloaded by the\ncombine job\n- No config-routing changes. `expected_leaves` remains the authority for\nwhich configs ran which categories\n- Recorded agent timeouts and nonzero exits continue to score as failed\nrollouts rather than incomplete data\n- Single-subject runs do not publish an unnecessary comparison artifact\n- No retry/timeout controls or LangSmith usage/cost analysis yet\n- No LLM-based semantic trajectory analysis (could be added in the\nfuture)\n\n## Tests\n\n- All 618 GitHub script tests passed.\n- 90 focused comparison, aggregation, and workflow tests passed.\n- Ruff checks passed on all changed Python files.\n- Focused `ty` checks passed.\n- The modified workflow YAML parsed successfully.\n\n# Working Example:\n\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/29799438205","verified_at":"2026-07-23T00:06:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/add94fbab7d1b73a88b5b83a84ea0cacaada9e3d/comments","author":{"login":"davibinboi","id":146694785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL5igQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146694785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi","html_url":"https://github.com/davibinboi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22"}]},{"sha":"5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVkY2Y3NDlhNmU3ZDVhYjY2MTFmMzBkNDg1YTMzODJjN2VmMzFmMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T23:52:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T23:52:18Z"},"message":"feat(code): let the rubric grader inspect working-directory files (#4835)\n\nLong-running tasks can now be graded against the final repository and\nconnected read-only state, rather than only a bounded conversation\nexcerpt. This prevents completed work from being marked incomplete after\nthe supporting evidence scrolls out of the grader's transcript context.\n\n---\n\n## Before and after\n\n**Before**\n\nThe completion grader received the original request and a bounded tail\nof the conversation, but it could not inspect the resulting files or\nconnected systems.\n\n- A task asks the agent to update `src/config.py` and create\n`docs/setup.md`.\n- The agent makes and verifies both changes, then continues through a\nlong debugging conversation.\n- By the time grading runs, the relevant tool results are no longer in\nthe retained transcript excerpt.\n- The grader cannot confirm either file and may report the criteria as\nunmet.\n\n**After**\n\nThe completion grader can inspect the final state with bounded,\nread-only tools.\n\n- It uses `read_file` or `glob` to verify `src/config.py` and\n`docs/setup.md` inside the effective working directory.\n- If a criterion concerns an external result, such as a Notion update,\nit can use the same filtered external context available while proposing\ncriteria: `fetch_url`, optional `web_search`, and MCP tools that are\nconsistently annotated as read-only.\n- It grades the criterion from the verified final state even when the\noriginal execution evidence is no longer present in the transcript\nexcerpt.\n\nRepository verification is limited to `ls`, `read_file`, `glob`, and\n`grep`; it does not give the grader shell access or the ability to run\ntests. Access remains subject to the configured filesystem-tool\nallowlist and requires a trusted local or sandbox working-directory\nroot. Path traversal and symlink escapes are rejected, and unknown\nsandbox types fail closed without repository tools.\n\nExternal verification follows the active approval mode. Approval\nrequests from nested grading runs pause and resume through the parent\ngraph, using the same live runtime context as the task agent.\nConfigurations that disable HITL remain uninterrupted. In normal server\nwiring, mutating or ambiguously annotated MCP tools are excluded.\n\nEach grading iteration has bounded call, web-search, and\naccumulated-result budgets. Repository operations also cap file size,\nlines read, directory entries, matches, and returned characters so\nverification cannot grow without limit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9ce56a7b16ca9b1d8494941f4b6d0b140896ef0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a9ce56a7b16ca9b1d8494941f4b6d0b140896ef0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYVeyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI20QAARYXgQOFG5WNEVzY94S6SIS\ntdTA8e9/DkNRoJx7rel1vrQ7klEAUgYSCTQrWcQBSzIM4ap9hfFL+dmwe3fGl6z2\nuYFYomhp48UC2czjLvxHbT31zor6gF9g3scBO6j8loV/VVzxlE8a2pwzz47+nt/B\n9tCMNFyMU6+b7MIEWeNCvByf5WVjQ57clASin+COeMV0/3byM3XOvvh4mtMswsKZ\nuAueeWTcbGnhGrnilj+Ey1WHR3cCOvvbsW5/fGwvQOhd4lUqYU0w1PLLPhgsaZay\nN3/ns0+hlGqVZggdFy1xf+o6Ox5U6q2r7VDyDPGKCerIJXlgDVSHfx0vwsV5WazP\nyED4bhiUy4tK08R39FzCtyFD2IQsIcwN9rD8aatCtHszDsS7V7iQe/moQDv2kydi\nqPRMdyJIRjWKBm+g0qCrYgSMhAPjcDeunH+lvU5MHzdLs9DWM+C0FKnJJ+rlX2D+\nspnuxtqCGzhsvgbgv7n7etwDZ7It39aYsUkxt2zGsHzUh65Y2MJER2HiX/x8zTfH\n/J6jnYejCwsO9JlMp71DLMM1Axxf0es//x6QtoUqvFMWMCDvNoVwn+Yevcc2rsXK\npLWzdvOV7amWeUTsh6W9Yh9er/Nmu10axFATWVjJ9BgU/ymP2zNbjOyGl28XC3un\nFyw+8z3UaU+TdwnnCDWu\n=F1hJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a9ce56a7b16ca9b1d8494941f4b6d0b140896ef0\nparent 465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784764338 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784764338 -0400\n\nfeat(code): let the rubric grader inspect working-directory files (#4835)\n\nLong-running tasks can now be graded against the final repository and\nconnected read-only state, rather than only a bounded conversation\nexcerpt. This prevents completed work from being marked incomplete after\nthe supporting evidence scrolls out of the grader's transcript context.\n\n---\n\n## Before and after\n\n**Before**\n\nThe completion grader received the original request and a bounded tail\nof the conversation, but it could not inspect the resulting files or\nconnected systems.\n\n- A task asks the agent to update `src/config.py` and create\n`docs/setup.md`.\n- The agent makes and verifies both changes, then continues through a\nlong debugging conversation.\n- By the time grading runs, the relevant tool results are no longer in\nthe retained transcript excerpt.\n- The grader cannot confirm either file and may report the criteria as\nunmet.\n\n**After**\n\nThe completion grader can inspect the final state with bounded,\nread-only tools.\n\n- It uses `read_file` or `glob` to verify `src/config.py` and\n`docs/setup.md` inside the effective working directory.\n- If a criterion concerns an external result, such as a Notion update,\nit can use the same filtered external context available while proposing\ncriteria: `fetch_url`, optional `web_search`, and MCP tools that are\nconsistently annotated as read-only.\n- It grades the criterion from the verified final state even when the\noriginal execution evidence is no longer present in the transcript\nexcerpt.\n\nRepository verification is limited to `ls`, `read_file`, `glob`, and\n`grep`; it does not give the grader shell access or the ability to run\ntests. Access remains subject to the configured filesystem-tool\nallowlist and requires a trusted local or sandbox working-directory\nroot. Path traversal and symlink escapes are rejected, and unknown\nsandbox types fail closed without repository tools.\n\nExternal verification follows the active approval mode. Approval\nrequests from nested grading runs pause and resume through the parent\ngraph, using the same live runtime context as the task agent.\nConfigurations that disable HITL remain uninterrupted. In normal server\nwiring, mutating or ambiguously annotated MCP tools are excluded.\n\nEach grading iteration has bounded call, web-search, and\naccumulated-result budgets. Repository operations also cap file size,\nlines read, directory entries, matches, and returned characters so\nverification cannot grow without limit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T23:52:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5dcf749a6e7d5ab6611f30d485a3382c7ef31f22/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4"}]},{"sha":"465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2NWI5ZGUxN2Y5ZjRlNmNkMDdhODY3NGQ5YTE4NmU2MGY1YmY0ZDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T22:21:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T22:21:08Z"},"message":"fix(code): show rubric grader defaults (#4966)\n\n`/goal show` and `/rubric show` now report the rubric grader's startup\nchat model and concrete default maximum iteration count, rather than\nimplying that per-turn `/model` changes affect the grader or leaving the\ndefault unspecified.\n\n---\n\nThe rubric middleware keeps the model chosen when the local server is\nconstructed, while `/model` only changes the configurable chat model for\nlater turns. Capturing that startup model keeps the displayed settings\naligned with actual grading behavior.\n\nThe SDK's default iteration count remains duplicated in the\ndependency-light display path to preserve startup performance. A drift\ntest compares it with the middleware default so the displayed value\ncannot silently become stale.\n\nAI assistance was used to implement and prepare this contribution.","tree":{"sha":"48ae6b90460e589e5f2cb8acd9200b9a4eb3b68b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/48ae6b90460e589e5f2cb8acd9200b9a4eb3b68b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYUJVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX90QAFpkDK3YgbjTyITSJUF44mfc\nNx66daozbmh0cUlr4nVxBLiSW9ZlRmyActdBc5EvZXZ00Ws/kbZlPTNy7w/0stYJ\n5scotnVr1uKq242VhDXVdKX9+ww73ap71GxhIs1Dk14DhPp42x0VycFFGUrO5ssC\nGiIh44D1hW+c7wry2VGNlcOAdNanGh4JvCuNLe52TjAFR6h8OGWau0E0BXsvw9qH\nl8yQmxFfbdvmjFBGpWdbNPqiJO5K9ki5IW6Aw1X1YAuFwCiMsEfA/2yoNLPaSWtw\nYAck4/Y8DlHoae7kLl9iEnKT/GP++pa4tKMHOsj6+jPlwMskYwfrlmTB1G9DZStU\n2YCITqVEEwYwbCOgl2e1Lx9NPc6wBRd6moLfclGb7/Ew+28SpPBSez8hsiF5cNbs\n40XcSlO4YZhur9lxZLStjpeCPB72GpBXpg+k3x7eoCZFKta5l75JCh6maG7VEySj\nmCuEve4cWt693m0COZCTCIVwvOHFNOubBU4VEreTyN2atgktNzGH8yU0DoBPcYhp\nUugBGZ0M+wsfgEiiI2MKURV65VeaOtVaLXovs19BJ42zSmwdSoBnZgfFwnLZe6qy\nH7T0RnqdDqPtEDJSD7gE5+x0R7pZTE1r28RuJnwlVU3WloSPP93OnJ4bC72Uyj3n\nA3yKHnR097KNma4qEA02\n=to1Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 48ae6b90460e589e5f2cb8acd9200b9a4eb3b68b\nparent d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784758868 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784758868 -0400\n\nfix(code): show rubric grader defaults (#4966)\n\n`/goal show` and `/rubric show` now report the rubric grader's startup\nchat model and concrete default maximum iteration count, rather than\nimplying that per-turn `/model` changes affect the grader or leaving the\ndefault unspecified.\n\n---\n\nThe rubric middleware keeps the model chosen when the local server is\nconstructed, while `/model` only changes the configurable chat model for\nlater turns. Capturing that startup model keeps the displayed settings\naligned with actual grading behavior.\n\nThe SDK's default iteration count remains duplicated in the\ndependency-light display path to preserve startup performance. A drift\ntest compares it with the middleware default so the displayed value\ncannot silently become stale.\n\nAI assistance was used to implement and prepare this contribution.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T22:21:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/465b9de17f9f4e6cd07a8674d9a186e60f5bf4d4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44"}]},{"sha":"d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQwNDY0MjdiNTM2YzhkZGJjZTVkODA0ZDZhZThiODYwNTExYTliNDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ccurme","email":"chester.curme@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-22T22:19:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T22:19:30Z"},"message":"revert(code,sdk): revert `SystemPromptConfig` (#4969)","tree":{"sha":"2f5cbcbda079b5fd047b156602066f97e0d1eafc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2f5cbcbda079b5fd047b156602066f97e0d1eafc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYUHyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASUsQAEqxdIy5fjcq44fh3nL6RNbf\nfjbkLNJCVEmMUAdyY8yZvgLWt40YBAjCYRmZk1E67QzlCHIVBDQlC6XBWcvkPlIk\nWfBcoiegGWemCPQeSAz/JWYpQVIuI+MlhwFEMBq0fYVPFr+XCjirjprXibIdMM1W\nUyalS+XdbiMRauewI30kraXiYvlb2ewUz9+Y4axmAEz5mwoZtIFoZvrAme8MZMZY\niiwJJ9cCvO651ApSMDsG5yY82meNwvwgqXDy7hasn1NfiJekTT+3MktAl+qOuDEY\n+rMqZA8Zaz894N4HAboVLFY9MRGn7qv0Iu9IcvawEBbyn73GsfudwF1z98ZFv+kD\nAeePXY2Z5BFl5ggPk/8kW13Z4aVDzNCa5dIbW1U1cEC7DTwz7aCwhrVRCu/AEB6P\nQk4xH3hb/FFBbkOq8kjsXCfJZ9vQyQ1+FFDXwlpB9UweIwAnCJ6G6nnLdup3SeEa\n8UM5CeyaneOCw9iCnApMxxVQamdjGjT/1Id7PJ/5t9Jlwo0fnjmzJhHc7ObYiycs\n4Iv5iFhsUDPUzBgOwkX6D/WZna3Nl1EXPQsEeHVwlLk/dmY1afoat+uMwxN3Wt6P\nlgQz0wqjsto7hUd+SSM/eGgYxOdp6OJH6yatj9aycXzIfPuDJ3gDHmHm57nvxHuT\nqcHORFx+ECy1xTSCAi93\n=7ALK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2f5cbcbda079b5fd047b156602066f97e0d1eafc\nparent 8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a\nauthor ccurme <chester.curme@gmail.com> 1784758770 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784758770 -0400\n\nrevert(code,sdk): revert `SystemPromptConfig` (#4969)","verified_at":"2026-07-22T22:19:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d046427b536c8ddbce5d804d6ae8b860511a9b44/comments","author":{"login":"ccurme","id":26529506,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTI5NTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26529506?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme","html_url":"https://github.com/ccurme","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a"}]},{"sha":"8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhjMzE1NDUxMDJiNzViZWQ4N2YyY2JkNjNiODFlNjllMjdjNzE4OGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T22:10:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T22:10:57Z"},"message":"style(code): render `-m` slash prompts as plain agent text (#4974)\n\nA prompt passed via `-m`/`--message` that starts with a slash (like a\nfile path) now renders as a normal user message in the TUI instead of a\nslash command.\n\n---\n\nText supplied through `-m`/`--message` is always dispatched as literal\nagent input — it never triggers a slash or shell command. However,\n`UserMessage` and its queued placeholder unconditionally ran mode-prefix\ndetection on the raw content, so a leading `/` (e.g. `-m /etc/hosts\nexplain this`) was rendered with the command glyph, command border, and\ncommand highlight, misrepresenting what was actually sent.\n\nThis adds a `detect_mode` flag (default `True`, so all existing\nslash/shell command displays are unchanged) to `UserMessage` and\n`QueuedUserMessage`, and disables it on the `-m` startup paths. Those\npaths route exclusively through `_handle_user_message`, which only ever\ncarries literal agent text, so mode detection is turned off there for\nboth the connecting placeholder and the submitted message. When\ndetection is off, a leading `/command` token is emitted as plain text\nrather than being dropped by the highlighter.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4c6eb77f-8a71-8326-97b9-89c073251068)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"84e0f2893f5dc3a0eddcaeeff9ac48777afb15e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/84e0f2893f5dc3a0eddcaeeff9ac48777afb15e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYT/xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABs4QABqjkKgzGKRudXPVfv4huTYe\nPpPQzPe6U3PWtEKBhK/nG9XcdhyQ7JnKzOurKeT4ioQU5wCj3hQI+xKcmWl23WK8\n855A5IpjM4Vg30j+JvRRRMm3p/sk3104dWJ/oqoXQ4xvZIhvHeF4+dZMoD2BTWRF\nnqVVTmTviMscQry5PD3eQ7XY6LTzA2InA9671qdgu6EIc8UpqJIsVqQnf9sH9HSO\nqEyPCAv63dV14K/ytosAOQs4gopQC/SVmpR3hpj/k1lFdKKaxQ55hUgfR6j0W9pB\nSUOpTttdufIzMhjurdDcyrQP2ZyU/94xuSjPbhoyCAqgsxat4tOmiH/Z5+fH0NhY\nYYpQTspB1wKz6hGiDtvkf1MWpRfWC9GW9vB+vXv9U3cuuvykD6MIcW8fFZ5ouKHi\nnPS/Qa3DGipQHTzic424ksQ6LJ7JxH43v6Tde0DhT1Zl6bZxXyxI7yKwK4xSZl64\nypZ8j9Ant+WRcgvUpXX80xhKSl02fjjdMywnPysZ0yLSsIjbShAuPQl05Fk0S54m\nuuu/CMvqNXgZyCoI6l0gQUnYVnA2SLSO+uXNrABAumuV3r3yt2B/srlczKu0woRy\niA73q1JqU71FTNs4WD4WUgDEgASns6FYbCRNplWoOsZt4hdpF5bwCq8gzVd2HvQV\nuyPVXK5KHNL7Swima/mu\n=1eIK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 84e0f2893f5dc3a0eddcaeeff9ac48777afb15e0\nparent f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784758257 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784758257 -0400\n\nstyle(code): render `-m` slash prompts as plain agent text (#4974)\n\nA prompt passed via `-m`/`--message` that starts with a slash (like a\nfile path) now renders as a normal user message in the TUI instead of a\nslash command.\n\n---\n\nText supplied through `-m`/`--message` is always dispatched as literal\nagent input — it never triggers a slash or shell command. However,\n`UserMessage` and its queued placeholder unconditionally ran mode-prefix\ndetection on the raw content, so a leading `/` (e.g. `-m /etc/hosts\nexplain this`) was rendered with the command glyph, command border, and\ncommand highlight, misrepresenting what was actually sent.\n\nThis adds a `detect_mode` flag (default `True`, so all existing\nslash/shell command displays are unchanged) to `UserMessage` and\n`QueuedUserMessage`, and disables it on the `-m` startup paths. Those\npaths route exclusively through `_handle_user_message`, which only ever\ncarries literal agent text, so mode detection is turned off there for\nboth the connecting placeholder and the submitted message. When\ndetection is off, a leading `/command` token is emitted as plain text\nrather than being dropped by the highlighter.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4c6eb77f-8a71-8326-97b9-89c073251068)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T22:10:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8c31545102b75bed87f2cbd63b81e69e27c7188a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1"}]},{"sha":"f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY1MWQzYTAxNDVhMDMwMTMxN2MzNmIwYWUxNTI2MzAwN2RhY2Q2ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-22T21:25:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T21:25:03Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): diagnose rubric grader structured output errors (#4938)\n\nRubric grader failures now identify the configured model and whether\nLangChain used provider-native structured output or tool calling. The\nsame details appear in evaluation errors, logs, and LangSmith trace\nmetadata, making provider-specific failures easier to diagnose.\n\n---\n\nPassing `GraderResponse` as the response format delegates strategy\nselection to LangChain's automatic structured-output handling.\nPreviously, a validation failure exposed only the exception type and\nmessage, so it was unclear which model or response path produced it.\n\nThis change reports the configured grader model and infers the effective\nstrategy from the resolved model profile, successful output, or\nstructured-output exception. It falls back to `unknown` when the\nstrategy cannot be determined, and trace instrumentation remains\nbest-effort so observability failures do not affect grading.","tree":{"sha":"e1c3d4af0cef96848c9cd5b0ae8f1f464825d167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e1c3d4af0cef96848c9cd5b0ae8f1f464825d167"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYTUvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALJ0QAFqAFYDt8Mp7HzrKuTDt8+kz\nwQuRUeTCs49YHMEAJf/e3HX4mTDCQJJZLl/4UUunVx25Q8B0+2UbbW2t2cAB55ea\nHWpdwgR2QCTktp/BfsPjkQxp/4P1SOFx4caEr7uFlK5TPKgWm0WhBRQtfeypxXNF\nJqcZSwz/TbhGSToOCvGsTwsYLa80BG6bA1a09Qg79fweWqNQJ0tkrAbgiLQDH3rK\nStvgYDdltrUrGyvGPN3iM5LlhTxTPzZF3sz1OuzDdQpMJYv4ra5/Y9WglxVRCmRX\nsDyyRHgWPGbNoqOVLxozsOwWrjLqCLYMBFUADtywIiRYmzWEOr6B/1+UiMvu+87J\njn28G/vfuUCzBkyGKUoMQ2w8g55Im2Oh+kmlhWK4jKRZGQqxRqzuQ6SUp9w6/hOz\ncrhVrqTccZAbSW6fp0bm2sLmGZV9vSmG4GK6pDC+6KVxoGmIjKLcvyy8PqKZvftb\nwy2cbwAZ9p3JD5SLalvuOuTHTUvbtQ/w4v+P6OeWGmRpvHX575pTguM7BJqxExOd\nvRO1MxntFHoMdhtAWOTMzn3GDwoUcXhvRS/+p2PHN3p1tDF3WxWEo7Dzi4AyD3rd\ntgX0Mns6bKbE1CuWrAyw2LvW3jmdMPEE0gOHDh255EOouu2wJ1Ku1x3iXp6KfU/J\nRb3vZTa6sNvNvibidz0R\n=wAhF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e1c3d4af0cef96848c9cd5b0ae8f1f464825d167\nparent c7d1ff00bd505a7d5f078922aca4a441a81b5125\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784755503 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784755503 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): diagnose rubric grader structured output errors (#4938)\n\nRubric grader failures now identify the configured model and whether\nLangChain used provider-native structured output or tool calling. The\nsame details appear in evaluation errors, logs, and LangSmith trace\nmetadata, making provider-specific failures easier to diagnose.\n\n---\n\nPassing `GraderResponse` as the response format delegates strategy\nselection to LangChain's automatic structured-output handling.\nPreviously, a validation failure exposed only the exception type and\nmessage, so it was unclear which model or response path produced it.\n\nThis change reports the configured grader model and infers the effective\nstrategy from the resolved model profile, successful output, or\nstructured-output exception. It falls back to `unknown` when the\nstrategy cannot be determined, and trace instrumentation remains\nbest-effort so observability failures do not affect grading.","verified_at":"2026-07-22T21:25:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f51d3a0145a0301317c36b0ae15263007dacd6f1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c7d1ff00bd505a7d5f078922aca4a441a81b5125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c7d1ff00bd505a7d5f078922aca4a441a81b5125","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c7d1ff00bd505a7d5f078922aca4a441a81b5125"}]}]